Samdech Techo Hun Sen's announcement was made in front of many Cambodian-Chinese investors at a dinner with leaders and members of the Khmer-Chinese Association at the Koh Pich Center on the night of April 9, 2019.
In front of those investors, with the participation of the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled the one-China policy implemented in Cambodia from the time of King Norodom Sihanouk in the 50s-60s until The reign of Samdech Preah Boromneath Norodom Sihamoni, the current King of Cambodia, and Samdech asked all investors to support this policy.
He added that he had opened up opportunities for Chinese nationals from Taiwan to do business in Cambodia, but had asked them not to allow Taiwanese embassies in Cambodia. It is not allowed to raise the Taiwanese flag on Cambodian territory.
Samdech gave an example explaining that China and Cambodia are not different. If anyone separates a Cambodian province from Cambodia to another country or an independent state, Cambodia does not agree, so China does not agree to separate Taiwan from itself.
"Respecting China's sovereignty over the Taiwan issue or the Tibet issue is no different from respecting the independence and sovereignty of Cambodia itself, so please understand," he said.
