Chairman of the Board of the National Veterans Fund: Veterans, Civil Servants and Veterans Receive Continued Social Security Regime from the Royal Government of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sam Heng Boros, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Chairman of the Board of the National Veterans Fund, stated that former civil servants and veterans have received additional social security from the Royal Government of Cambodia. In addition, the Royal Government also provided a subsidy of 50,000 Riels per person on the occasion of Khmer New Year, Khmer New Year 2562.
Mr. Sam Heng Boros made the remarks at the 14th Board Meeting of the National Veterans Fund, 3rd mandate, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on April 08, 2019.
Mr. Sam Heng Boros added that according to Sub-Decree No. 48 on the extension of the social security system for former civil servants and veterans, it was amended and installed as follows:
The monthly social security system for former civil servants and veterans set out above will be implemented from April 1, 2019. Mr. Sam Heng Boros added that this is encouraging and shows that the Royal Government of Cambodia pays high attention to former civil servants and veterans. The current offer from the Royal Government will further improve the lives of former civil servants and veterans.
On that occasion, the Chairman of the Board also announced the composition of Mr. Hong Hean as the Director of the National Veterans Fund.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Touch Poliva, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, addressed a number of health officials at a meeting to review the work results for 2018 and the work direction for 2019 of Svay Rieng Provincial Health Department this morning, April 9, 2019. That the Royal Government of Cambodia has placed the health of the people as the main factor for the development of human resources, sustainable social and economic progress.
The ceremony was attended by Dr. Ke Ratha, Director of the Provincial Health Department and the Director of the District Hospital, Municipal Health Center throughout Svay Rieng.
Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province said that the progress made by the Department of Health in 2018 reflects the improvement of the health of the people, including coverage of maternal and child health services, child health, immunization rates. Diseases are on the rise and rates are declining, as is the elimination of counterfeit medicines and illegal private health services.
Mr. Toch Poliva stated that around the achievements we have achieved, we still have many challenges to fight to make the health sector more prosperous, give more confidence to the people in our health system. Let the sector play a more active role in contributing to reducing poverty of the people.
The Deputy Governor continued that in order to promote the health sector to be more successful, it requires the Department of Health to cooperate smoothly with the relevant institutions, especially local authorities at all levels.
In this sense, the public and private health sectors must play a role as development partners and communicate well with each other, and must strive to eliminate anarchy in this sector, which is detrimental to the health and livelihood of the people.
In that, the Department of Health must strengthen the quality of human resources even more at the health center level, which is one level closest to the people. Therefore, it is necessary to allocate and manage human resources well to ensure that human resources at all levels of technology to serve the health sector effectively at all levels of the health network in both urban and rural areas.
