(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said on April 9, 2019 that the Ministry of Public Works is working with the Ministry of Economy and Finance to find a solution to the delisting of vehicle ownership. Convenient for all car owners.
The remarks of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol were made on the occasion of the Senior Minister's participation in the meeting to review the results of road safety work in the first quarter of 2019, chaired by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior. National Road Safety Committee this morning, April 9, 2019.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated, "Our people do not want to change because they have to pay about 4% of the cost of ownership change and it is difficult, so the Ministry of Public Works is working with the Ministry of Economy to connect the system. "Taxes with the ministry's online system can be done in one place, and he can change the name of his property."
The minister added that the Ministry of Public Works and the Ministry of Economy are also discussing lower fees for those who have not yet come to register within three months. He added that during the three months, he also wants all car owners to update their residence, otherwise when the fine is not found.
At the same time, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also asked all car owners with old license plates to come and exchange for new license plates with QR Code to have the right to keep their license plates when selling cars. Death news! CPP Central Committee Member Moh Kosal Dies at 70
