(Phnom Penh): The annual dialogue between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the United Nations (UN team) will be held on May 6, 2019 in Phnom Penh. This is according to Mr. Ket Sophan, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
He added that in the annual dialogue between the top leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the UN working group, Cambodia will also raise three topics to ask the UN working group to cooperate. These topics include: First: Social Protection, Second: Data for Development, and Third: An Annual Report of Cambodia, which will be submitted to the UN in New York in July. This.
Mr. KET Sophan said that in response to the request of a senior UN official, the Cambodian Chief of Mission reaffirmed his full support that Cambodia will continue to cooperate with the UN indefinitely, especially in support of the annual dialogue between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the upcoming UN working group.
The Deputy Prime Minister also reaffirmed his strong support for continuing this good cooperation in the future, especially on May 6, the annual dialogue between Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the UN working group. This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had a dinner with the leaders and members of the Khmer-Chinese Association
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of Tuesday, April 9, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will have a dinner with the leaders and members of the Khmer League Association. - China at the Diamond Island Center.
Oknha Pung Kheav Se, President of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia, said that the dinner meeting between Samdech Techo and the association this evening is the third dinner. Oknha Pung Kheav Se considers Samdech Techo Hun Sen's invitation to join the dinner with the leaders and members of the association as a noble honor for the association. In particular, show concern for investors, traders and businessmen doing business in Cambodia.
This dining meeting is also an opportunity to receive more recommendations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen for investing in Cambodia. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Pung Kheav Se.
According to Mr. Pung Kheavse, the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia has participated in many activities in 2018 to support the business of Khmer-Chinese in Cambodia and also do a lot of humanitarian activities.
At the same time, the association subsidizes the salaries of poor teachers who teach in Chinese schools across the country, funds teachers' training centers, promotes local Chinese language education and trains Chinese language experts.
In addition, the association actively interacts with business associations and investment institutions and warmly welcomes delegations from all over the world to serve and act as a bridge connecting the Chinese rich in Cambodia. And cooperation with China and the world. General Director of Rural Development Bank urges young people to play more sports, strive to be good citizens, stay away from drugs
