Minister Say Sam Al Urges Provincial, District and Municipal Authorities in Preah Sihanouk Province to Transform and Build a Modern Administration
(Preah Sihanouk): The Minister of Environment and Chairman of the National Task Force for Preah Sihanouk Province urged the provincial, district and municipal authorities in Preah Sihanouk Province to transform and build themselves into a modern administration as well as to lead the local economy. To serve and respond to the sacred intentions of the people.
Kampong Seila district is one of the five potential districts of Sihanoukville province with special economic zones, agro-industries, acacia plantations, orchards and oil palm plantations, as well as many factories.
Mr. Say Sam Al said: "In its local management work, the authorities need to transform and build themselves into a modern administration and know how to lead their local economy by knowing where their economic sources are and planning." Properly and comprehensively to reap the benefits of development for local development.
"We must all work together to reap the benefits of development in order to maintain the national economic growth of around 7% per year, create jobs for Cambodians, reduce poverty, increase people's livelihoods," he said. "People will ensure sustainable development."
The Chairman of the National Task Force for Preah Sihanouk Province strongly emphasized that Sihanoukville must completely end the long-standing land dispute. "New conflicts must not arise and efforts must be made to resolve old land disputes completely," he said.
Regarding the issue of fresh water for use in Sihanoukville, Mr. Say Sam Al said that fresh water sources in various areas in Sihanoukville must be maintained in order to maintain long-term water sources for use as well as production. Water and water distribution in accordance with the needs of people and businesses in Prey Sihanouk province.
The Minister in charge of the working group also said that the same case applies to the management of electricity as well as the sewer system and solid waste management. In order to manage the cleanliness of the environment in Sihanoukville, the Minister requested all relevant institutions, including the people, as well as business owners of entertainment venues in Sihanoukville to cooperate in cleaning the environment and litter properly.
(Phnom Penh): To celebrate the upcoming Khmer New Year, Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited has partnered with Cellcard and Aruna Pure Water Company to distribute thousands of gifts to customers who support Wing's products and services.
This offer takes place in front of the head office of Wing Specialized Bank as well as Cellcard from April 8th to 12th. Wing Specialized Bank will provide customers with thousands of cases of Aruna Pure Water for customers who have made Transaction at least $ 3 through Wing account from April 1 to April 12, 2019.
To receive this gift, customers simply find the Wing staff waiting at the Wing booth at any of the above locations and show their latest transactions, except for deposits and payment of electricity bills under $ 25. All transactions through Wing account from $ 3 up can be exchanged for one case of Aruna pure water gift.
Jojo Malolos, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, stated that it is the Bank's goal to ensure that in addition to bringing innovative products and services that can help improve the daily lives of all Wing customers, Take this memorable gift when they travel to their hometown during Khmer New Year.
In addition to getting free Aruna water, customers who come to both locations can also get many gifts when they sign up for Cellcard. In addition, they can enjoy a lot of discounts if they buy more Aruna water.
