Senior official of the Ministry of Information: Cambodia has 650 publications, including 411 in Khmer and 25 foreign.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Phos Sovann, Representative of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Information and Audiovisual of the Ministry of Information, stated that Cambodia currently has a total of 650 newspapers, including 411 newspapers in Khmer. And 25 foreign language newspapers.
Mr. Phos Sovann stated, "In Cambodia, the media sector has grown significantly and currently has a total of 650 print media outlets, including 411 Khmer language newspapers, 25 foreign language newspapers, 194 magazines and bulletins. 20 units of information.
He said there are a total of 21 units of foreign news agencies, permanent offices of foreign radio and television stations, including China Radio International (CRI) and other Chinese media units. In addition, there are many Chinese public and private institutions that have been cooperating with the Cambodian Ministry of Information.
The General Department of Information and Audiovisual of the Ministry of Information emphasized that through the development of the information and audio-visual sector, it is clear to the world that the Royal Government of Cambodia supports freedom of the press.
Cambodia is also preparing to amend the Law on the Media, prepare to draft the Law on Audiovisual, the Law on Advertising and promote respect for the professionalism of the press to ensure that the press is more effective and professional in contributing to development. Nation. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Phos Sovann.
He said that through international cooperation to promote the long-term development of the country, the Royal Government of Cambodia has put in place policies to protect and facilitate foreign investors, including many Chinese and Chinese investors. And the use of Chinese in Cambodia is getting more and more attention day by day.
