(Banteay Meanchey): The 605-meter-long Stung Bot Bridge connecting Cambodia and Thailand at the Poipet International Port will be inaugurated on April 22, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to facilitate Cambodia-Thailand freight forwarding. This is according to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this on April 8, 2019, when he and the Minister of Public Works and Transport of Thailand inspected the Stung Bot Bridge to be ready for its official opening on the 22nd. This coming April.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the Stung Bot bridge was built entirely by Thai engineers, with a length of 605 meters, of which the Cambodian side is 215 meters long. The Thai side is the sole payer of the bridge, connecting Thailand and Cambodia, leaving only cargo, while passengers have to enter through the Poipet international gate.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also confirmed that the Thai side has also provided loans to build checkpoints along the border.
