The official inauguration of the "Isanvarman Srey" Museum was held with great pomp and ceremony under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and was attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders from Ministries, institutions, leaders, civil servants of the National Bank and many other people in Phnom Penh.
The "Isanvarman Museum of Economics and Monetary" was started after receiving a high recommendation from the Prime Minister on the occasion of the 30th anniversary of the re-establishment of the National Bank of Cambodia on October 08, 2009. For the purpose of presenting to the national and international public the history of Cambodia's economy and currency. The construction and preparation of this museum took only 10 years to complete.
On the occasion of presiding over the official inauguration of the museum, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure and pride in the historical presence of the "Preah Isanvarman" museum, which is the result of the efforts of many experts under the direct leadership. Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto added that the construction and design of the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman" has begun research from zero. According to Chea Chanto, due to the volatile and complicated history of Cambodia, as well as the lack of documentation, it has been difficult to compile and build this museum.
Please note that the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman", a museum that brings the Cambodian people to know the history of its long economy and currency, is located in the heart of Phnom Penh and former Phnom Penh City Hall. In 1908, the former airline in 1992. The museum building depicts the patriarchal style of the early 20th century.
The museum also has a library, souvenir shops, cafes and a beautiful garden. After opening, the public will be allowed to visit the museum, which shows the history of Cambodia's economy and currency since the Funan period.
