Lt. Gen. Hun Manet Leads Cambodian Army Delegation for First Official Visit to US
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army, led a Cambodian military delegation on its first official visit to the United States from 8 to 12 months. April 2019 at the invitation of the Commander of the Pacific Special Operations Command of the United States Army
According to the announcement of Mr. Hun Manet's team, during this visit, the Lt. Gen. will attend the International Workshop on Pacific Special Operations "PASOC 19". On that occasion, the Commander of the Army will meet with the Commander of the Pacific Special Operations Command of the United States Army in order to strengthen the friendship and cooperation between the two armies.
Please be informed that General Hun Manet has been promoted to the position of Commander of the Army after the 6th National Assembly Election. Prior to his visit to the United States, he visited a number of key countries, including China, Russia and Thailand.
Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy: National economy and people's economy grow rapidly under the shadow of peace
(Prey Veng): Addressing sub-national officials in Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province on April 7 during the traditional New Year celebration, Mr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Working Group Help Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, said that the national economy and the people's economy have grown rapidly under the shadow of peace in the last two decades.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Economy said that in the last 20 years, Cambodia's economy has grown by 7%, the poverty rate has decreased by more than 1% a year. In fact, in 2018, the Cambodian economy achieved an unexpected growth rate of 7.5%, the highest growth in the last 10 years.
During the ceremony, Mr. Steng Sokhom also brought greetings from all CPP leaders, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to local officials.
As a National Assistance Officer for Kamchay Mear District, Mr. Steng Sokhom brought with him the orders and instructions of the Head of the Royal Government, as well as the advice of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Chairman of the National Assistance Team for Prey Veng Province to the Chairman of the District Council. Districts and commune chiefs, commune councils and village chiefs need to pay attention because it is the direction for leadership at both the national and sub-national levels.
On the same day, Mr. Steng Sokhom and his accompanying delegation also inspected the construction of a concrete road in the primary school of Moab Upasak and Mok Sem Prey Tuol. After that, the team leader continued to inspect the construction site of Smach school building in Smach village, Krabao commune and continued to inspect the construction of concrete road in Krabao Thmey Primary School.
Finally, the Chairman of the National Task Force for Kamchay Mear District continued to inspect the construction site of 4 school buildings, 16 classrooms, a library and a football table donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister at Cambodia-Indonesia Friendship Secondary School in Trabek commune, Kamchay Mear district.
