National Bank of Cambodia: The banking sector in Cambodia is recognized as open and highly integrated in the region
(Thailand): The banking sector in Cambodia is recognized as open and highly integrated in the region, with banking and financial institutions from most countries in the region now present in Cambodia. According to Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Chea Chanto made the remarks while attending the 15th ASEAN Central Bank Governors 'Meeting and the 5th ASEAN Finance Ministers and Governors' Meeting in Chiang Rai, Thailand.
The Regional Summit of the Financial Sector aims to review and discuss the progress of integration and cooperation in the ASEAN financial sector to support economic growth and strengthen regional financial stability in line with the objectives of the ASEAN Economic Community Plan 2025.
The National Bank of Cambodia has played a key role in ASEAN financial integration, contributing to the strengthening of banking sector integration and regional payment system connectivity. The Cambodian banking sector is recognized as open and highly integrated into the region, with banking and financial institutions from most countries in the region now present in Cambodia.
These banking and financial institutions have brought in capital and technology that provides a favorable environment for the development of the banking sector in Cambodia. On the other hand, Cambodia has connected its payment system with countries in the region and the world.
Currently, the National Bank of Cambodia is developing payment systems through modern technology, including: QR Code system with regional countries such as Thailand. Payment via QR Code system will contribute to improving payment efficiency, security and reasonable cost.
