Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Ignoring the National Currency Loses Sovereignty over National Economic Management and Sovereignty (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this morning, April 08, 2019. Ignoring the role of the national currency will lead to a loss of control over the economy, national sovereignty and the nation will be weak.
On the occasion of the official inauguration of the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman", a museum showing the history of the economy and currency of Cambodia since the Funan period, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that all these factors motivate the King of Cambodia. Some try to build national sovereignty by issuing their own national currency.
The Prime Minister said, "Ignoring the role of the national currency will lead to a loss of control over the economy, national sovereignty and the country will be weak in all areas, all of which have prompted the King. "Some Cambodians try to build national sovereignty by issuing their own national currency."
He pointed out that Cambodia used to use currency from different regions through foreign trade from the first century in the Nokor Phnom period to the Angkorian period, when Cambodia became a prosperous empire, but Cambodia did not print the national currency, but used flat coins brought in by the Chinese.
(Banteay Meanchey): On April 08, 2019, Colonel Sing Tum, Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the 51st Infantry Brigade, led a force to dismantle and repair houses for people affected by the strong winds. On the evening of April 7, 2019, a total of 48 houses were located in 2 districts, Ta Kong commune, Malai district and Soeur commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Colonel Sing Tum said that on the afternoon of April 7, 2019, a large guest mixed with lightning caused the collapse of people's houses and damaged some equipment, but did not affect the lives of any people. No. At the same time, the people were happy to see that the district and provincial authorities and the armed forces always pay close attention to them.
They observed the dismantling and rebuilding of people's houses, not only brought a lot of zinc sheets and some food items donated by Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Working Group to Banteay Meanchey Province to hand over. Reach out to the people whose houses are damaged to provide first aid to solve the people's difficulties.
