(Phnom Penh): On Monday, April 4, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inaugurated the Museum of Economics and Monetary. Srey Isanvarman ”is a museum showing the economic and monetary history of Cambodia since the Funan period.
The event was also attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders from various ministries, institutions, government officials of the National Bank, as well as leaders from financial institutions.
The Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Srey Isanvarman", a museum that introduces the people of Cambodia to its history of economic and monetary history, is located in the heart of Phnom Penh and was the former Phnom Penh City Hall in 1908. , Former airline in 1992. The museum building depicts the patriarchal style of the early 20th century.
This area is rapidly developing into a modern area. The museum is not only located near the Cambodia Securities Exchange, but also surrounded by the building of the National Bank of Cambodia, the Banking Technical Study Center, which is the center for training the staff of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Before being renovated into the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman", the museum building was in a dilapidated condition. The layout of the museum has been kept as original as possible, while the interior has been designed to display the treasures of currency and artifacts from the Funan period.
Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the construction of the museum building, which was considered an "ambitious" project, was started in 2012 after receiving a recommendation from Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Governor-General claimed that the Museum of the History of the Economy and Currency of Cambodia was designed according to the currency published and used in the past.
Please note that the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman" has 12 exhibitions that describe the history of Cambodia, highlighting the economic and monetary system in the Funan period to the present. The interior of the museum is modern and is equipped with documentaries, games and touch screens that provide fun and knowledge to the public.
An abundance of descriptions through video and animation exhibitions at the Museum of Economics and Monetary "Isanvarman", including 50 videos, games and touch screens, a large exhibition of fonts, as well as a script layout. The modern design and production by the company in Cambodia will satisfy the Cambodian and foreign public as well.
