Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted that neglecting the role of the national currency will lead to a loss of control over the economy, national sovereignty, and the country will be weak in all areas, which has prompted the King of Cambodia. Some try to build national sovereignty by issuing their own national currency.
Due to the war crisis, documents related to the history of Cambodia as well as the currency were buried and rarely compiled. As a result, the next generation of Cambodian children do not know much about the history of the birth and use of their currency. In this morning's ceremony, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also presented the background of Cambodia's currency.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, described that Cambodia used to use currency from various regions through foreign trade from the first century in the Phnom Kingdom period until the Angkorian period, when Cambodia became an empire. Progress has been made, but Cambodia has not printed the national currency, but has used the flat currency brought in by the Chinese.
At the beginning of the 16th century, "Preah Srey Chetha Reach Vea Manathipadi" called "Sdech Kan", Cambodia's first king, issued the national currency "Prak Sleng" to strengthen economic, political and national sovereignty through economic ties with foreign countries Such as trade with Portuguese and Spanish businessmen through "money" and the establishment of a clear monetary tax system based on the nation.
In the 19th century, King Ang Duong issued the national currency "temple money" to strengthen the economy and national sovereignty and liberate the nation from the influence of neighboring countries.
Under French tutelage, Cambodia did not have monetary sovereignty, but Cambodia did use banknotes issued by the Bank of Incheon, a French commercial bank for Indochina countries, including Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos, as a means of payment, savings and pricing. And service until 1948.
The three countries were later formed by the French into the Indochina State Association with the Indochina Silver Printing Institute, established in 1952, headquartered in Phnom Penh to issue currency for use in three countries: Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam under French rule. .
In late 1954, in Paris, the Union of Indochina met in a quadrangle (France, Cambodia, Vietnam, and Laos) to find a solution to the monetary independence for each state. On December 23, 1954, Cambodia gained monetary independence and established the National Bank of Cambodia, after which the riel was successfully introduced in September 1955.
Less than two years after Cambodia gained monetary sovereignty, the civil war began in the early 1970s, and the riel depreciated to uncontrollable levels due to a loss of public trust and influx. US Dollar. High commodity prices pushed inflation to 22% in 1974.
Cambodia then fell under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot in 1975, when the riel, the economic system and all private property were completely abolished. On January 7, 1979, the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia rescued the nation, the motherland and the people throughout the country from the Pol Pot regime.
On October 10, 1979, the Central Bank, then known as the "National Bank of the Cambodian People", was re-established to show the world Cambodia's national sovereignty, which had to be restored from scratch by the building. The National Bank of Cambodia has been demolished, with no financial resources left, no legacy of the bank before, both documents, experience and human resources.
On March 20, 1980, Cambodia issued the national currency, the riel, and put it back into circulation. At that time, the Cambodian people all over the country were very happy and celebrated, it was the first historical event after the Great Victory Day on January 7 and the success of the government in implementing the national economic policy.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was made on the occasion of the official inauguration of the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman", a museum showing the history of the Khmer economy and currency since the Funan period on the morning of the 8th. This April 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "It is difficult for the riel to appreciate too much, because among our workers, there are about 1 million of our workers who use foreign currency to receive their salaries in dollars." At this point, the bank has to act when the riel appreciates, we release the riel to buy the dollar, when the riel depreciates, we release the dollar to buy the riel back.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that every year in March and April before Khmer New Year, the riel always appreciates, only for one month, August or September, which he noted that the riel always depreciates. .
Samdech Techo stated that it is a good thing that the bank does not act as a judge on the exchange rate, leaving the private sector as the judge, and does not hurt the investors. Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, said, "We do not play a role in setting the exchange rate, let the market judge, which is an attractive investment."
The Prime Minister stated that the riel was issued on March 20, 1980, which is now 39 years old, and if changed from one form to another, it is still present to open Salary for civil servants of the Armed Forces.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister said this on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the inauguration of the Museum of Economy and Currency "Preah Isanvarman", a museum showing the history of the economy and currency of Cambodia since the Funan period in the morning. April 08, 2019.
