Minister Ouk Rabun and his delegation return to Cambodia after attending a ministerial meeting in the Republic of Costa Rica
The purpose of the meeting was to review the progress made in water supply, sanitation and hygiene and to share experiences gained from relevant countries for strategic planning to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals on Ensure water, clean living and sustainable sanitation for all people by 2030.
According to the Minister for Cambodia, the Royal Government has set out its policy vision since 2000, stating that "by 2025, all people in rural communities must have adequate water supply and sanitation and live. In a hygienic environment, sustainable.
With high commitment, the Royal Government of Cambodia has successfully led the implementation of the first phase of the action plan on water supply, rural living and sanitation 2014-2018, achieving a sanitation coverage rate of 71.2% and water supply. Rural areas received 58.7% by 2017.
Currently, the Royal Government is focusing on leading the implementation of its second phase action plan 2019-2023, setting 90% target for rural water supply and sanitation. It is a great honor for Cambodia to be recognized as one of the countries on track that will be able to successfully achieve this goal.
