Former students of Koh Sotin High School Level 1, 1986 and 1990, show their friendship again after 30 years of separation
A group of about 100 former alumni of Koh Sotin High School in Koh Sotin commune, Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province, from 1986 and 1990, reunited through a Facebook group chat group called "Former High School Generation" 1 Koh Sotin "and expressed their excitement and express their memories of each other after being separated for many years.
Alumni of Koh Sotin High School Level 1 said that the current meeting was an opportunity to reunite, express their memories and pay tribute to the merits of the teachers who trained. Friends of all generations to become good citizens, good parents, especially with basic knowledge, reach out to acquire professional skills to have enough knowledge to work for the motherland.
It should be noted that for 30 years, the teachers have been teaching, and we have also separated from the teachers and peers to go to work, so these groups of alumni can not forget. Nostalgia and gratitude of teachers.
The gathering on this occasion really showed the joy of the alumni reunion and was a model activity for the next generation of students to love, appreciate and appreciate. Teachers who have been training hard in the past.
Please note that this is the first time that a group of alumni of Koh Sotin High School Level 1 in 1986 and 1990 organized a reunion program, including a commemoration ceremony for teachers and provided some allowances to teachers. Retired and the teachers who are teaching today and hope that we will hold this ceremony every year.
President of the Bar Association of Cambodia promotes the promotion of women in the legal field
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Suon Visal, President of the Bar Association of Cambodia, spoke about the promotion and promotion of women in the participation of leaders in the field of law and other social activities to be better in line with the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The encouraging speech of the President of the Bar Association of Cambodia was made on the occasion that he presided over the celebration of the 7th professional training course for lawyers on the night of April 6, 2019 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Ms. Say Srey Chan, Chairperson of the 7th Lawyer Training Course, the first woman to chair the course, thanked the Royal Government, the President of the Bar Association and the Director of the School of Lawyer Training for promoting women to become Lead to help women lawyers have a name in the legal field.
She emphasized that the Accession of Lawyers is a supplement to the skills of lawyers who already have a career as a lawyer to fill the gaps with well-known professors to strengthen the capacity of lawyers, which is an important sector in helping to develop the country. National.
Ms. Say Srey Chan said, "I would like to thank the Royal Government for its attention and great respect for women in all fields. In each ministry, the Royal Government is always looking for ways to make women more prominent in society, when women are progressing, our society is also progressing.
"At the end of this course, we are committed to finding justice for specific clients, facilitating the work of the judiciary, and facilitating society, as lawyers are a field that not all institutions "There is a shortage, especially to help the poor."
According to Say Srey Chan, Cambodia currently has more than 1,000 lawyers, about 300 of whom are women, or 30 percent. The number of lawyers is still short.
Please be informed that the 7th Law Accreditation Training Course has 89 interns, including 28 women, all of whom are committed to respecting the ethics and profession of lawyers to contribute to the society.
