Does Saudi Arabia really want to build nuclear weapons?
Washington: A building-rich area on the outskirts of Riyadh is rapidly turning into a nuclear power plant site in a context where the US Congress, including Iran, is concerned that Saudi Arabia could use it to build nuclear weapons. One day. But Riyadh has repeatedly claimed that its nuclear program is aimed only at civilian energy.
* If Iran had nuclear weapons, Saudi Arabia must have the same
The nuclear power plant program is an ambitious plan of the 2030 vision strategy of Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, who does not want to see Saudi Arabia rely solely on oil. According to former International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA) chief nuclear inspector Robert Kelley, the reactor could be completed in nine months to a year.
But it is noteworthy that both the US Congress and Iran are concerned that Saudi Arabia may one day develop nuclear weapons. In fact, even Prince Bin Salman himself claimed in 2018 that there was no doubt that if Iran had nuclear weapons, Saudi Arabia would produce nuclear weapons as soon as possible.
