The signing ceremony took place on the occasion of the 23rd ASEAN Finance Ministers' Meeting by the ASEAN Finance Ministers in Chiang Rai, Thailand.
It should be noted that the 23rd ASEAN Finance Ministers' Meeting, the 5th Meeting of ASEAN Finance Ministers and Governors of the Central Bank of Vietnam and related meetings were held from 4 to 5 April 2019 in Chiang Rai. Thailand and Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, led the Cambodian delegation to the meeting.
The meeting concluded successfully and the ASEAN Finance Ministers reaffirmed their strong commitment to ASEAN integration efforts to sustain economic growth and strengthen financial stability in the region. That the world and the region are experiencing the uncertainty that arises from trade restrictions and policy adjustments of developed countries.
For tax cooperation, the ASEAN Finance Ministers welcomed the progress of the negotiation of the bilateral agreement on the avoidance of double taxation (DTA) between ASEAN member countries and requested all members to continue to negotiate the remaining agreements. Coming soon.
The meeting also agreed to further strengthen cooperation on two key points: 1) strengthening ASEAN resilience amid the rapid development of financial technology and 2) promoting the management of sustainable financing.
