Legal Awareness: Occupational Accidents
(Phnom Penh): Several weeks ago, the Legal Awareness Program of Fresh News in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation raised a number of issues related to the field of labor to the public, such as the topic of "Contracts. Work, dissolution of labor contracts, labor disputes, labor dispute resolution mechanisms, unions, individual delegates, etc.
For this week, our Legal Awareness Program brings another new topic related to employment to the public: "Occupational Accidents."
What is an occupational accident? If workers face an accident, what compensation will they receive?
Accidents that can be considered as occupational accidents include:
1: Accidents that occur during work are accidents that occur from the use of machines or other equipment in the workplace and cause injury or paralysis of any part of the body or cause loss of life. Example: While working, a "A" woman was injured by a finger-slicing machine.
2. Accidents that occur during travel are accidents that occur to workers when traveling straight to work and back home without stopping or stopping to do any activities for personal gain. . Example: On the evening of January 1, 2018, a "B" woman left work to return home and met with a traffic accident that caused her to break one of her legs.
* All workers of enterprises and establishments registered with the National Social Security Fund are entitled to Occupational Risk Insurance. * Daily allowance for temporary incapacity for disability. * Provision of allowances or allowances for permanent incapacity for disability. * Provision of allowances for cremation and allowances to the victims.
