(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notice to all Capital-Provincial Labor Departments, employers, federations, unions and all workers about the celebration of the World Day for Occupational Safety and Health on April 28, 2019. In the future, it is recommended to celebrate this day in their enterprises and put up banners and slogans on the fences in front of those enterprises.
The ministry said the day was held annually by member countries of the International Labor Organization in order to promote occupational safety and health and to commemorate the workers who lost their lives due to occupational accidents and illnesses in Cambodia. In the world.
