Police have arrested a suspect in the brutal murder of a woman and her granddaughter in Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province.
(Kampong Cham): The suspect who killed a woman and his granddaughter and took her head and left her alone was arrested and arrested by the police on the afternoon of April 6, 2019, Trapeang Boeung village, Thmor Poun commune, Prey Chhor district. Kampong Cham Province.
Brigadier General Heng Vuthy added that through interrogation, the assailant admitted that he had killed the victim out of resentment. Anger because the suspect loves the victim and someone else falls in love, as well as the story erupts, leads to the killing of the victim.
According to Heng Vuthy, the suspect had once killed a person in 1995 who had a vicious character, and after his arrest, the people wanted to beat him to death without the help of the authorities.
Please be informed that on April 3, 2019, there was a brutal murder case, two victims were beheaded by the first victim: Uncle Oun, 65 years old and second: Kheng Savoeun 6 years old, in Toul Thmor village, Thmor Poun commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province.
After the heinous murder, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Chairman of the Kampong Cham Provincial Unity Command, ordered the police to open an immediate search to catch the killer to be punished according to law. After the outbreak of African swine fever in Ratanakkiri province, joint police force at Trapeang Phlong international border checkpoint in Tbong Khmum province cracked down on illegal pig imports from Vietnam
Competent forces include: Immigration Police at Trapeang Phlong International Gate, Chief of Military Forces, Customs and Excise Branch, Trapeang Phlong International Port, and Veterinary Specialists of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture.
According to the immigration police officer at Trapeang Phlong International Gate, in the early morning of April 5, 2019, the immigration officer at Trapeang Phlong Gate was standing in the corridor area at Post 117/2 within the jurisdiction of Trapeang Phlong Gate. A group of traders transporting pigs from Vietnam found that they did not have an import permit and immediately arrested the group.
After checking that there is no illegal permit, the police handed over people and exhibits to the veterinary specialist of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to proceed with the procedure.
The African swine fever epidemic in Vietnam, which has killed dozens of pigs, has spread to Cambodia, with officials finding the disease in a village in O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province. On the border with Vietnam since March 22, 2019, killing about 400 pigs.
However, a senior official at the Ministry of Health and spokesman Ly Sovann claimed that the disease was not contagious and could not be transmitted to humans, so appealed to all residents not to worry.
