Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Disseminate Fire Rescue Methods and Call for Caution
(Banteay Meanchey): Under the direct command of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General At Cam, a group of police officers from the Fire Expert Office of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commission disseminated and trained on fire prevention, first aid and firefighting techniques. To more than 200 people and traders.
This advertisement was made on April 5, 2019 at Chamkar Kor market, called Phsar Thmei, which had a fire selling plastic toy stalls, completely damaged by a recent electric shock in Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province, caused the loss of property worth about 20,000 dollars.
Deputy Commissioner for Firearms, Explosives and Fire Management, Colonel Bun Pheng, said that the primary training on fire prevention and rescue is to prevent fires effectively.
According to the Deputy Commissioner, the training is for practical police officers to use equipment in the event of a gas tank leaking, causing a fire. On the gas tank, the fire can be extinguished.
He said that another measure in case of fire caused by gasoline is to prevent the police officers put gasoline in the tank and inject gas to ignite a large fire.
The Deputy Commissioner confirmed that "such fire problems, professional police officers advise and train not to use water poured on the fire. "Gasoline fires are caused by the use of gas pipelines to put out the fire in time."
