Ministry of Health announces on the prevention of diseases and health problems during the traditional Khmer New Year
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has issued a notification on the prevention of diseases and health problems during the traditional Khmer New Year.
In the past, the Ministry has issued a statement informing the public about the prevention of food poisoning and alcohol poisoning several times, but the Ministry of Health has observed that cases of food poisoning and alcohol poisoning continue to occur. In the communities of some provinces.
According to the announcement, during 2018, there were 19 cases of food poisoning, with a total of 852 poisoning, of which 13 died and 5 were alcohol poisoning with 206 alcohol poisoning. Twelve of them died. In addition, during the period of 2019 to March, there were a total of six cases of food poisoning, with a total of 246 cases, including 2 deaths.
