(Svay Rieng): PRASAC, the largest financial institution in Cambodia, held a groundbreaking ceremony for a library building in Svay Rieng province on April 5, 2019 with the aim of contributing to the promotion of reading and education in Cambodia. .
The library building to be built is 7 meters × 9 meters in the Samrong Primary School in Chek Village, Samrong Commune, Chantrea District, Svay Rieng Province, and it will take 4 months to complete the construction. This construction is entirely funded by PRASAC.
Say Sony, Chief Marketing Officer of PRASAC MFI, said: “Once completed, the library will be equipped with books, documents and other facilities to serve the reading needs of students and teachers. PRASAC has also partnered with the Curriculum Development Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to provide training to librarians and support the three-year project.
Mr. Sony continued, "On behalf of the management and staff of PRASAC, I would like to donate this library building for the public benefit to help cultivate a culture of reading and improve education in Svay Rieng province, also Cambodia." I hope that the students at Samrong Primary School will enjoy learning and improving their reading skills through the library provided by PRASAC. ”
Speaking at the event, Mr. Nhek Kreun, Director of Chantrea District Education Office, warmly welcomed and expressed his deep gratitude to PRASAC Microfinance Institution for promoting the education sector by providing the library building to Samrong Primary School at This.
