Cambodia and Thailand continue to strengthen payment ties and develop financial technology through QR payment interoperability
Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said: "Establishing a QR code payment system is very important for both countries to facilitate cross-border payments and reduce the risk and cost of payments as well. "Strengthen the settlement between the two countries."
He said that this development is very important because Cambodia is a popular tourist destination for Thai tourists and the possibility of using mobile banking to pay with Cambodian merchants will be able to strengthen the efficiency of cross-border payments. Such as promoting the use of electronic payments between the people of the two countries.
"Today's presentation is just the first step in the QR payment interaction between the two countries," he added. "Going further, the wider implementation of the QR payment interoperability mechanism will allow cross-border QR payments to be made by most banks in Thailand and Cambodia."
