In the morning of April 05, 2019, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration and the General Department of Taxation jointly organized a dissemination workshop on "Collection of stamp duty for transfer of ownership or possession of real estate, property tax and preparation for the declaration on determination." Stamped tax base for transfer of ownership or possession of real estate ”at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Dr. also requested the local authorities and relevant units around Phnom Penh as follows:
1: Help widely disseminate Proclamation No. 343 MEF.PrK dated 22 March 2019 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the determination of the tax base for the transfer of ownership or possession of real estate and the annex on the distribution Geography and property prices for tax bases in Phnom Penh.
In particular, help disseminate to the people about the effective date of implementation on July 1, 2019 of the appendix, which has updated the new price and encourage people who own property that has been transferred in the past and has not yet declared the stamp duty. To hurry to declare tax before July 1, 2019 to get the implementation of the price still in force.
2: Continue to promote cooperation in encouraging the owner or the holder of the right to occupy the property, especially for the unregistered property owner who has transferred the tenure at the Sangkat level to pay the stamp duty at the tax administration in force.
3. Pay more attention to strengthen cooperation in collecting some taxes, which are beneficial for the local development of the sub-national administration to its full potential, such as: taxes on unused land and taxes on real estate.
4. Regarding the property tax, the Khan / Sangkat administration shall encourage the owners or local property owners to cooperate with the team to update the property information to provide information related to the property to be included in the data management system of the General Department of Taxation.
5. For the tax on unused land, request the Khan and Sangkat administrations to encourage and encourage the owners or occupants of their local real estate to fulfill their tax obligations in a timely manner and in accordance with the procedures as much as possible.
6: Continue to pay attention to guide the implementation officers in providing cooperation in the tax collection process to use soft words, politeness and have a decent attitude to the people who come to receive services and facilitate the provision of services properly. According to the approach of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, it should be done quickly and transparently.
