According to Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and a spokesman for the Royal Government, the draft law has been amended in some words.
According to Phay Siphan, the draft law on "Management of Petroleum and Petroleum Products" is designed to be in line with the current context of the petroleum sector in Cambodia.
This draft is designed and developed with the aim of promoting the sustainable and effective development of the petroleum sector to contribute to the socio-economic development and long-term interests of the nation, while the exploration and development of both land and sea oil resources to advance. Towards the first production of oil resources in the history of Cambodia in the coming year.
Since 2006, the former National Petroleum Authority of Cambodia has revised the draft law in consultation with technical and national and international legal experts. The draft law on the management of petroleum and petroleum products is prepared and is divided into nine chapters and 72 articles.
