Letter to readers: Cambodia's good economic growth, strong finances and manageable debt are a bloody disappointment for the opposition! (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia is now in a good position because the economy is growing at a good rate, the financial situation is stronger because the deposits in the National Treasury are more and more. The external public debt situation is also manageable.
Both the Ministry of Economy and Finance and major international financial institutions such as the World Bank, the Asian Development Bank and the International Monetary Fund (IMF) have forecast that Cambodia's economic growth in 2019 and next year will remain stable. Around 7% (can go up or down slightly).
Economic growth has been stable for many years and will continue to be stable for many years to come, which is a sign that Cambodia has a strong economic situation, although some countries in the region and the world are experiencing economic deficits. Due to various issues, especially the impact of the trade war between China and the United States, however.
Cambodia's economic and financial strength is due to the efforts of the government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the active contribution of the private sector as well as the Cambodian people in general.
Sharp government package reforms will increase the efficiency and productivity of the private sector so that it can compete freely in international markets on an equal footing.
This reform is seen as a driving force for the Cambodian economy to become stronger, faster and more sustainable, enabling Cambodia to stand firmly on its economic strength without relying on external assistance. Not before.
In terms of debt, Cambodia can also manage well. According to a press release issued by the Ministry of Economy and Finance on April 2, as of 2018, Cambodia's external public debt was $ 7 billion, which means the current value of foreign public debt compared to GDP. White is only 21.4% compared to the base ratio of 40%.
In this sense, it can be concluded that Cambodia is becoming stronger and stronger from year to year and now has reached a point where it can stand on its own strength without having to borrow foreign breath. At the same time, the Cambodian government is stepping up its efforts to strengthen its national economy while keeping foreign public debt in a manageable and low-risk position.
This situation is also very favorable for the Cambodian government to achieve its goal of becoming a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
Therefore, the opposition and extremist analysts who are waiting to see the Cambodian economy collapse due to their devastating work will be disappointed and have no more words to say.
