The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen during the 4th Solidarity Dinner with the Great Sports Family of Cambodia at Koh Pich Center on the evening of April 4, 2019, stated that the reason why Cambodia set May 2023 to organize The SEA Games are to avoid being affected by the election.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that during July or the end of 2023, when Cambodia is busy with elections, and every time there is an election, there are riots and other phenomena from the losers. At the same time, Samdech also said that in order not to be disturbed by any activities after the election, Cambodia decided to play in May before the election.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, 2023 is also the year that the first expressway in Cambodia, Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville, will be completed. This route can serve to host the upcoming SEA Games.
In addition to explaining why Cambodia has set May for the SEA Games, the Prime Minister also explained why Cambodia is the last host for the SEA Games. According to Samdech Techo, the refusal to host the SEA Games last year was due to the fact that Cambodia, which emerged from the flames of war, needed a lot of money for the development of the country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that in 2023, Cambodia must host the SEA Games well and with more honor. In preparation for the 2023 SEA Games, Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Ministry of Education and all federations to work hard to strengthen the capacity of athletes and train Cambodian sports resources to be more active. Samdech added that this training is not only for the SEA Games but also for the competition.
For Samdech Techo, owning a SEA Games ranking is not important for Cambodia, but the important thing is to organize a game that is successful and honest.
In order to strengthen the quality of Cambodian sports in response to the hosting of the upcoming SEA Games, Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the national team to assist at the local level as well as local authorities to promote sports activities in schools. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged local authorities to prepare land for sports competitions and schools to have facilities for sports training.
Phnom Penh authorities call on doctors to take care of patients and their families because they are all suffering
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Keo Sok Pisey, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, called on all doctors in Phnom Penh to continue to strengthen the quality of treatment and adhere to professional ethics in the care and treatment of patients.
She also said that while her people are sick and any family members are sick and sent to the hospital, the patient's family often asks for reasons for the symptoms, treatment immediately wants to know the effect of the fear of loss. His family members, who sometimes have a little bit of conflicting words, so as doctors we do not have to be prejudiced but have to explain to them in detail.
This statement was made by the Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh on the occasion of the opening of the meeting to review the work of 2018 and the direction of 2019 of the Department of Health of Phnom Penh on April 4.
"Patients and their relatives are all people who are suffering. They come to us for help, so if there is a misnomer, do not treat him as a hospitality, we have to meet his needs," she said. "It's getting better."
