Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Opportunity to Meet and Have Solidarity Dinner with Over 4,000 Athletes
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of Thursday, April 4, 2019, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, met and had a solidarity meal with the Cambodian sports family. The fourth time at the Koh Pich Center.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Samdech was happy to meet and eat with the athletes again.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports as well as all federations for their joint efforts to promote sports development with excellence.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the athletes for their efforts to develop their abilities and bring honor to the nation through various competitions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked sports teachers and referees for their hard work in sports.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, also thanked all private companies for supporting sports.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the reason why Samdech chose May 2023 as the time for the 32nd SEA Games is because during July or at the end of the year, when Cambodia is busy with elections.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that every time there is an election, there are always riots and other phenomena from the losers. In order not to be disturbed by any activities after the election, Samdech decided to take the contest in May before the election.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, claimed that 2023 is the year that the first expressway in Cambodia, Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville, is completed and can serve to host the SEA Games.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister also explained the reasons why Cambodia became the youngest host for the SEA Games. According to Samdech Techo, not hosting the SEA Games last year because Cambodia, which emerged from the flames of war, needs a lot of money for the development of the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the 2023 SEA Games must be hosted with honor.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Ministry of Education and all federations to work hard to strengthen the capacity of athletes and train sports resources to prepare for the 2023 SEA Games. Samdech added that this training is not only for the SEA Games but also for the competition.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the ownership of the SEA Games does not matter how many ranks, the important thing is to organize a game to be successful and honest.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the national team to help at the local level as well as local authorities to promote sports activities in schools.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged local authorities to prepare land for sports competitions and schools to have facilities for sports training.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that exercise has made people healthier and avoid vascular disease.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged to promote the ethics of the referee in boxing so that there will be accurate judgments so as not to discourage players.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his surprise to some TV stations when there was a match between Cambodians and foreigners, if Cambodians do not fight foreigners, Cambodians will not win.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded that Samdech used to push for a review of the match between Long Sovandoeun and Keo Roomchang until it led to a re-match and finally Keo Roomchang, who was judged by the referee to lose a lot. Times beat Long Sovandoeun.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged to pay attention to the training of arbitrators and strengthen the ethics of arbitrators.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister has warned some TV stations to strengthen their judgments on boxing, otherwise Samdech will come forward to seek justice for that boxing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that from April 12 to 18, for seven days, 120 public buses will be provided to transport people from Phnom Penh to the provinces and from the provinces to Phnom Penh free of charge.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that during the 7 days of the New Year, people in Phnom Penh can also take the public bus for free.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the traffic problem between Ms. Yin Mana and Ms. Dum Rida was a tragedy for both the families of the victims and the perpetrators.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this traffic accident will be a warning to other parents not to abuse their children by letting them drive underage.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all athletes should not be involved in drugs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called for social assistance on three issues, including: Help educate road traffic to reduce traffic accidents, 2. Help educate and prevent the use of drugs, at least friends and family do not use drugs and the third. Help prevent the spread of AIDS.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Orders 4 Capital-Provincial Governors to Resolve the Impact of 230 KV and 500 KV Transmission Lines Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville
Samdech's order further emphasized that in order to ensure the construction of 230 kV and 500 kV transmission lines, complete the construction and put into operation according to the Royal Government's plan, please issue regulations to the relevant ministries and institutions and the four capital-provincial authorities. As follows:
1: The Governor of Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu, Preah Sihanouk Province shall be the direct director of the impact management.
2. The new task force must complete the impact assessment and hand over the land to the 230 kV and 500 kV transmission line construction company Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville within five months from now.
3. If necessary, the capital-provincial governors shall take administrative measures in accordance with the law on expropriation in force in case the appropriate compensation is not accepted by the landowner to ensure that the project in the national interest is continuously extended.
4: The above four capital-provincial governors must report monthly on the progress of addressing the above impacts to the Royal Government.
The following is the order of the Royal Government of Cambodia: Samdech Kittipritthbandit, I would like to bow down to deliver a message of thanks to His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia.
In the message, on behalf of the leadership, members, staff and staff of the Cambodian Red Cross, I would like to express my deep gratitude to His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia. Most of all, he is always willing to receive royal support every quarter to support the humanitarian activities of the Cambodian Red Cross.
