Please do not discriminate and stigmatize drug addicts! Nationwide drug crackdown for April 4: 25 cases cracked, 41 arrested
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide campaign against illegal drugs for April 4, 2019 showed that law enforcement forces cracked down on 25 cases, including 8 cases of use and 17 cases of trafficking, arrested 41 suspects .
According to the report, from January 1 to April 4, 2019, law enforcement forces cracked down on 2,111 cases and detained 4,530 people (372 females), including 121 foreigners. Also. 20 MW Solar Power Station Starts Transmitting Electricity to National Grid to Help Electricity Shortage This Dry Season!
(Phnom Penh): A 60-megawatt solar power station in Thmat Pong, Kampong Speu province, will start generating 20 megawatts of electricity before the plan to help meet the shortage of electricity by the end of the dry season in 2019. This is according to the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Electricity of Cambodia.
Such a joint statement is based on the conclusion of the delegation of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and the delegation of Electricite du Cambodge, which inspected the connection of the solar power system located in Thmat Pong, Kampong Speu province, with a capacity of 60 MW yesterday. .
Delegates confirmed that after testing and transmitting electricity to the national grid safely and successfully today, technicians installed almost 20 megawatts of electricity into the national grid in the first phase on April 4, 2019. Unplanned due to rain in the vulture area today.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia plans to deploy another 200 megawatts of solar power stations in Kampong Chhnang and Pursat provinces, while Cambodia's first 10-megawatt solar power park was launched last year. 2017 in Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province. Tbong Khmum Province Prepares for the First Sankranti Meeting to Celebrate Khmer New Year
The provincial governor said that this year is the first year that the provincial administration celebrates the New Year, next year he will organize a bigger event with more exhibitions and entertainment. He also urged all law enforcement forces to maintain security and order for the people during the Khmer New Year to be in good order, safe and not to throw water at each other, which may cause accidents.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan also called on the people in the province as well as national and international tourists to participate in the Sankran Tbong Khmum event in large numbers.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: Training of professional soldiers for rotation is an important factor to increase work efficiency in reform in all areas in Cambodia
