Germany provides over 600 million US dollars in grant aid to Cambodia over the past 30 years!
(Phnom Penh): From 1992-2018, the German government has provided bilateral grants totaling more than 600 million US dollars to help Cambodia. This is according to the press release of the Council for the Development of Cambodia published on April 4, 2019.
This amount does not include funding provided by the German side to Cambodia through regional and global projects, the European Union, the United Nations, international financial institutions and other multilateral institutions.
The Council for the Development of Cambodia also stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Federal Republic of Germany regularly hold bilateral talks on development cooperation every two years, and this year is the 13th round of talks.
The talks are aimed at strengthening and expanding development cooperation and partnerships, as well as to discuss and agree on the final proposal of the German government on development projects and pledges to provide funding to Cambodia for two years. 2019 2020, which was proposed in the bilateral consultation meeting in November 2018.
This development cooperation focuses on three priority areas: 1: health (protection of social welfare and food security and nutrition), 2: rural development, and 3: governance, which are all priority areas of the Royal Government. Cambodia, as stated in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4.
In fact, on April 4, 2019, the Council for the Development of Cambodia organized an inter-ministerial meeting to prepare for the talks on development cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of the Federal Republic of Germany, which will take place from 14-16. May 2019 in Berlin, Federal Republic of Germany.
The above meeting was chaired by Mr. Chheang Yanara, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Committee on Rehabilitation and Development of Cambodia of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (NCDD) and Chairman of the Cambodian Delegation for Negotiations. This.
