Phnom Penh Capital Administration calls on residents to be vigilant and vigilant against fires as the temperature rises to 40 degrees in two months
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has called on all residents to be vigilant and vigilant in the event of a fire, as the temperature will rise to 40 degrees Celsius in the next two months, making it vulnerable to possible fires. This is according to the announcement on fire prevention in the dry season by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, which was received by Fresh News on April 4, 2019.
This announcement confirms that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration is honored to inform all citizens and the public that according to the meteorological forecast, the weather in our country will rise to over 40 degrees Celsius from This goes on for about two months, which makes the hot, dry weather more likely to cause fires eventually.
In particular, all local authorities and competent forces must be prepared and will find all means sufficient to prevent the eventual occurrence of fires in their localities in accordance with the appeal of the Ministry of Interior. The Phnom Penh Capital Administration hopes that the people and authorities at all levels are vigilant at all times to avoid accidents and disasters caused by fires.
