(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee, through the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, on April 1, 2019, submitted its fifth report on the implementation of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights to the UN Human Rights Committee. Cheat already. This is according to the press release of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee published on April 4.
According to a press release issued by the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, the Kingdom of Cambodia became a State Party to the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights on May 26, 1992 and submitted its first report to the Human Rights Committee. United Nations on December 23, 1998.
The Cambodian Committee for Human Rights (CCHR) said that the second, third and fourth compilation reports were submitted in September 2012 and were reviewed by the Committee at its 3157th session (CCPRC / SR.3157) on 31 May. March 2015. In that review, the Committee approved the concluding survey with 31 recommendations for Cambodia to implement.
Then, a technical inter-ministerial meeting was organized to review and correct this report and discuss with civil society organizations before submitting the inter-ministerial meeting at the political level for review and decision. In fact, this fifth report was reviewed and decided by the inter-ministerial meeting on March 12, 2019.
Please note that the main contents included in the above report are summaries and summaries related to laws, regulations, political programs, strategic plans, action plans, other figures, strategic challenges, etc. as a result of the implementation of the recommendations of the Relevant ministries and institutions.
Following the submission of the above report, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee has been preparing to lead an inter-ministerial working group to defend this report before the United Nations Human Rights Commission upon receipt of this notice. On the date of the review session of the 5th report of Cambodia.
