He added that the goal of serving the real interests of veterans is the result of the active and voluntary efforts of the leadership and the Royal Government, especially the Cambodian Veterans Association, which always supports all kinds of assistance. Provides funeral assistance to families, corpses, funeral funds, and charitable movements to support food.
Minister Vong Soth said this in a meeting with the Steering Committee for the 12th Anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day, June 21, 2007 - June 21, 2019, held at the Ministry on April 4. 2019. The steering committee celebrated the anniversary with Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, as the chairman of the steering committee and many other members.
On the occasion of the opening of the meeting, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, asked the officials in charge of organizing the day to pay the utmost attention to the 12th anniversary of the former day. Cambodian fighters are doing well.
Mr. Vong Soth added that the organization of this day is to provide a large part of encouragement to Cambodian veterans and the families of Cambodian veterans who have sacrificed their physical and mental strength and life to help the motherland of Cambodia to achieve peace. Right now.
It should be noted that the Steering Committee for the 12th Anniversary of Cambodian Veterans Day, June 21, 2007 - June 21, 2019 is divided into four sub-committees, including:
1: Content Sub-Committee, which is responsible for preparing draft documents
2: Subcommittee on Protocol and Hospitality
3: Sub-Committee on Security and Public Order
