The following is the decision of the Ministry of Economy and Finance: CamControl branch in Koh Kong province continues to inspect goods at Phum Thmey market and at people's houses in Mondul Seima district, no goods containing banned chemicals were found.
(Koh Kong): Cam Kong branch in Koh Kong province, in cooperation with trade officials, this morning, April 4, 2019, inspected all goods displayed by traders in Phum Thmey market and at people's houses in Pak Klang commune, district. Mondul Seima, Koh Kong province, focusing on vegetables, squid, shrimp, fish, meat, beverages, as a result, no products are defective, chemical or outdated.
Mr. Chea Ny continued that as a result, the CamControl branch and the professional officers inspected the fruits and vegetables at the houses and stalls in the new village market, where the vendors of the CamControl branch did not find any beverages after the expiration date. The production year will contain no chemicals. The professional officers conduct continuous and responsible inspections and the traders have a higher awareness of this issue as well.
