NEC Takes May 26 for the Third Mandate Council Election (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has decided on Sunday, May 26. May 2019 is the election day for Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Council
The district for the third mandate is called the council election.
The NEC has announced the date of the council election on April 3, 2019.
Council elections are non-universal elections in which members of the Commune / Sangkat Council are elected to elect two councils: the Capital Council, the Provincial Council, and the Municipal Council, District Council, and Khan Council.
This election differs from the general election in that each voter casts two ballots to elect a council in each category and has two ballot boxes. The two ballot boxes include: The first yellow ballot used in the election of the City Council, District Council, and Khan Council for one ballot box.
The second white ballot is used in the election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council for another ballot box.
According to the NEC, the number of constituencies and council seats for the third mandate includes: Capital, provinces, a total of 25, with a total of 559 council seats and municipalities, districts and Khans across the country. A total of 203 seats with a total of 3,555 councilors.
The NEC also stated that the total number of voters who are members of the Commune / Sangkat Council is 11,572. The total number of polling stations for this council election is 203, located in towns, districts and Khans.
