(KUALA LUMPUR - MALAYSIA): "The 11th World Halal Conference and the 16th Halal Conference" in Kuala Lumpur, attended by about 1,400 participants from 56 countries and halal exhibition booths from 72 countries. The path to Cambodia to strengthen and strengthen economic, trade, and halal industry relations with the business and leaders of halal institutions in all participating countries.
This was stated by Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Vice Chairman of the Committee for the Inspection of Halal Products of Cambodia this morning, April 3, 2019 at the Malaysian International Trade and Exhibition Center (MITEC) in Kuala Lumpur. Delegates attend the 11th World Halal Conference and the 16th Halal Exhibition
Senior Minister Osman Hassan stated that in line with Cambodia's economic growth and development in all areas, this conference makes it more valuable and beneficial for Cambodia as a partner, as this conference is a special forum for halal industry business people and leaders. Halal institutions around the world meet to share the growth of the halal industry and inform about the investment potential of all sectors in their respective countries.
The talks also focused on participating in the preservation and security of the future of humanity on earth in the age of globalization, which is increasingly demanding the use of food products and access to services.
According to the World Islamic Economic Report 2018, Muslims consumed $ 2.1 trillion worth of halal products and services on food, beverages and daily living in 2017 and are projected to increase. To reach 3 trillion US dollars by 2023
