Following is a decision by the Ministry of Economy and Finance: The European Union provides more than $ 3 million to Cambodia for the reintegration of children from the center to the community.
The current funding of more than US $ 3 million is for the project "Effective Response to Improving the Child Welfare System" (REACT) for the period of 3 years 2019 to 2021 in 5 target provinces. .
The launch of the project "Responding Effectively to Improving the Child Welfare System" (REACT) was held on April 3, 2019 at the Cambodiana Hotel in Phnom Penh.
On this occasion, Mr. Nim Thoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, also expressed support for this project, as it is in line with the Ministry's policy of integrating children in the districts to the community.
He said that living in the center is not a good option, it is only a last resort. That is why the Ministry has set an integration policy for children whose parents, relatives and siblings return to the community to receive better care.
At the same time, Ms. Lon Bormey, Project Manager REACT confirmed that the five target capitals - provinces are Phnom Penh, Kandal, Battambang, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap. She said the project would benefit 1,200 children.
Mr. Nim Thoth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, confirmed that the Ministry of Social Affairs has started to integrate children in the districts to the community since 2016. As of 2018, the Ministry has integrated 1010 children. Geographical distribution and property value for stamp duty base in Kampong Cham province
