The following is the decision of the Ministry of Economy and Finance: The cyclo that Samdech Techo rode was purchased and kept at the Photo Center of Cambodia as a historical object.
Regarding the reason for placing the cyclo at the Photo Center of Cambodia, Mr. Chhay Sophal stated that this center is a place to store historical objects to collect all the old objects related to history. Mr. Cyclo is a legacy that Cambodia has been preserving and left over from the French colonial period, so it is also a historical object.
Mr. Chhay Sophal stated, "I saw a cyclo that Samdech Techo rode with the cyclo workers, so I think I have to buy that cyclo from him so that he can make some money and buy some money to buy a new cyclo." "I brought this cyclo as a souvenir to show to those who visit the place, showing that this is a cyclo that the Prime Minister used to ride in a talk show with cyclo riders."
According to Chhay Sophal, a veteran Cambodian journalist, people abroad like this kind of antiques, just like in museums, they like to find things that senior leaders have used before because Those things are meaningful, and in restaurants, when high-ranking officials come in, they take pictures, which attracts more visitors.
More than $ 230,000 has been spent on setting up the Cambodian Photo Center, starting with a small size with a big vision for the future. After the opening day, the national and international public can visit for free.
The Photo Center of Cambodia also has a display of some of the older media and materials. Visitors spending about an hour or so at the Cambodian Photo Center can learn about some of Cambodia's specific history from before 1970 to the present through photos and video clips. The Ministry of Economy organizes a meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee to review and discuss the "Draft National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023"
