Mr. Sous Yara: Linking the "One Road, One Belt" and "Rectangular Strategies" Initiatives Will Boost Cambodia's Development Momentum
Mr. Sous Yara emphasized that Cambodia is a country that strongly supports the One Belt One Road initiative, expecting that this initiative will contribute to peace and prosperity together. As a small and open economy, Cambodia is committed to building an open and environmentally friendly international system.
To further harmonize the "One Belt One Road" initiative with Cambodia's "Rectangular Strategy", Suos Yara suggested that Chinese companies and factories should build vocational training centers or schools to build. And transfer skills to local workers.
He said that due to the shortage of local skilled labor, most Chinese companies choose to bring in their Chinese workers, who are more expensive than hiring local workers. Chinese companies should also provide on-the-job skills training to local workers to improve productivity and industrial relations.
