According to the press release, the General Assembly is a major annual event of the World Parliamentary Organization with 1,600 participants, including 80 Speakers, 40 Vice Presidents and more than 800 MPs.
During the General Assembly, the Head of the Cambodian Delegation will address the National Assembly as a forum for the promotion of education for peace, security and the rule of law in the General Assembly.
The Cambodian National Assembly delegation will attend the ASEAN Plus Three Asian Parliamentary Coordinating Group, the Asia-Pacific Geopolitical Group, the Women's Parliamentary Forum, the Young Parliamentarians Forum, the Inter-Parliamentary Union Council, the Standing Committees and the World Parliamentary Secretariat.
In addition, the delegation will attend meetings of committees, groups and mechanisms of the Inter-Parliamentary Union, as well as informal meetings with national parliamentary delegations of friendly countries.
