(Phnom Penh): At 7:30 pm on April 2, 2019, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, together with Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor and Mr. Sarin Vanna, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction of Phnom Penh inspected the situation. The flooding of the Tonle Bassac River after the past few days has been strongly criticized by Facebook users and some other circles who are not yet aware of the flooding of the Tonle Bassac canal.
Speaking in an interview with reporters at the site of the landslide, Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that the Phnom Penh administration does not intend to remove the Bassac River, as criticized by Facebook users and some media outlets.
He said that the landfill was only the construction of a wastewater treatment plant that flows into the river because the tributary of the Bassac River suffers from sewage from high-rise buildings and houses of people living on both sides of the river. To protect the environment, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has also decided to build a wastewater treatment plant by equipping this wastewater pump and dropping it into the Boeung Trabek drainage canal.
The governor stressed that "this landfill is the construction of a sewage treatment plant, which is a project of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, not the landfill of traders. Please do not confuse the people."
