(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation and the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents (CATA) have called on all tourism business owners to fulfill their obligations to register for licenses and to properly pay taxes to the state in order to provide revenue to the state. Develop the nation and also be free from fines and punishments.
This joint appeal was made during the second workshop on Tax Obligations for Tourism Enterprises held at Green Palace Hotel, Phnom Penh on April 3, 2019, chaired by Mr. Eng Ratana, Director of the Department of Management. Major taxpayer of the General Department of Taxation and Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of CATA.
