(Phnom Penh): On April 2, 2019, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Vice Chairman of the Supreme National Economic Council, chaired a review meeting on the preparation of a partnership strategy for the development of Cambodia in 2019. - 2023 between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Asian Development Bank (ADB) at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
It should be noted that under the cooperation between the Royal Government and ADB, the draft strategic partnership document for the development of Cambodia 2019-2023 was prepared in consultation with the relevant ministries, institutions of the Royal Government, the private sector, and civil society organizations. As well as research institutions.
Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State for Strategic Partnership for Cambodia's Development 2019-2023, will set out a joint strategic framework for the next five years under the Asian Development Bank's co-financing to meet development needs. Of Cambodia, especially in achieving its goal of becoming a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
He also praised the ADB for preparing and revising the draft strategic document at the request of the Cambodian side in a series of meetings in the past to make the partnership strategy more consistent with the National Strategic Development Plan. Of Cambodia, especially the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, which is the socio-economic policy agenda of the political program of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
In fact, this strategic document is based on four pillars: (1) economic diversification and competitive promotion, (2) human resource development, and (3) sustainable development. 4) Governance in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4.
He also called on the ADB to continue to support decentralization and deconcentration reforms, especially the analysis and division of functions that will be transferred from the national to the sub-national level.
