Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia is negotiating with neighboring countries to open more new border crossings to expand trade with each other (Video inside) (Kampot): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who struggled to liberate the country from The flames of war until today's development say that Cambodia is currently in talks with neighboring countries to open more new border crossings to expand trade with each other.
Samdech Techo PM's statement was made on the occasion that Samdech and Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia presided over the inauguration of the Kampot Water Supply System, built with the assistance of the Government of Japan. More than 26 million US dollars this morning, March 2, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "For the neighboring countries, we have already turned and continue to promote trade with the neighboring countries, because our border has become a place of peace. "Friendship, Cooperation and Development Already We are negotiating with Laos, Thailand and Vietnam to open more new channels to promote bilateral relations with our neighbors."
It should be noted that in 2018, the trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand will reach more than 8 billion US dollars, the trade volume between Cambodia and Laos will be 24 million US dollars and the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam will be more than 5,000 US dollars. Million US dollars.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the achievement of these trade volume was due to the Royal Government of Cambodia having a clear vision to lead the country in a context of peace and good relations with neighboring countries. "So this point can be traced back to the vision of a nation governance that puts the internal situation in a context of peace and good neighborly relations with countries bordering us," he said.
It should be noted that the report on the export-import of Cambodia presented by the Ministry of Commerce states that in 2018, the volume of Cambodia's trade with foreign countries totaled 24.985 million US dollars. For the export of Cambodian goods to other countries amounted to 11.21 million US dollars, this figure increased from the same period in 2017 to only 10.7777 million US dollars.
