(Phnom Penh): Ms. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, said on April 2, 2019 that the implementation of the Royal Government's strategies and policies has boosted the living conditions, status and role of women. Better day by day.
Ms. Men Sam An's remarks were made on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the results of 2018 and work direction 2019 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, which was held at the Phnom Penh Hotel on the morning of the 2nd. This April 2019.
Ms. Men Sam An said that although Cambodia has made progress in terms of gender equality, including the empowerment of women, we still have some challenges that need to be addressed gradually, including:
1: Women's participation in public, political and economic sectors is still incomplete and strong 2: In the field of education, especially at the tertiary and postgraduate levels, gender inequality still exists Violence against women and girls according to court and legal procedures, as well as the provision of services to help victims, has not been smooth and untimely.
Ms. Men Sam An stated that, therefore, 2019 is the first year, the sixth legislature of the National Assembly, it is time for us to continue to find a solution together. To achieve even better, we need to focus on the following practical tasks:
1: To pay attention to each other by giving priority to increasing the number of women to have leadership roles in all fields and at all levels according to their capabilities and to help solve various problems that arise in the job opportunities. Their role.
2. Strengthen the women's network through women's gatherings and strengthen the capacity of women to fulfill their role as decision makers, those responsible for management and public administration.
3. Jointly enforce the law and expedite the trial process in order to prevent gender-based violence and to work together to establish a formal joint statistical base that can monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of victim assistance services. Victims of gender-based violence.
4: The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports must instruct all educational institutions to strengthen the implementation of discipline, while continuing to provide opportunities for girls at all levels to study science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM), which is the age of technological modernization. .
5. The Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Ministry of Information must effectively control the use of the Internet throughout the country to prevent many issues related to violence, exploitation of women and girls through the Internet and other media. Loss of social order.
6: The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ministry of Information and all media must continue to strengthen and promote social morality, the values of Cambodian women and families through the establishment of good educational programs to show the character of Cambodian women, especially the dress with dignity. The characteristics of a Cambodian woman deserve to be a country with a glorious civilization in all generations.
7. Increasing investment in gender equality, especially through the review of fiscal policies to establish and increase public spending on gender equality, as well as monitoring and analyzing the impact of public spending on gender inequality through Budgeting programs that address gender issues.
At the same time, it is necessary to implement the strategy of gender mainstreaming of all ministries and institutions through the preparation of budget plans and inclusion in the budget according to the programs of ministries and institutions in order to receive the national budget and additional development partner budget for the implementation of their work.
8. Strengthening accountability mechanisms for gender equality is a key task to measure the effectiveness of the implementation of policies and measures of ministries and institutions, as well as to ensure adequate resources for gender work. Therefore, each ministry and institution must strengthen the means of monitoring and control, as well as evaluate the allocation of resources, its budget allocation for gender work.
9. Continuing to promote women's participation in the economy is a priority to increase the economic power of women and their families and enable them to participate in public and political work.
She stressed that in this spirit, relevant ministries and institutions must continue to prioritize the participation of women in the economy by increasing women's awareness of access to relevant services to develop businesses for small and medium enterprises. Samdech Techo Hun Sen sends a message of thanks to the King for sending a message wishing him a happy birthday on April 4
