Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurates Kampot water supply system worth more than 26 million USD
(Kampot): On Tuesday, April 13, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will officially inaugurate the water supply system. Kampot province was built with the help of the Japanese government worth more than 26 million US dollars.
Construction of the Kampot water supply system began in July 2016 and was completed in August 2018. Through this water supply system, the Kampot Water Supply Authority will have a total production capacity of 13,260 cubic meters per day, which is more than twice the previous production capacity.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, the presence of the new water supply system, along with a total distribution network of 176.9 km, enables the Kampot Water Supply Authority to supply safe, sustainable water. And reasonable price with an average price of 1,400 riel / m3 for people in Kampot city and Teuk Chhou district, a total of more than 13,000 families.
The presence of this water supply system also contributes to the Kampot Provincial Water Supply Authority to achieve the government's policy that "to expand the scope of water supply in urban areas to 90% by 2023 and "100% by 2025 to serve the basic needs of the people, as well as for production and services."
Kampot is a coastal province with potential for tourism development and seaports. In recent years, Kampot has undergone significant changes in terms of physical infrastructure and growth in economic and social development. At the same time, the demand for clean water has also increased significantly.
Thus, the presence of a clean water supply system in Kampot province arises from a grant from the Japanese government, which contributes significantly to the well-being of the people, economic and social development, and especially to attract more investment. In this coastal city as well.
Citizens applaud the achievements of the red road repaired by APSARA Authority at West Baray
(Siem Reap): In order to restore the ancient infrastructure and facilitate general travel for people as well as tourists, the APSARA Authority has just repaired two red dirt roads behind the western Baray Dam. The repairs are on the east and west sides, with a total length of nearly 3,000 meters.
Mr. Moan Phanith, Technical Officer of the Water Management Department in charge of the work at the West Baray, said that in the past, the road along the back of the dam was damaged, there were large potholes, and when it rained, there was always water leaking, which affected the back of the dam. Damage. In addition, traveling on the road behind the dam is difficult, with only bicycles and motorbikes accessible to residents.
In addition to the above benefits, Mr. Phanit said that this road also facilitates tourists who like to visit the sunrise and sunset at the back of the baray. The repairs totaled nearly 3 kilometers, but the previous repairs totaled 10 kilometers. APSARA Authority will continue to repair the remaining 10 km of the road on the back of the baray.
People passing through these roads applauded the achievements and thanked the APSARA Authority for the development of new achievements in the local people. Mr. Chhay Phat and his family riding a motorbike across the newly renovated Dey Krahorm Road expressed their interest that traveling on the road behind the dam is now easier because in the dry season there were big potholes and the rainy season was very slippery. It is very difficult to travel.
