(Prey Veng): PRASAC inaugurated a library building at Krachap Primary and Secondary School under the presidency of Mr. Yav Sanin, Governor of Kampong Trabek District and Deputy Governor of Prey Veng Province in late March 2019. .
Also present at the event were Mr. Sun Bonna, Deputy Director of Curriculum Development Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Ven Proney, Deputy Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, and Mr. Oum Sam Oeun, Executive Vice President of PRASAC MFI Monks, local authorities, teachers, students and hundreds of people in the community of Peam Mantear commune, Kampong Trabek district, Prey Veng province.
Mr. Ven Prony, Deputy Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, reported on the situation of education in Kampong Trabek district and thanked PRASAC for building a library building in Kampong Trabek district, Prey Veng province. Basic education.
Mr. Oum Sam Oeun said, "The construction of this library building is a social work that PRASAC is designed to benefit the people in the community and to enhance the capacity of students who are the children and grandchildren of the people in the community." In the countryside.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Sun Bonna, Deputy Director of the Curriculum Development Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, also expressed his deep gratitude and appreciation for PRASAC for funding the construction of this library. He said that this library building is very valuable for students and residents of Kampong Trabek, because previously it was difficult to find documents or books for more information.
"But now they are not as difficult as before, because now there is a beautiful library building with enough books for students as well as citizens to do more research," he said. He also thanked PRASAC for its good cooperation with the Curriculum Development Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in implementing this project successfully to contribute to the cultivation of reading culture and human resources in Cambodia.
Finally, he also asked teachers, students and parents to help maintain and use this library as much as possible by encouraging more reading, revitalizing, love and take good care of all books to use. Long lasting and many generations.
