People in Koh Kong town are happy after receiving heavy rain for one month when there is a shortage of water for daily use
Residents say the heavy rains have left thousands of families in the province extremely happy, having been affected by water shortages for months.
People are preparing to filter the rainwater and put it in jars, buckets, bowls, pots and pans for use because they do not know when it will continue to rain and they do not know when the Water Supply Authority will use the water again.
Residents said that despite the thunder, they tried to filter the rainwater to save for daily use.
