Mr. Em Chanmakara: Addressing the major challenges of people with disabilities requires the support of all institutions, both human and financial resources of the Royal Government
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Em Chanmakara, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council, said that solving large structural problems as well as many important practical challenges in the field of disability is not easy. We need the support of all relevant institutions, human resources and financial resources of the Royal Government.
He added that the settlement required a number of reforms, including reaching the beginning of the review and consultation process for proposing amendments to the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities in order to harmonize with progress. New in today's society to ensure that people with disabilities in Cambodia receive more benefits and policies from the Royal Government.
The remarks by the Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Council for the Action of Persons with Disabilities, Mr. Em Chanmakara, Representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Alumni and Youth Rehabilitation, took place in the "National Workshop on Policy Recommendations and Data Collection to People with autism for the first time in Cambodia "organized on April 1, 2019 at Tonle Bassac 2 Restaurant, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that in the spirit of promoting education for the mentally retarded and the autistic, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has cooperated with NGOs to implement this program to support the development of special education classes, incorporating various curricula. Such as: sports programs, art training programs, as well as many other professional programs.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia will launch the National Strategic Plan on Disability for the next 5 years 2019-2023 to promote the reform of the disability sector to enhance institutional capacity, strengthen social and economic infrastructure in order to create employment opportunities. For people with disabilities, reduce poverty and develop important jobs of the disability sector in Cambodia.
The growth of Cambodia's disability sector and economic development is seen as an incentive policy, an active incentive from the Cambodian government to investment companies, including the provision of priority opportunities for the recruitment of persons with disabilities. Work too. The Royal Government of Cambodia is committed to recruiting 2% of people with disabilities to work in government ministries and institutions.
How to choose a skill for a suitable career
(Phnom Penh): Choosing skills for a lifetime career of each of us is important and can not be overlooked. If you make the right choices, you will lose time, money, or even great remorse for being in a work environment that does not suit your interests.
You probably already know that choosing a skill or doing something that is against your will is like destroying your natural talents. You just have to be more discriminating with the help you render toward other people. Therefore, what should we do to choose the right skill?
Based on past experience and research, there are four key factors to consider in choosing a suitable skill:
1: Natural talent: Each person has different talents by birth, some are good at arithmetic, calculating exercises or solving problems related to real subjects, and some are also good at art, painting or music, etc. As a result, each of us pursues a different career. Before embracing any skill, we should judge whether the basic characteristics of that skill really match our natural talents.
Studying is a long-term investment, some may take years to complete their studies in a program. Therefore, each of us should consider researching the relevant information clearly and find out their true interests, and what is indispensable is to choose a school with standard teaching techniques, including Internationally recognized.
