The Lieutenant General made this statement at a press conference on "Legal Aspects and Traffic Accident Prevention Measures in Cambodia" with the participation of Mr. Sok Pheng, Secretary of State of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Vice Chairman of the Legal Council. Mr. Phay Siphan, Spokesman of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which took place on April 1, 2019 at the Office of the Council of Ministers.
The head of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the National Police General Commissioner said: "This year, what we are worried about is that so far this quarter (3 months) more than 500 people died. "Some days there are up to nine people and some days up to 5.7 people, this is a problem." The lieutenant general said that each year, Cambodia loses $ 350 million due to traffic accidents, while more than 78% of fatalities do not wear helmets.
Lt. Gen. Run Rath Veasna also called on all institutions to educate and disseminate the traffic law to all staff and the public as much as possible in order to help raise awareness among the people about the consequences. Occurs due to this accident as well.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Pheng also mentioned the legal aspect of Cambodia that the payment of compensation to the victims is a civil compensation that does not lead to exemption from criminal liability, and the harm caused by Victims of loss of life as well as property damage in connection with this traffic crime have two consequences: civil and criminal consequences.
He explained that the civil consequences arose from the civil compensation arising from the autonomy of the will of the individual and the private individual, meaning that the compensation to be paid depends on the victim and the perpetrator negotiating on the matter. Happened only.
Mr. Sok Pheng continued that although the perpetrators resolved the compensation to the victims by mutual consent, the perpetrators could not be freed from criminal liability. But the masses must remember that if a mob beats the perpetrators, they will become the perpetrators of a new crime of intentional violence and murder. Guilty of mistakes.
Mr. Sok Pheng also asked the media to help spread more measures to prevent traffic accidents. End all violence against perpetrators and find out about the law together. Another important task of this propaganda system is to spread the illegal activities of the masses using violence against the perpetrators.
