An international roundtable suggests that students should not be banned from using smartphones as it enhances classroom knowledge.
(Phnom Penh): In a roundtable program focusing on the challenges of Cambodian youth in the development of information technology and digital systems, the speakers said that students should not be banned from using smartphones because of the use of smartphones in Learning helps increase knowledge in the classroom.
The roundtable was held on the afternoon of March 28, 2019 with the participation of government officials, representatives of state institutions, the Senate, the private sector, representatives of the European Chamber of Commerce, international organizations, professors and more than 70 students at the Francophone Research Center in Phnom Penh in the Institute. Cambodian technology.
The theme of the roundtable was made at a time of progress in the field of communications and modern technology. Speakers and participants highlighted the many benefits of science, questioning the various issues that negatively affect youth and education.
Representatives of the Ministry of Education said that students should not be banned from using smartphones because it helps increase knowledge in the classroom. In particular, teachers should find ways to motivate and encourage students to study, research and use the phone effectively, otherwise students will misuse.
In addition to the negative effects, some speakers also mentioned the benefits that many young people have taken advantage of the evolution of technology and social media through research, online and remote learning, good sharing, creative ideas and Create many new applications and so on.
The roundtable ended with a private snack and informal meeting to increase communication between students, professors, entrepreneurs and representatives from various institutions in a friendly atmosphere.
