As a measure to release and avoid contaminated water that could damage Cambodia's coasts and seas, the Cambodian Coastal Area Management and Development Committee, headed by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, has decided to build four wastewater treatment plants along Cambodia's coast.
This wastewater treatment plant is located on Ekareach Beach, behind Sokha Beach Hotel, at O Sam Ath and at Ochheuteal Beach. The four wastewater treatment plants have been under construction for four months and were officially put into operation on March 29, 2019 under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara.
After all the treatment plants were put into operation, the sewage canal that flowed into the sea at Sokha Beach for many years was closed to the sea and instead was pumped down to the treatment plant at Ochheuteal. This is a big success step in saving the Cambodian coast from dirty water.
With this success, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara expressed his happiness and considered this a step in the fulfillment of duties under the orders of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara also called on the people to protect this beautiful beach for all generations and be proud to be born a Cambodian.
