Mr. Neth Pheaktra: Every citizen can participate in protecting the earth by saving water, electricity, planting trees and reducing waste
This is the appeal of the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, on the night of March 30, 2019 on the occasion of the celebration of "One Hour for the Earth" 2019 under the theme "Connect with the Earth" in The premises of Aeon Mall 2 Sen Sok with the participation of hundreds of people.
In order to prevent and prevent wildfires, Secretary of State Neth Pheaktra said that the Ministry of Environment would like to appeal to the sub-national administrative units, the Department of Environment, the competent authorities, including local communities and all stakeholders to implement the following measures:
1: Prevent and advise to be very careful about the use of fire as a means to harvest non-timber forest products, burning forests, intercepting animals and burning grasslands, etc.
2. Prevent the clearing, encroachment, burning of forests and flooded forests for other purposes, which are illegal activities and cause forest fires, flooded forests and spread to the homes of people, offices, subdivisions and physical infrastructure in and Around protected areas.
3. Be very careful to use fire as a means of burning various wastes in protected areas and biodiversity corridors.
4: Relevant authorities must instruct stakeholders to implement appropriate technical measures that can ensure the safety of wildfires by extinguishing the fire as necessary before leaving the fire.
5: In case of severe wildfires, the relevant authorities should take immediate action to prevent it through the declaration of emergency, and the Capital-Provincial Unity Command must direct the use of mixed forces, including people, communities, monks, civil servants. The armed forces and all those involved in the base work together to effectively prevent and extinguish wildfires.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra expressed strong optimism that the spirit of celebrating "One Hour for the Earth" now will make people more aware and more actively involved in protecting the environment and the planet. Our planet is sustainable and beautiful. Mr. Chea Sophara appreciates the activities of Tycoon Tea Vichet and inspires young people to plant seedlings and conserve rare animals
