Citizens ask Sihanoukville veterinarian to effectively prevent mixed meat smuggled from neighboring countries
(Preah Sihanouk): Citizens, civil servants, especially housewives living in Sihanoukville, expressed concern again after the veterinary officers of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Sihanouk Province in the next few days caught fresh meat More than 100 kilos smuggled from neighboring countries for distribution in Sihanoukville.
Starting from this issue, the housewife requested the relevant officials of the relevant institutions, including: CamControl branch, especially the veterinarian of the Department of Agriculture of Sihanoukville to help increase the inspection activities, especially fresh meat that is being sold both legally and illegally. Legally in various markets in Sihanoukville to be effective.
In this case, both people, especially housewives living in Sihanoukville, expressed concern that fresh meat illegally imported from neighboring countries to distribute in Sihanoukville every day contains banned chemicals that lead To affect the health of people or consumers.
At this point, the people requested the relevant officials, especially veterinarians of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Sihanoukville to help increase the work of inspecting the import of all kinds of fresh meat at the border through the bus and sell at Markets regularly and efficiently.
Mr. Nen Chamroeun said that the arrest of fresh meat imported by traders from neighboring countries is a measure to prevent the illegal import of fresh meat to help maintain the health of people and prevent plague. Africa on meat or meat containing various chemicals.
Mr. Nen Chamroeun added that as a first step, veterinary officials required the owners of the goods and the bus owners who transported the illegal meat to make a contract to stop the illegal import of fresh meat in case of non-compliance. Under the guidance of professional officers, some individuals will face legal action.
