Royal Government decides to turn Rural Development Bank into Rural Development and Agriculture Bank with an additional $ 50 million
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has confirmed that the Royal Government has decided to turn the Rural Development Bank into a Rural Development and Agriculture Bank with an additional investment of US $ 50 million to strengthen its capacity. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement while he was chairing the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum held at the Peace Palace on March 29, 2019. The forum is attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia and investors, businessmen who are investing and doing business in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "I have decided to turn the Rural Development Bank into a Rural Development and Agriculture Bank, which serves as both a commercial bank and a policy bank .... For this purpose, I have decided to increase the capital by 50 Million dollars to the Rural Development Bank.
Samdech Techo emphasized that this was done in order to strengthen the Rural Development Bank as a policy bank of the Royal Government and to be able to provide full financing and services effectively and sustainably for the development of agriculture and economy. Rural.
Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank, once confirmed to Fresh News that the transformation of the Rural Development Bank into a source of capital from the public, from the Royal Government and other sources in response to the economic growth. Digital. He said the shift was aimed at providing banking services nationwide, with regional branches and mobile offices as well.
It should be noted that the Rural Development Bank was established in 1998 by Sub-Decree No. 01, dated January 21, 1998, in order to fill the gap between demand and supply of financial services in rural areas to contribute. Reduce the poverty of the Cambodian people.
