The Ministry of Health and relevant partners raise further directions to achieve the TB Eradication Strategy by 2035
(Phnom Penh): Although in 2018, the TB control program in Cambodia achieved new important achievements, especially the maintenance of a successful treatment rate of more than 90% and more than 20,000 cases of tuberculosis. Health and relevant national-international partners continue to raise the direction to achieve the direction in line with the new international strategy called "Strategy to end TB 2016-2035 and sustainable development goals 2019-2030.
This was stated by the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Dr. Yok Sambath, during the closing ceremony of the 24th National TB Control Conference on March 29, 2019 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
In addition, the Secretary of State provided additional encouragement with five recommendations, including:
* Further strengthen cooperation with partners at all levels and further mobilize resources to achieve the goals of the National Program for 2019 and the following year to research all types of TB patients with all plans and please continue to maintain treatment rates. More than 90% success
* Promote the provision of TB research and treatment services to high-risk groups, including TB, HIV, prison prisons, pediatric tuberculosis, diabetic tuberculosis and adult tuberculosis.
* Need to prepare, strengthen and expand to better fight against drug-resistant TB
* Keep DOTT's anti-TB activities at the health center and further expand the DOT community, which is the closest medical care activity to the patient's home.
* Continue to encourage the participation of other health institutions such as the General Department of Prisons, the Department of Health of the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, private health care services, including NGOs and the Cambodian Association in the fight against tuberculosis.
