(Phnom Penh): Mr. Svay Sitha, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Press and Quick Reaction Unit, said that fake news is not only related to political security, but it is a dangerous psychological war that has been created to attract people. Popular through misleading the public.
The senior official made the remarks on the afternoon of March 29, 2019 at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the occasion of the closing of the vocational training course on fake information, provided a summary and highlighted some key points. About 100 participants, who are representatives from ministries, institutions, capitals and provinces, as a basis for practical implementation in each ministry and institution after receiving training for 5 days.
Mr. Svay Sitha also noted that some false information is currently polluting the society and causing people to lose time, money, cheat or make wrong decisions by fake media caused by some people. Therefore, all participants must monitor and verify the information that has occurred on social media and must work together to prevent and neutralize fake information in a timely manner.
In addition, in order to contribute to stopping the spread of fake news, the media, public officials and Facebook users must work together to fight fake news by not spreading or sharing fake news and participating in neutralizing information. Fake when it is made in time.
Svay Sitha also said that many countries have enacted laws to combat fake news, including France, Russia, Malaysia, Qatar and Egypt. Many other countries have also begun to take measures to address the rise of fake news, such as Australia, Belgium, Canada, China, Bangladesh, India, Singapore and the Philippines.
Mr. Svay Sitha encouraged all participants to increase and strengthen friendships and relationships with supporters and the media, as well as reporters. Mr. Svay Sitha also urged all participants to work responsibly and professionally in the fight against this false information.
