Senior Health Officer: Ensuring the quality, safety and effectiveness of medicines is the main task in providing services to patients
(Siem Reap): The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Dr. O Vandin, stated that ensuring the quality, safety and effectiveness of medicines licensed in Cambodia is a major and important task in improving the quality of health services to the people. .
This statement was made by the Secretary of State on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the National Workshop on "Quality Control of Medicines on the Market" for health officials from the Department of Medicine, National Center for Health Experiments, National Center for Tuberculosis and Hansen, National Center for Combating Diseases. AIDS, dermatitis and STIs, central drug depots and drug control agents from 12 provincial health departments.
"For the effectiveness of the drug or the quality of the drug is closely related to the quality of treatment, if the drug is not the right quality according to technical standards, the quality of treatment can not be successful, although The doctor was skilled and talented no matter what. "And if the medicine is of poor quality, it will seriously affect public health as well as the family economy and the national economy."
In addition, she said that the Ministry of Health has always paid attention to and actively supported the activities to control and monitor the quality of medicines in Cambodia, for drugs that are allowed to be sold or circulated in the market, the Ministry of Health has assigned agents to control Regularly inspect medicines and buy medicines from the market to re-analyze the quality and take action against any drugs that do not meet the technical standards.
She added that the workshop provided knowledge on the use of tools to identify drugs and where to extract drugs based on risk. If we follow this tool, we will be able to select the medicine and the location to be targeted, using less money and save time. The workshop also improved the protocol for monitoring the quality of medicines in line with the current situation in the country.
The workshop on risk-based drug control in the market has contributed to preventing the detection and early action of counterfeit and substandard drugs, which is now a model for Cambodia. Area.
Meanwhile, the World Health Organization (WHO) Representative from Geneva, Switzerland, Diana Aram Lee, added that the problem of counterfeit and substandard medicines was not unique to any country, but was global. Which we must solve together. The World Health Organization (WHO) is committed to strengthening the capacity of drug regulatory agencies, including supporting drug regulatory activities in the marketplace.
At the same time, in order to ensure the quality, safety and effectiveness of the medicine, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health added that the work of quality control of this medicine requires the participation of relevant parties who have been trained now, especially all officials must implement. Consistent, such as:
* Departments of Medicine, Food, Medical Equipment and Cosmetics and Capital / Provincial Health Departments shall regularly inspect pharmaceutical establishments, importers, pharmaceutical importers and pharmaceutical establishments in accordance with their duties.
To control the quality of medicines on the market, to determine the type of drug and the location of the drug extract based on the risk classification.
* The National Center for Health Experiments must continue to strengthen its capacity to control the quality of medicines, including traditional medicine, health supplements and cosmetics.
Taking this opportunity, she called on all people to avoid the use of over-the-counter drugs and drugs sold on social media and websites, because these drugs are not safe, but it costs you money to extend the time. Treatment and can cause life-threatening.
