In addition, Samdech also thanked the Ministry of Public Works for its efforts to negotiate and get the results of the parking fee reduction. Some companies have also agreed to reduce their fees from $ 5 TEU on container loading services.
"For this price, the company claims that there will be more discounts if the port has a discount," he said. In this case, the profit from the reduction of parking fees will be approximately $ 2,500,000. "So at this point I propose to continue the conversation because the carrier has said that they will be able to lower prices if both ports lower prices, so this point asks both ports to consider."
"We must not take advantage of these two ports by killing the country's economy," he said. We would like to reduce the profits at both ports, but it is for the benefit of our entire national economy. "Therefore, it is hoped that this measure will be further reduced to make it more profitable for shipping fees inconsistencies between containers."
