Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of Meeting with Investors on Investment, Trade and Business in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, March 29, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum. Held at the Peace Palace.
The forum is also attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia and investors who are investing and doing business in Cambodia. The forum has an open discussion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen with the leaders of relevant ministries and institutions and business people in Cambodia on issues related to investment, trade and business for more than 5 hours.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is sincerely grateful for the generous assistance of international partners.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the future, Cambodia needs more cooperation to provide mutual benefits with our key partners based on mutual respect.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the spirit of pre-action, considered and prepared sufficient measures and budget to solve the problem that arose and ensure the national economic growth and the stability of people's lives.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the failure of the Royal Government-Private Sector Forum since 2014 was due to the work being completed by the working group without any obstruction.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the talks between the Cambodian and Turkish sides have reached an agreement and bring the power plant to Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Deputy Prime Minister and all the working groups for successfully resolving some issues in the past.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that in 2018, Cambodia's economic growth exceeded expectations by more than 7%
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the economic growth in 2018, which is also the election year, is due to the vibrancy of all sectors
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that all these economic achievements came from the participation of all investors in Cambodia
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today I will summarize and announce the launch of a package of reform measures to address the structural problems of villages, communes, as well as other important practical challenges that cause investors and businesses. People are experiencing in their business.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen proposes discounts at both Cambodian ports
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that to solve all these problems, Cambodia has invested in a lot of electricity generation
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the price of electricity will be further reduced in the future
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that next week there will be a meeting of the Council of Ministers to decide on the construction of some more power plants.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen, after adjusting the payment of other services, the private sector gained $ 400 million from the cost of other services. Samdech Techo claims that according to this amendment, even if the EU does not provide preferential tariffs, Cambodia will not die.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he must follow the advice of His Majesty the King and not sell his national sovereignty to any foreigner.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the fact that Samdech did not sell the customs institution at the request of foreigners in the past was the right decision because now the revenue from customs is the national revenue and not distributed to foreigners. If Samdech listens to foreign advice from the past, Cambodia will have to distribute customs revenue to foreigners.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen proposes to reduce the number of holidays by adding one day off each day plus New Year and Pchum Ben.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has ordered the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to reduce inspections in factories.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodian Rice Federation is considering filing a complaint to the World Trade Organization. Samdech Techo said that this tax is because Italian rice does not compete with Cambodian rice.
* However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to use the full potential of the existing Cambodian market for Cambodian agricultural products.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen decides to transform the Rural Development Bank into a Rural Development and Agriculture Bank. This modification allows the bank to participate in agricultural development. Samdech Techo has decided to add $ 50 million to the bank.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to end the Royal Company's railway business of Duke Kith Meng, leaving the Ministry of Public Works and Transport as interim manager to wait for a new company to invest in improving the railway.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decision to terminate the business was not the fault of Duke Kith Meng, but to find a way to improve Cambodia's railways.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the re-investment bidding for the railway is open to all companies to participate in the bidding, not to tie the mosquito net as before.
* Samdech Techo expressed confidence that Mr. Prayuth Chan Ocha will remain the Prime Minister of Thailand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth to release compensation to Kith Meng Company after the completion of the railway business.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has about $ 3 billion in treasury reserves.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked the Chinese, Vietnamese and Japanese ambassadors to provide locomotives and develop Cambodia's railways.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that Cambodian trains in both directions will transport people free of charge.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the use of automation systems in various ministries and institutions. Samdech Techo Hun Sen praises the Ministry of Public Works and the Ministry of Economy for their efforts to develop and promote the use of automation in the provision of services.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that since Samdech led the country, he has never used foreign money to pay the salaries of civil servants and the armed forces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will also consider joining the Trans-Pacific Partnership (TPP) if all ASEAN member countries agree to join this agreement.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen agreed to the request of the private sector by allowing ministries and institutions to provide services online.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also agreed to the request of the private sector to try to prevent too many strikes and demonstrations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked countries that want to punish Cambodia what they think of Cambodia, which is playing a role in contributing to peacekeeping activities in other countries as some countries withdraw. Samdech Techo questioned that if the Royal Government of Cambodia is not legal, can Cambodia afford to go to the international arena.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia is a poor country in ASEAN, but Cambodia actively participates with the international community in humanitarian activities through the Blue Hat Army.
