(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, on March 29, 2019, confirmed that the investment situation in Cambodia has improved in the last five years by approving the project. 959 investment projects with a total investment of 23 billion US dollars, which can create 1 million jobs.
For the first two months of 2019, 73 investment projects were approved with an investment capital of about 2.2 billion US dollars, compared to the same period in 2018, only 39 investment projects with a total investment of 327 million US dollars.
This was confirmed by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth at the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum at the Peace Palace on March 29, 2019.
"Cambodia remains a potential destination for both local and foreign investors," said Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth. "Obviously, based on the record of the Council for the Development of Cambodia for the five years (2014-2018), the investment situation is good."
According to the Minister of Economy, Cambodia's economic growth has averaged 7.7 percent over the past two decades, plus the fruits of the past implementation of the Rectangular Strategy, coupled with the introduction and implementation of the principles. Cambodia's Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025 and other relevant policies have encouraged investment activities in Cambodia to expand and diversify.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that with the increase in investment activity recorded by the Council for the Development of Cambodia, there were other investment activities that were not registered with the Council for the Development of Cambodia, including the construction sector and the banking and financial sectors. There has also been significant progress.
