Minister of Justice Meets with Samdech Techo Sen, Chief of Volunteer Lawyers, Mr. Ky Tech, to Accelerate Prosecution Procedures to Protect the Rights of Pregnant Women, Young Children and Elderly Women in Prison
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of March 28, 2019, Mr. Ang Vong Vathana, Minister of Justice, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, and Mr. Ky Tech, President of the Samdech Techo Sen Volunteer Law Group, and a group of 30 volunteer lawyers met. Collaborate and find solutions to expedite the trial of women in prison, especially pregnant women, women with children, minors and the elderly at the Ministry of Justice.
On that occasion, Mr. Ky Tech stated that the purpose for which he led a group of volunteer lawyers to discuss this work was to follow the high advice of Samdech Techo and asked the Minister to cooperate and help issue a notice or circular. An introduction to all provincial / municipal courts to request cooperation when working with a group of volunteer lawyers to perform their duties in the provinces and regions.
In response, the Minister of Justice stated that the Ministry had already prepared and instructed the prosecutors, judges and court presidents in the provinces to cooperate with Samdech Techo Sen's group of volunteer lawyers at their local level.
Minister Ang Vong Vathana added that in order to cooperate with the volunteer lawyers, Samdech Techo Ministry has also appointed a representative of the Ministry to be ready to work with the volunteer lawyers in all operations.
Tycoon Tea Vichet invites monks to pray in front of the altar of Mrs. Mao Pich Nil for passengers on National Road 4
Mr. Oknha Tea Vichet said that he noticed that traffic accidents on National Road 4 occurred almost every day, so he came together to organize a procession of monks to organize Buddhist ceremonies. This is to contribute to reducing or preventing the rate of traffic accidents on National Road 4 to reduce the number.
Veteran comedian Neay Koy was also present at the ceremony. After praying and inviting monks to pray in the Buddhist way, Mr. Oknha Tea Vichet believes that the prayer ceremony in front of the altar of Mrs. Mao Pichnil on National Road 4 above will lead to a reduction in traffic accidents. Low number.
He said that the reason why he asked the team to pray and invite monks to pray for relief on this occasion, because the subsequent traffic accidents on National Road 4 continue to occur almost every day and caused. Causing deaths and injuries as well as damage to vehicles and destruction of both public and private property.
Tycoon Tea Vichet also reminded all drivers or road users to adhere to the code of ethics in driving, especially to respect the road traffic law regularly, no matter how close or far the road. In particular, it is necessary to understand and tolerate each other when using public roads to reduce the rate of traffic accidents in Cambodia, especially to reduce traffic accidents on National Road 4 to reduce.
