(Phnom Penh): The Five-Year Strategic Plan for Combating HIV / AIDS is a plan that contributes to the National AIDS Authority and the Royal Government of Cambodia in their commitment to eradicate HIV / AIDS by 2025 to prevent the spread of HIV / AIDS. People dying of HIV and AIDS. This was stated by Mr. Sok Buntha, Under Secretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs and a representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
He said this at a workshop to find input into the draft five-year strategic plan for the fight against HIV / AIDS of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation held on March 28, 2019 with the participation of officials from the Ministry of Social Affairs. Chairman, partners of many other relevant organizations.
Workshop on input into the drafting of a five-year HIV / AIDS Strategic Plan with relevant partner organizations to strengthen the prevention and care of HIV and AIDS victims and other important tasks to identify shortcomings and work Improved service delivery to be more efficient.
Speaking at the seminar, Mr. Sok Buntha thanked the National AIDS Authority and the AIDS Committee of the Ministry of Social Affairs and partner organizations for including people living with HIV in special vulnerable groups. Provide social protection and support good ideas that address the need for strategic and systematic linkages.
Mr. Sok Buntha continued that in today's workshop, the importance of responding to the stigma and human rights of people living with HIV and other affected people in the context of social protection and Disseminate to the members of the committee and partner organizations about the 4th comprehensive national strategy to fight HIV / AIDS 2015-2020.
Mr. Sok Buntha added that in this workshop, they also raised the topic of learning, understanding the experience of partner organizations and understanding the shortcomings in order to improve in providing services more effectively. There is also the implementation of the resolution issued by the decision of the National Authority for Combating AIDS in the past.
At the same time, Mr. Chhour Sopanha, Director of the Department of Social Welfare of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has paid special attention to the causes of HIV / AIDS victims and Other Vulnerable People have developed and implemented a number of strategic policies and plans aimed at preventing and caring for victims of HIV / AIDS.
In addition, Dr. Hor Bunleng, Representative of the National AIDS Authority, praised the Ministry of Social Affairs and all partner organizations for their cooperation and activities in helping and protecting HIV / AIDS victims. AIDS in the past.
