(Kampong Chhnang): At Kbal Teuk Secondary School, education and dissemination of road safety was organized on March 27, 2019. Kbal Teuk Secondary School is located in Krasaing Dod Leung Village, Kbal Teuk Commune, Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province, on National Road 53, which connects Kampong Chhnang City to National Road 44 in Kampong Speu Province.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Pech Heng, Coordinating Officer of Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Pea Kimvong, Road Safety Advisor, Principal, as well as about 250 teachers and students.
On that occasion, Mr. Pech Heng said, "Roads are not the cause of traffic accidents, but road users, which cause traffic accidents almost every day on the roads of Cambodia." He added that human factors have caused and caused many national accidents and accidents, as well as left many consequences for society and families.
At the same time, Kim Mean, principal of Kbal Tuek Secondary School, said that he now observes that traffic accidents kill people almost every day and he is concerned about the safety of young people going to and from school. Pedestrians use bicycles and some use motorcycles.
The principal of Kbal Teuk Secondary School stated that some students who live more than 15 kilometers away from the school are forced to buy a motorbike by their parents without even knowing how to use the motorbike and the road.
Mr. Pea Kim Vong also stated that the purpose of this education and dissemination is to organize education and dissemination on road traffic safety at this time in order to prevent and reduce road traffic accidents that are threatening your life. Use the road and hinder the development of the nation as well.
The road safety consultant added that the program will continue to educate people living along the road, including students at schools along the road.
Mr. Pea Kimvong urged all road users to pay attention to road traffic safety, especially to obey the law on road traffic at all times, such as speeding, driving after drinking alcohol and not respecting the right of way. And many more issues.
He said that although today he mentioned only two causes of accidents (speeding and the use of helmets), but asked you to find out more through the documents distributed as a skill. Life to the future.
On this occasion, also provided helmets, T-shirts and some study materials to students to learn, understand and encourage them to respect the law and show good behavior on the road.
