(Phnom Penh): The teaching profession is highly valued because this profession has helped train people to have knowledge and lead to a better future. Although this profession has contributed to providing knowledge and creating human resources for the society, some people say that being a teacher is not good.
This word has become a weapon to discourage teachers and also become a barrier for some people not to reach this profession. However, many new generations of young Cambodians continue to pursue a career as teachers.
What motivates the new generation of young Cambodians to continue their careers as teachers, even though they know that this career cannot make them as rich as other professions?
On Wednesday, March 27, 2019, a total of nearly 2,000 Cambodian student teachers received their degrees from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, after overcoming difficulties and obstacles for at least 17 years. That.
During the ceremony, the new generation of educators, young people, showed a happy face, almost everyone was happy with the graduation of a new career as a transmitter of knowledge to their next generation.
Cheng Pheary, a young smiling teacher, graduated from the National Institute of Education and taught at the New Generation School in Phnom Penh at the end of 2018. On the day of graduation, the 24-year-old teacher from Kirivong district, Takeo province, expressed her happiness as an achievement that came from her own efforts and strong support from her family.
According to Pheary, a daughter from a farming family, after graduating in 17 years to become a teacher, she faced many difficulties and obstacles. But the father's advice and encouragement, as well as seeing the example of his uncle, who was a scholar, helped Pheary overcome those difficulties and achieve her life goal.
During her studies, Pheary also heard the saying, "Being a teacher does not make you a better person or a richer person." But this one word did not become the pressure to stop trying to become her teacher. Pheary saw that the teaching profession could not be rich, but the profession made life dignified and contributed to society.
Not only satisfied with her teaching career, Ms. Pheary is also committed to transferring her skills to the next generation of Cambodian children to acquire a better knowledge of mathematics, which is a teacher's skill, and to educate them. The next generation of children to have a dignified morality in society and become a cell to help develop the nation.
Minister of Tourism Thong Khon: Request all stakeholders to promote the use of local products in the tourism industry
(Phnom Penh): Under the framework of the Trade Capacity Building Program in Tourism (TCBP), the Ministry of Tourism, the National Committee for Clean Cities Assessment, in collaboration with the French Agency for Development (AFD) and the United Nations Office for Industrial Development (UNIDO), Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, requested all stakeholders to help promote the use of local products in the tourism industry.
Mr. Thong Khon made this proposal on March 28, 2019, when he chaired a workshop on "Production value chain and increasing consumption of domestic products in tourism." »At the Green Palace Hotel, with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, sub-national administrations, the private sector in the tourism sector, local producers, development partners and national-international organizations.
At the same time, the private sector in the tourism sector must continue to support and use local products to the maximum, while local producers have been continuing to strengthen production in terms of both quantity and quality at competitive prices. Arranging "intermediaries" is also important in acting as a matchmaker between the supply and demand sectors, acting as a guarantor for both parties.
In this regard, promoting the consumption of domestic products in the tourism industry in response to the growing demand through the growth of international tourist arrivals and the growth of domestic tourist travel is of strategic importance, which requires Involvement of all stakeholders, public, private and development partners.
