Nearly 300 students at Sre Ampum Primary School and teachers receive study materials and funds from the Cambodian Scouts Association of Mondulkiri Province
(Mondulkiri): Students of Sre Ampum Primary School, Pichreada District, Mondulkiri Province, on March 28, 2019, Mondulkiri Women's Scout Association of Cambodia, led by Mrs. Yean Dina, wife of Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province and President of Scout Association. The Cambodian women from the province and the team brought study materials, school bags to give to 282 students and the budget.
Materials distributed to students at that time, from kindergarten to 6th grade, a total of 282 students, each received a backpack and a budget of 5,000 riels. Separately, 8 teachers each received 100,000 Riels.
