A former military officer has been remanded in custody by an investigating judge on charges of inciting soldiers to disobey, possessing or transporting weapons without permission, and inciting others to commit crimes.
(Siem Reap): A former military officer has been remanded in custody by an investigating judge on charges of inciting soldiers to disobey, possess or transport weapons without permission, and inciting them to commit crimes under articles of the Penal Code. The decision to detain the suspect was made on the afternoon of March 28, 2019.
According to Mr. Theng Samnang, this act is a crime to incite soldiers to disobey, possess or transport weapons without permission, and incite to commit crimes, especially at the mouth of the Siem Reap River. Located in the village / Sangkat and time as above is a criminal offense that is stated and punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 471, Article 490, Article 494, and Article 495 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
PRASAC held a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of two more library buildings
(Phnom Penh): PRASAC, the number one position in the microfinance sector and one of the five largest banks in Cambodia, held a groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of two additional library buildings in two different provinces this morning. March 27, 2019 In the mission to promote reading and education in Cambodia.
The two library buildings to be built are 7 meters x 90 meters in size:
1: Treng Trayeung Primary School is located in Village 4, Treng Trayeung Commune, Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province.
2: Banteay Neang Primary School is located in Banteay Neang Village, Banteay Neang Commune, Mongkul Borey District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The two library projects will start construction on March 28, 2019 and are scheduled to be completed in July 2019, which will allow students to use the library after the traditional New Year holidays. Our Khmer nation is coming.
It should also be noted that the PRASAC Library Project can be implemented with the close cooperation of the Curriculum Development Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, school principals, teachers and local authorities at all levels.
