Mr. Mal Reuy, Director of CMAC Central Workshop, said that each year, the workshop has the capacity to maintain and repair an average of about 400 vehicles of all kinds, about 250 machines of all kinds of mines and about 70 machines of all kinds. He said that in a year, a car or a demining machine can be maintained and repaired more than once.
It should be noted that the CMAC Central Workshop building was built in 2005 under a grant from the people and the Government of Japan in the 4th phase of the mine clearance improvement project. The construction of this workshop aims to increase the efficiency in the maintenance and repair of heavy demining equipment, vehicles of all kinds and demining equipment to support the demining operations and explosive remnants of war by CMAC throughout Cambodia.
According to a JICA report, from 1992 to 2018, Japan joined Cambodia in clearing more than 1,000 square kilometers of landmines and destroying a total of nearly 4 million mines of all kinds. Japan also contributed to reducing the number of mine casualties from more than 4,000 in 1996 to 58 in 2008.
According to Mol Reuy, CMAC Central Workshop needs to move mobile vehicles or demining equipment to the workshop to repair or send experts and equipment to the CMAC operation site.
