China promises to speed up construction of Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway ahead of schedule for Cambodia to host ASEAN Summit
Wen Gang made the remarks during a working meeting with Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, in Beijing on March 26, 2019.
The first expressway in Cambodia was officially opened for construction on March 22, 2019, presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The 190-kilometer road through Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Speu, Koh Kong and Sihanoukville is scheduled to take 48 months to complete in March 2023.
During the groundbreaking ceremony for the expressway, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that in 2022, Cambodia will host the ASEAN Summit and related meetings. Samdech also presented plans to take Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville for this meeting.
However, during the ceremony, Samdech Techo did not expect to use this expressway to serve the travel of the leaders and delegations of ASEAN member countries and relevant countries who came to the meeting in Cambodia. Road construction is planned until 2023. Samdech only expected to use this road to host the SEA Games.
But for now, the vice president of the Chinese Transport and Construction Corporation (CCCC) has pledged to push for the construction of the expressway in time for Cambodia to host the ASEAN Summit.
