Officers crack down on illegal vehicles across Kampong Speu province, public officials call on vehicle owners and company owners to respect the law
(Kampong Speu): The vehicle inspection team of Kampong Speu province, in cooperation with the vehicle inspection team of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on March 27, 2019, stopped 2 vehicles for inspection with a total length of 18. 60 meters, which the road traffic law stipulates that this type of car has a total length of only 16 meters.
Therefore, the two vehicles that are being stopped now need to cut the tail of the tuk tuk 2.06 meters long, leaving only a total length of 16 meters.
According to Mr. Chan Chhay Hong, Deputy Director of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, the vehicle inspection team stopped and cut the tail of the truck at the point on National Road No. 4, km 52 at In Preah Trapeang village, Sangkat Kandol Doum, Chbar Morn city, Kampong Speu province.
