(Battambang): A senior official of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport said that the construction of the 85-kilometer National Road No. 5 from Battambang to Serei Sophorn, Banteay Meanchey province, with the assistance of the Japanese government, has reached 41%. .
In addition to the rehabilitation and widening of this section of road, two inter-city roads are being built, including a 23.92-kilometer road between Battambang and 9.34 kilometers between Serei Sophorn. The road will cost 19.988 million Japanese yen (185 million US dollars). Construction of the road will take 36 months and is scheduled for completion in March 2020.
