On that precious occasion, Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, made five important recommendations to the leaders and officials at all levels of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to implement in order to achieve the education development policy.
The five recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen include:
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised the joint efforts and close cooperation of leaders and officials at all levels of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, professors, teachers, parents, students, communities and local authorities throughout the country. Contribute to the development of education and human resources with a sense of responsibility according to their respective roles and responsibilities.
Samdech highly appreciated the development partners of national and international organizations and all relevant institutions who cooperated and provided support in terms of materials, budget, action plan and support in the implementation of work activities in the field of education, youth and sports.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that the reform of the education sector will create an environment and hope to improve the quality of human resources and skills to supply the labor market by establishing a new generation of schools, improving the quality of learning. Teaching, capacity building, school management, curriculum updates and creating a good learning environment.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "The Royal Government will continue to allocate an additional annual budget to the education sector to recruit and train teachers, which is a top priority to supplement the work of teacher deployment and replacement of retired teachers." Teaching curriculum improvement, inspection, strengthening management capacity and exam quality.
Samdech Techo added that at the same time, the Royal Government will continue to consider raising salaries and incentives for teachers and academic staff, as well as efforts to mobilize resources from all walks of life to encourage the private sector to invest. In the field of education and vocational training.
The Prime Minister said that this is to ensure the stability of the labor market, improve productivity and livelihoods of the people with the delegation of power, transfer of functions, transfer of resources and technical sharing through decentralization and deconcentration mechanisms to units. Administration at all levels under the supervision of ministries and institutions.
Samdech Techo continued that strengthening the quality of education in Cambodia is a priority goal of the Royal Government set in the Rectangular Strategy for implementation at all stages: education, training, technical skills, science and technology, orientation for the labor market.
"Especially the strengthening of technical skills for young people to ensure that young people have at least one skill in life to improve family life better, contribute to social and economic development." This is an additional confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Please note that in 2019, the Royal Government will spend about 3,661,670.2 million riels for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, about 915.41 million US dollars.
The Royal Government pays the most salaries to teachers and doctors because these two sectors are a priority for the society. The current minimum salary of teachers (before April 2019) of 1,170,100 riels will increase to 1,200,100 riels from April 1, 2019.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2018 and the work direction of the new year 2019 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on the afternoon of March 27, 2019. This.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to ask for understanding from people from all walks of life about the shortage of electricity due to the unprecedented drought in Cambodia. At the same time, Samdech urged Thailand and Laos to supply electricity to Cambodia ahead of schedule and requested Vietnam to supply at least 50 to 100 megawatts more.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "We are working with Turkey, where tomorrow the Turkish Commission will come to negotiate in Phnom Penh, maybe we can avoid dragging a ship carrying black oil generators. Take Phnom Penh, about 200 megawatts more .. This is unfortunate for us because this year there is a severe drought, which makes our electricity shortage of about 400 megawatts.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen acknowledged that Cambodia had misjudged the amount of electricity used due to the drought and the high growth of the construction sector, which used electricity in the country beyond expectations.
"We need to add more electricity, but before this, we need to bring in Turkish ships for about three years and ask Vietnam, Thailand, Laos to help supply more with the investment that will be put in next week," he said. This with additional investment.
Samdech also continued that in the past, we did not dare to receive investment because for the electricity sector, if you invest, you have to buy them all at once.
Under Japanese aid, Battambang Referral Hospital building worth more than 11 million USD, 40% completed
(Battambang): Mr. Kak Seila, Director of Battambang Provincial Referral Hospital, said that as of now, the project to improve Battambang Provincial Referral Hospital has completed 40% of the construction process, while the construction team is working hard to achieve the plan.
The renovation of Battambang Provincial Referral Hospital is being carried out under the Official Development Fund (ODA) of the Government of Japan at a cost of more than 11 million US dollars.
Speaking to the media during the visit of journalists on ODA 2019 on March 27, 2019, Mr. Kak Seila confirmed that the construction of this building has started from January 2018 and so far the construction process. Achieved 40%. He said construction will also be completed in December 2019.
Please note that Battambang is the target province of the ODA Hospital Improvement Project, located in the northwest of Cambodia with a total area of 1,166 square kilometers and a population of over 1 million. Battambang is about 300 kilometers from Phnom Penh and is the second largest province in Cambodia.
