Minister of Agriculture urges authorities to take measures to prevent and suppress the import of animals, meat and forestry-fisheries crimes, especially the illegal import of pigs from neighboring countries
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on March 27, 2019, requested the authorities at all levels to take measures to prevent and suppress the timely import of animals and meat, forestry, fisheries and Illegal agricultural materials.
The request of the Minister of Agriculture was made on the occasion that he presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of 2018-2019 and the direction of implementation for 2019-2020, which was held at the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Tbong Khmum Province. This afternoon, March 27, 2019.
Mr. Veng Sakhon stated that "We must cooperate with the relevant departments and authorities at all levels to take measures to prevent and suppress the timely import of animals and meat, illegal forestry, fisheries and agricultural equipment, especially to prevent the illegal import of pigs. "Laws due to African swine fever are now spreading in neighboring countries."
The Minister added that it is necessary to strengthen internal unity, pay attention to perform duties in a responsible manner, and ensure high efficiency in accordance with the code of ethics and the general statute of civil servants. Must manage and maintain the state property to be good and must strengthen the efficiency of providing public services to the people.
He stressed the need to continue to strengthen the provision of training services and disseminate modern and appropriate agricultural techniques. Strengthen professional farming communities, turn farmers into agribusinesses, and work with the private sector to develop value-added production chains on key crops through the implementation of contract farming.
At the same time, he proposed to continue to increase agricultural productivity, diversification and trade in agriculture by shifting the focus from affluent development to intensive development to increase yields, ensure food security. Increase revenue and respond to market demand.
He stressed the need to continue to transfer modern technology suitable for rice, vegetables, animals, aquaculture, agricultural inputs in accordance with soil quality, crop type, water source and climate change. NagaWorld continues to plant seedlings to make Cambodia more beautiful!
(Kampot): In continuing the efforts to make Cambodia greener and more beautiful, the social team of NagaWorld Company or "NagaWorld Generous Heart" has joined the Ministry of Environment, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. And students to plant about 400 rare seedlings in some schools in Kampot province.
The Tree Planting Initiative is a NagaWorld Generous Social Responsibility Program after the "Environmental Awareness and Tree Planting" press conference held in December last year to help raise awareness. Raise the beauty of Cambodia to be more beautiful and raise awareness of the importance of the environment and nature.
Studies have shown that a large, leafy tree can produce enough oxygen for 10 people a year to breathe, as it can absorb up to 21 kilograms of carbon dioxide. Its shade also reduces the heat around, which can reduce the heat from two to three degrees.
"Therefore, planting new seedlings is very important that we can all do to improve the environment and the well-being of our students, teachers and community."
He said that since 2014, NagaWorld has planted more than 3,300 saplings throughout Cambodia, and through the Ministry of Environment's guidance on how to care for and conserve the environment, students will better understand the value of Conserve the environment. I urge you all to join us and make Cambodia greener and more beautiful! ”
Mr. Chiep Bun Eang, Director of the Department of Environmental Education of the Ministry of Environment, praised the program and encouraged the preservation of ecosystems and nature.
"We welcome this initiative to help mitigate the effects of climate change, which is one of the biggest problems the world is facing right now," he said. "Trees absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere and release oxygen, so trees are very important for our lives."
Heng Raksmey, Deputy Director of the Education, Youth and Sports Office of Kampong Trach District, also said that "providing natural shade in the school yard is something that the Ministry always encourages to create a better learning environment."
In addition, he said, tree roots absorb water and prevent soil erosion, which reduces flooding, causing schools to suspend operations and affect students' education.
"We support all initiatives that help improve the environment in our community," said Khim Samy, deputy governor of Kampong Trach district.
On the other hand, Mr. Nen Vuthy, Director of Koh Tromong Primary School, also said, "Thanks to NagaWorld, generous heart and all relevant ministries for supporting these rare seedlings to our school."
