According to Heng Piseth, director of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Tbong Khmum has the potential for agro-industrial crops on 177,453 hectares, covering almost two-thirds of the total cultivated area. Rubber, cassava, pepper, cashew, red corn are the priority crops in the province, cultivated on an area of 162743 hectares.
Apart from that, there are mixed crops such as beans, sesame, mango, banana, vegetables grown on an area of about 14,455 hectares, as well as local fruit trees such as turmeric, monsoon, rambutan, which is grown on an area of about 655 hectares. In particular, the area under rice cultivation in the rainy season and dry season is cultivated on an area of about 88,800 hectares.
