Ministry of Environment Spokesperson: Climate change is not just about deforestation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): While some people often say that deforestation is the cause of climate change Mr. Net Pheakdra, spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, replied that climate change is not just about deforestation, it is also due to natural factors.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment made the remarks at a press conference on "The Impact of Summer Climate Change and the Preventive Response to Public Health Care" organized by the Government Spokesperson's Unit. This conference was held at the Office of the Council of Ministers this morning, March 27, 2019.
Responding to a reporter's question, Mr. Neth Pheakdra said that climate change has two natural causes: First, climate change, when the earth rotates and the inner surface is warm, it increases the growth. Global warming and second: the increase in global warming.
"Of course, the impact of deforestation and deforestation is only a small part, but global warming is caused by household gas consumption," he said. "Various means and burning of fuel."
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said that some countries that are industrialized and used in large factories that emit smoke also cause climate change, so do not think that only one forest problem causes There is climate change.
"Climate change is on the rise, and even if we increase urban sprawl, it will also affect climate change," he said. He said that due to the need to build buildings and use other structures that cause overheating.
At the same time, Mr. Net Pheakdra stressed that "urbanization is also a factor in causing climate change, so we can not identify a problem from the forest, climate change is a factor. "Others that contribute to the impact of climate change."
