(Sihanoukville): The sewage canal flowing into the sea at Sokha Beach has been closed to the sea and instead pumped back to the treatment plant at Ochheuteal to filter out toxins before discharging into the sea.
The decision to close was made on March 26, 2019, after the third pumping station at this point was equipped with a pump.
Mr. Chiao Vicheak, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Chairman of the Drainage System Management Committee of O Canal canal, stated that the reason for the decision to close the drainage dam at Sokha Beach above to stop the sewage from the canal flowing into the pumping station. The third dirt to be pumped to the filter station in Ochheuteal, filtered and then discharged to the sea. Because the construction of the sewage pumping station has been completed and is being tested.
Mr. Chiao Vicheak emphasized that the main purpose of this work is to reduce the amount of wastewater that has flowed into the sea as much as possible to avoid affecting the beach and sea.
However, the Sihanoukville provincial administration expects that in the future the pollution problem in Sihanoukville will be resolved and it will no longer be a serious concern as it is today.
It should be noted that the establishment of liquid waste management system in Sihanoukville is considered by the Royal Government very carefully. The Cambodian Coastal Area Management and Development Committee (CCHR) was also established under the leadership of Mr. Chea Sophara, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Lands to help solve the problem of wastewater.
In fact, with the efforts and good cooperation of Sihanoukville Provincial Administration, eight wastewater pumping stations have been set up, while four stations have been completed and are being tested.
He said that the first station: at Ekareach Beach, the second: behind Sokha Beach Hotel, the third: at O Sam Ath and the station, the fourth: at Ochheuteal beach, all four stations have been built for four months. On March 25, 2019, the working group inspected the technical specifications and tested the pump successfully and planned to officially launch the pump on March 29, 2019 under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara.
The first pumping station is the second pumping station, the third pumping station is the third pumping station and the fourth pumping station is pumping down to the main mechanical filter tank in Ochheu 16 hectares. The Ministry of Public Works and Transport is preparing to increase the filtration capacity of the filter station from 5,700 cubic meters per day to 250,000 cubic meters per day.
