Senior official of the Ministry of Commerce: In 2018, Cambodia exported more than $ 33 million worth of goods to Indonesia
(Phnom Penh): At the opening ceremony of the Cambodia-Indonesia Business Forum 2019 on the afternoon of March 26, 2019, Mr. Chuon Dara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, said that in 2018, Cambodia's exports to Indonesia amounted to more than $ 33 million, an increase of 29% compared to 2017, which is more than 25 million US dollars.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Commerce added that Indonesia's exports in 2018 to Cambodia amounted to more than 525 million US dollars, an increase of 2% compared to 2017, which amounted to more than 513 million US dollars.
Mr. Chuon Dara also pointed out that in 2018, bilateral trade between Cambodia and Indonesia amounted to more than 558 million US dollars, an increase of 4% compared to 2017, which amounted to more than 558 million US dollars. More than $ 539 million.
