A: The Transport and Infrastructure Working Group is chaired by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, with 21 other members. .
G: The Working Group on Export Processing and Trade Facilitation Affairs is chaired by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Chou Vichith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy. Vice-Chairman and 22 other members.
H: The Working Group on Industrial Relations, chaired by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Chou Kim Leng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy 28 others.
The Energy and Mineral Resources Working Group is chaired by Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Chan Sovuth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture. 21 other members.
The Education Working Group is chaired by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Pich Sophoan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor, as the Vice-Chairman Other.
The Health Working Group is chaired by Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and has 17 other members.
The Construction and Real Estate Working Group is chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Mr. Tep Thorn, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management. Chairman and 21 other members.
