Beijing, Paris join hands again to build future for all
Chinese President Xi Jinping's visit marks the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and France. Therefore, both China and France emphasize that this visit has a special meaning. On the eve of his visit, Chinese President Xi Jinping said he had brought special affection to the French people and sowed new hopes for Sino-French cooperation.
In less than 24 hours, Xi Jinping met with the French President twice, reaching a consensus on building a strong and vibrant strategic partnership between China and France. Based on the starting point of a new history.
In 1964, France took the lead in establishing diplomatic relations with China's new government among Western powers. The two countries' international political views have much in common, which makes them a powerful impetus for the continuous development of Sino-French relations.
Xi Jinping stressed that the Chinese side is willing to work with the French side to make greater historical contributions to building a world of lasting peace, security, prosperity, openness, environment and beauty.
When the two heads of state met with journalists, Xi Jinping reinterpreted China's development ideas. "We are seeking happiness for the Chinese people, but we have never forgotten our international obligations," he said.
China's development is not just for personal gain, for example, the "One Belt and One Road" initiative is a peaceful, mutually beneficial and win-win development that all countries build together. Discuss and share the results with each other, and the ultimate goal is to create a harmonious coexistence of humanity, which is the core of Chinese civilization with a history of 5,000 years.
