After 22 months of investigation, US Special Prosecutor Robert Mueller has finally completed his report on the investigation into a major scandal involving Russia in the 2016 US election. The report does not find that Trump or any of his campaign members conspired with Russia to influence the outcome of the 2016 US presidential election.
The "Cambodian Young Entrepreneur" Award Program has started accepting applications!
The conditions of the competition are that the candidates must have:
* Ages 18 to 45 * The business was first established in Cambodia and has at least 51% owned by Cambodians * The business must be legally registered and have been operating for at least 2 years * The business must have At least 5 permanent staff * Entrepreneurs / businesses not involved with the selection committee and organizers * Not involved in any offenses * Women are encouraged to apply.
Please note that this is the fifth time that the Cambodian Young Entrepreneur Awards program has organized this competition. This program aims to recognize and encourage young Cambodian entrepreneurs to have the opportunity to demonstrate their abilities and share national success.
In particular, this year, the Cambodian Young Entrepreneur Awards will include a live tour of each of the entrepreneurial business locations in the semi-finals. In 2019, this program will provide an opportunity for entrepreneurs who have participated in the competition to present their business potential to the public, as well as the Committee of Entrepreneurs, Investors, Associations and so on.
It should be reminded that this competition also contributes greatly in promoting Cambodian entrepreneurs to have the courage and confidence to show their creativity, perseverance and success in running their business.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly Standing Committee Meeting on March 26, 2019, the National Assembly instructed the deputies and officials of its General Secretariat to visit their respective bases frequently to help solve the problem of drought. Such as the lack of water for the people. This is according to Mr. Leng Penglong, the spokesman of the National Assembly.
Mr. Leng Penglong said that the National Assembly also asked the people to be patient while the shortage of electricity is facing while the Royal Government is also finding ways and speeding up the solution for the people.
At the same time, the National Assembly urged people everywhere in the city and near the mountains to be very careful about fires that may occur this summer.
