National Assembly issues proclamation on the outcome of the March 26 meeting of the Standing Committee
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly issued a press release on the results of the meeting of the National Assembly Standing Committee on March 26, 2019, chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
The press release stated that the meeting discussed and approved a number of agendas, including:
1. The meeting approved the report on the activities of the National Assembly between the first and second sessions of the 6th legislature.
2. The meeting approved the composition of three secretaries of the second session of the National Assembly of the sixth legislature, including: Mr. Khuth Chandara, Mr. Khieu Phearith and Mr. Rofi Osman.
3: The meeting approved to set the date for the opening of the second session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature on the morning of April 1, 2019 with the following agenda:
Message from His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia to the Second Session of the National Assembly of the 6th Legislature.
* Report on the activities of the National Assembly between the first and second sessions of the 6th legislature.
* Election of Ms. Ly Vouch Leng as a member of the Constitutional Council for the term of 2019-2028.
Election of Mr. Prach Chan as Member of the Commission on Human Rights, Complaints, Investigations and Relations of the National Assembly, Senate and Election of Mr. Chan Sophal as Member of the Committee on Interior, National Defense and Public Function.
Kampong Cham Governor Encourages Provincial Health Department to Develop Strategy to Eliminate Patient Discrimination Using Equity Fund Cards
(Kampong Cham): At the Closing Ceremony of Kampong Cham Provincial Health Review Meeting 2018 and the 22nd Anniversary of 2019 on March 25, 2019, Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Mr. Kouch Chamroeun inspired the leadership of Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department to develop a strategy. To eliminate discrimination, patients use equity fund cards.
According to the Director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department, Mr. Kim Sour Phirun, a total of 740,078 people of both sexes used health services for medical examination and consultation in 2018. A total of 48,954 cases were hospitalized in public places throughout the province.
According to the Director of the Department of Health, the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) has signed agreements on the use and provision of health services at 98 public health facilities in Kampong Cham province, including one provincial hospital. Referral to 8 districts and 89 health centers. And a total of 22,668 females (20,960) came to be examined and treated using the services of the RPF in 2018.
The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, took this opportunity to highly evaluate the work of Kampong Cham Provincial Health Officials over the past year with patience and optimism.
Along with the successful results, the provincial authorities hope and believe that the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department will continue to strive to develop and improve the quality of work even better under the support and close cooperation with local authorities and partner units. Aims to truly improve in all areas, especially to continue to improve the quality of hospital services based on the principle of providing equitable services to the people.
At the same time, after the meeting was divided into groups with health officials and local authorities to discuss the challenges for a day, the meeting found 16 challenges to address. But out of the 16, the governor of Kampong Cham is interested in one of the challenges that there are cases of discrimination against patients who use the equity fund card.
And this point was raised by the provincial governor to find a solution to completely eliminate discrimination against patients from poor families in 2019. In that, the provincial governor inspired the leaders of the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department to pay attention and regularly monitor the health officers under his advice and find strategies to eliminate discrimination against patients from poor families.
However, in the detailed explanation from the provincial governor to the health officials and local authorities also fully applauded and agreed to change the behavior to eliminate discrimination against patients from poor families in This year 2019 as well.
China agrees to study plan to develop modern train system to reduce traffic congestion in Phnom Penh
The agreement was reached during a meeting between Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Zhou Keqin, vice chairman of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference (CPPCC). Chongqing on March 25, 2019 yesterday.
During the meeting, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol thanked Zhou for his visit to Cambodia in November 2018, which encouraged further cooperation and the exchange of the Cambodian delegation's visit to Chongqing.
The meeting also discussed the connection of the Southern Corridor between China, Chongqing, Singapore, Vietnam and Cambodia to strengthen friendly relations and cooperation in tourism, trade and investment between Cambodia and China. Regional countries.
Mr. Sun Chanthol expressed his appreciation and gratitude for the will and position in strengthening the friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and China, especially the relationship between Chongqing and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. The Senior Minister hopes that this relationship and cooperation will contribute to the development of transport infrastructure in Cambodia to another level.
It should be noted that Senior Minister Sun Chanthol has been leading a delegation from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to pay a six-day visit to China from March 23 to 28, 2019. The visit is aimed at seeking further cooperation in the field of transportation between Cambodia and China.
