(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has decided to charge a fee for passenger ferry services after the administration launched a fee-free operation for the past year. However, some people are not charged, ie follow the public bus service. This is according to the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration issued yesterday, which was received by the Information Unit this morning, March 26, 2019.
Please be informed that on April 6, 2018, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Phnom Penh Capital Hall announced the temporary operation of passenger ferries from Khan Prek Pnov - Phnom Penh - Takhmao City.
Inland passenger ferries from Prek Pnov district to Takhmao city, Kandal province, along the Tonle Sap and Tonle Bassac rivers, there are 6 ports and 2 ferries imported from Vietnam, and there are also 2 old ferries. In total, there are 4 units.
Locations for passenger ferries between Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, Kandal Province are under construction, including: Location 1: Prek Pnov Port, Location 2: Port in front of Russey Keo Gas Station or at Freedom Park, Location 3: Floating Port Opposite Night Market, Location 4: Naga Port near Koh Pich, Location 5: Doeum Chan Village Port in Chbar Ampov and Location 6: Takhmao Park Port.
