Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Opening Ceremony of Cambodia Vision 2019 Conference
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, March 26, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the 13th Cambodia Vision Conference. 2019. The conference was attended by about 350 local and regional leaders, experts, researchers, government officials, international development partners, the private sector and civil society.
The 13th Annual Cambodia Vision Conference is held under the theme "Digital Transformation to Industry 4.0", a partnership between the Institute for Training and Research for Development of Cambodia (CDRI) and Chi G Gear. The Cambodia Vision Conference was held at the Great Duke Hotel Phnom Penh (formerly InterContinental Hotel).
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this is the 13th time that Samdech has been invited to attend the Cambodia Vision Conference.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, emphasized that through the warm welcome with the clear message of artificial intelligence, Ms. Robo Sophia to me just now on "Digital Transformation to Industry 4.0" and "Cooperation The Close Partnership for Digital Transformation in Cambodia ”is a testament to the advancement of digital technology, which provides the following key benefits:
Along with the positive effects, digital technology also offers various disadvantages, including: Robots have been replacing human labor that will cause people to lose their jobs. Requires high level of skills to keep pace with advances in technology and information technology,
3: Inequality of benefits due to inequality of access to knowledge and technology, 4. Advances in digital technology will increase vulnerabilities caused by information technology-related crimes or offenses that undermine national security and social security.
* Samdech Techo stated that along with the advantages, but the development of digital systems also caused some disadvantages such as job loss and information technology crime.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that digital technology is currently popular all over the world, while the Cambodian economy is growing in all areas with high economic growth of up to 7.5 percent in 2018 through continuous growth. In all areas.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the structure of the Cambodian economy is changing from a country that relies on agriculture to a country that relies heavily on industry and services. Therefore, in order to take full advantage of the digital economy, Cambodia needs to make more efforts to promote high and strong economic growth in the long run.
* In order for the Fourth Industrial Revolution, which is the current of scientific and technological growth, to benefit the sustainable socio-economic development and environment, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the following initiatives and priorities:
Second. Encouraging investment in infrastructure: Continue to build backbone infrastructure such as fiber optic cables, submarine fiber optic cables, distribution and connectivity to homes and business locations and data centers to make the Internet faster and more cost-effective. Reasonable and accessible everywhere across the country.
Third. To maximize the benefits of the Fourth Industrial Revolution: The development of human capital is essential. At the same time, the Royal Government will continue to improve the quality of education, promote Stem Education (STEM), promote skills training and study, research and development.
* Samdech Techo stated that the Fourth Industrial Revolution, the current of scientific and technological progress, has been becoming an important catalyst for the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo expressed the hope that the 13th Cambodia Vision Conference will vigorously discuss the opportunities, challenges and solutions for joint solutions arising from the Fourth Industrial Revolution in the spirit of contributing to the socio-economic development of Cambodia. Present and future.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the CDRI Institute was initiated directly by Samdech, so no exchange was allowed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also criticized the liberal countries that recognize the context and problems of other countries, but why not recognize that Cambodia has its own situation and context.
