Ministry of Water Resources: From today to March 29, the monthly rainfall will drop, the temperature may rise to 37 degrees Celsius!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a statement on the weather in Cambodia, stating that from March 26 to 29, the effect of the intersection of low pressure (west and northwest) and high pressure in the region. Weakening of the plateau also causes the monthly rainfall to drop. Meanwhile, the heat will return to a maximum temperature of 34-37 degrees Celsius.
In particular, from March 30 to April 2, the effect of the combination of low pressure and high pressure continues to recur, causing a series of recurrent rains, which bring with it a thunderstorm. Lightning and wind twitching as well. The average temperature is 30 to 33 degrees Celsius.
