Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh: Cambodia welcomes exercises with other countries, but must check the sincerity
(Kampot): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, openly announced that Cambodia welcomes joint military exercises with all friendly countries, not only China, but Cambodia must examine the sincerity What is the purpose of the exercise and how does it respond to the work? Samdech continued that if it meets the actual needs, Cambodia welcomes all.
This statement was made by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh on March 25, 2019 during the closing ceremony of the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army at the actual shooting range of Techo Sen Training School. Chum Kiri of the 70th Brigade in Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province.
The Cambodian Defense Minister said: "This exercise is not only with the People's Republic of China, but whoever has a properly organized discussion and follow the principles set by the law, we will do it. "We have to check the goodwill and honesty of the training exercises for what, and whether it responds to the work or not. If there is a response to the needs, we welcome all, no matter who."
At the same time, Samdech continued that through the joint exercise between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army, which has already been three times, Samdech believes that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces of Cambodia has enough capacity to cooperate with other countries. Those wishing to conduct joint military exercises with the Cambodian Army as well. However, for military exercises, the conditions must be met in accordance with Cambodian law.
The Cambodian Minister of Defense added that Cambodia now has a committee to organize exercises with countries full of techniques, commanders, officers and sufficient forces, all of whom have undergone proper and competent training to respond to both tasks. Therefore, Cambodia has enough space to respond to all circumstances at the request of countries intending to hold joint military exercises.
Samdech Pich Sena also reiterated that the exercise between the Cambodian and Chinese armies is not a threat to any country, as some have suggested. Therefore, let the people and friendly countries do not be afraid, and this exercise is only to strengthen the friendship and build the capacity of the two armies to respond to any problems that may arise.
