(Ratanakkiri): On the afternoon of March 25, 2019, Major General Yin Chamnan, Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Commissioner, and Mr. Ma Vichet, Governor of O'Yadao District, announced the transfer of duties and ranks to National Police officers of the Border Police Battalion. Land No. 623 and O'Yadao District Police Inspectorate with 72 officers and 18 positions.
Also present at the ceremony were the Deputy Commissioner, the Chief of the Specialized Bureau, the Commander of the 623rd Border Guard Battalion, the Commander of the 2nd Border Guard Battalion and the O'Yadao District Police Inspector.
It should be noted that 20 police officers to be announced and promoted at this time are 20 O'Yadao District Police Inspectorate officers, from lieutenant colonel to lieutenant colonel and 6 officers.
As for the 523rd Border Guard Battalion, 52 officers have been promoted from lieutenant to lieutenant colonel and 12 positions have been announced.
