(Phnom Penh): After many years of interest and anticipation, the American University of Phnom Penh (AUPP) announced on Tuesday that from 2019 onwards, those who want to pursue a bachelor's degree High abroad, especially in the United States, do not need to spend more money, can come to study in Cambodia.
According to a recent press release, AUPP will offer Master's degrees in a number of majors, including Master of Business, Master of Finance, Master of Marketing, Master of Public Policy and Master of Law.
Professor Dr. Nial Farrell, Vice Chancellor for Curriculum and Student Affairs, said that a master's degree at AUPP could add more potential to students in the national and international labor market and self-employment.
Students or intellectuals who are busy with work and other business activities have the option of studying from Monday to Friday from 5:30 to 8:30 pm or only on Saturdays and Sundays.
Enrollment: August 23, 2019. Applications will be accepted from the date of this announcement.
