Minister of Women's Affairs: Cambodia has many positive achievements in women's participation
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of March 25, 2019, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, said that in Cambodia, there are many positive achievements in the participation of women in decision-making. Over the past two decades, the emergence of high-level political commitment and the implementation and implementation of many special measures.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi added that at the national level, there is an increase in the composition of women ministers, secretaries of state, undersecretaries of state and members of the National Assembly. In fact, compared to 1993 to 2018, the number of female National Assembly members increased from 5.8% to 20%, the number of female Secretaries of State increased from zero to 50, and the number of Undersecretaries of State increased from 2 to 67.
Another positive point is that in all capitals, provinces, municipalities, districts and Khans, there must be at least one female Deputy Governor (currently 17% of the Deputy Governors of the Capital and Provincial Governors and 26% of the Deputy Governors of the Board of Governors). Municipalities, districts, Khans are women.
"In these developments, we still have a number of areas that need to be further addressed in order to achieve gender equality in the executive and regulatory bodies in Cambodia," she said. Key challenges include: gender perspectives that need time to change, the level of confidence and empowerment of women in a male-dominated work environment, and the level of support from family members, communities, political parties, and the workplace. "
