Asian Injury Prevention Foundation Donates Helmets to High-Risk Students in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Asian Injury Prevention Foundation held a handover ceremony of helmets to about 96 students at O Primary School in Sangvei Commune, Chi Kreng District, Siem Reap Province.
The event also taught students and discussed with parents and guardians the importance of adhering to road traffic laws and traffic safety rules at all times. This effort comes at a crucial time for road safety work in Cambodia, the upcoming traditional Khmer New Year celebrations, where traffic accidents are generally high. .
He compared traffic accidents involving motorcyclists (including children) who were not wearing helmets to the flames that were or could take the lives of people on the road, especially children, which is a valuable asset of each family and The future of bamboo shoots is where these dangers occur due to our own negligence or inattention to safety measures.
Therefore, in order to protect the valuable assets of the Cambodian society and family, he requested the school management, parents or guardians, students and local authorities to use the (water source) nearby (traffic safety rules) to put out this catastrophic fire. Effective and prompt, without expecting only measures to be taken by the authorities or civil society / private sector at the national or provincial level.
In this regard, he suggested that parents or guardians of students should set a good example and remind their children to adhere to safety behavior when traveling, especially when going to school and to buy / give Have your children wear helmets every time they travel on a motorcycle, whether near or far.
In particular, the school management and teachers must educate and disseminate to students through the curriculum and frequently, as well as examine the possibility of mobilizing the private sector in their communes and districts to provide support for traffic safety activities, especially the provision of Helmets for students traveling on motorcycles and bicycles.
If necessary, the school can discuss with the commune authorities to ask for support from the local relief team in their commune to examine the possibility of mobilizing resources to support traffic safety activities, especially the provision of helmets for all students. To protect vital resources in the families of citizens and communities for which this task force is responsible for supporting local development.
"We are proud to be able to share this message and announce the launch of helmet activities for children," he added. "This event is made possible by the generous participation of the local motorcyclist community and our partnership with the Asian Injury Prevention Foundation."
At the same time, Mr. Say Set, Principal of O Village Primary School, said that the donation of helmets and traffic safety education to students at this time is very important to protect students from serious head injuries that can lead to Died in a car accident.
"We are committed to working with parents, guardians and stakeholders to make helmet wear a necessity for students as they travel to school," he added.
Please note that O Village Primary School was selected for the donation of helmets, this school is located along National Road 6, is one of the national roads with a high number of accidents per Years. Last school year, there were at least three traffic accidents involving students at this primary school.
