Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin urges the Ministry of Education to continue its efforts to recruit children and youth for education or short-term skills training
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Binh Chin, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister and Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, on March 25, 2019, requested the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to continue its efforts to mobilize children and youth to receive education or training services. Short skills, equitable and non-discriminatory.
The request of Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin was made on the occasion of his participation in opening the conference to review the work of education, youth and sports for the 2017-2018 academic year and to raise the work direction for 2018-2019 at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia (Techno) on the morning of the 25th. This March 2019. This conference is held for 3 days from today to March 27, 2019.
"The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports should continue to mobilize school-age children, over-school-aged children and drop-out and out-of-school children to receive educational services or short-term skills training," said Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin. "Equity and non-discrimination, especially the training of skills in accordance with the policy, a young person has at least one skill in life."
The Deputy Prime Minister added that the physical education and sports sector should continue to work hard to set up stadiums and improve the implementation of physical education and sports training programs in educational institutions and promote sports competitions for students and public sports more widely and effectively. Regular.
At the same time, it should focus on the good preparation of national players in regional and world competitions, and especially the 2023 SEA Games, which Cambodia will host. This was further confirmed by Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, said that the three-day education conference will focus on the implementation of education, youth and sports reform strategies to participate in the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy Phase II. 4 of the Royal Government of the National Assembly. The topics at the national level focus on:
* School management * Improving the quality, quality of education and implementation measures * Teaching methods in a new context * Transforming a community learning center into a lifelong learning center or lifelong learning center * A young person with at least one skill Life * Sports to the 2023 SEA Games * A young man has at least one sport in his life.
