(Preah Sihanouk): Police in Preah Sihanouk province said that a fire broke out in two Chinese shops located around the Old Theater in Sangkat 2, Sihanoukville, but did not cause any casualties in the afternoon. March 25, 2019 caused damage to the shop and damage to some equipment.
Immediately after the incident, the specialized police force sent fire trucks to intervene to prevent the fire from spreading to other houses or shops.
According to the fire brigade, the fire that broke out in the two shops was caused by an electric current from the generator that the owner started when the state power outage.
Starting from this issue, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin called on people, both Cambodians and foreigners living in Sihanoukville to be careful about fires or flames that could ignite at any time, because this season is summer. There is dry weather and frequent blackouts.
In addition, we would like to remind people who have generators to be careful regularly and to monitor all the ignition of their generators, because it can spill gasoline or oil, which can cause a fire eventually occur. Kampong Cham Deputy Commissioner of Criminal Affairs chaired a meeting to strengthen measures to prevent and suppress criminal offenses in their locality
