44 Families Affected by Typhoon in Rovieng District Receive CRC and Sous Yara Deputies
(Preah Vihear): The humanitarian donation of the Cambodian Red Cross and the gift of Mr. Sous Yara, Member of Parliament of Preah Vihear Constituency, was handed over to 44 families affected by the strong wind and damaged their houses in Romdos Commune, Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province on the afternoon of March 25, 2019.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Chairman of Rovieng District Working Group, Mr. Hor Bun Hour, Rovieng District Governor and many others.
On that occasion, Mr. Peng Trida brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as a message from Mr. Sous Yara and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Honorary President of the Branch. Cambodian Red Cross for the victims of this natural disaster.
Mr. Peng Trida added that these days, natural disasters and windstorms have occurred almost all over the district in Preah Vihear province, and other provinces have also suffered from this natural disaster. At the same time, he would like to express his condolences to the people affected by this tragic incident. He said that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister, no people are allowed to live in isolation.
In fact, today he brought humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross and Mr. Sous Yara to hand over to the families of 44 families affected by natural disasters in Romdos commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
