Cambodia - A Japanese organization agrees to draft a new agreement to regulate and protect the interests of Cambodian workers working in Japan
(Tokyo-Japan): The Cambodian Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has agreed with Japan's JITCO to draft a new cooperation agreement in accordance with the new law on "skilled workers" who go to work in Japan to ensure the management and Protecting the interests of Cambodian workers in accordance with the laws of both countries.
The agreement was reached during a meeting between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and a representative of JITCO on March 25, 2019 in Tokyo, Japan.
This discussion focuses on past cooperation with Cambodian interns who are doing internships and working in Japan and with regard to the Law on "Skilled Workers" who go to work in Japan through the dissemination of laws and procedures. To agents in both Japan and Cambodia.
