Parents of Samdech Techo Scholarship Students Express their Excitement After Successful Graduation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The parents of Oum Bunthoeun expressed their happiness after their hard work, dedication and overcoming obstacles Until he achieved a satisfactory achievement, his son successfully graduated with a bachelor's degree and received a degree in person from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Oum Bunthoeun is one of more than 1,000 other students from Phnom Penh International University (PPIU) who have successfully completed their studies. The graduation ceremony was held under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on March 25, 2019.
Oum Bunthoeun is one of the outstanding students in the university and he also received the opportunity to receive a degree in person from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
After overcoming thousands of difficulties and obstacles, from the first grade to the graduation of the bachelor's degree, graduation day is a wish and anticipation for every student. Receiving a degree is a joy for every student, but Bun Thoeun's joy is even greater when he receives a scholarship from Samdech Techo to study and finally receives a degree in person from Samdech Techo.
Graduation is a happy thing for Oum Bunthoeun, but Bunthoeun's parents are even happier. They are very happy because their desire to see the light of life through knowledge has come true.
After graduating from this bachelor's degree, Bun Thoeun is committed to using his skills to work to build a better future and support his family in return for his parents' efforts.
The student also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for providing him with a scholarship to study and gain higher knowledge as the light of life. He also promised to take the knowledge and skills born from this study to contribute to the development of a better society. 89 pigs illegally imported from Vietnam fined 25 million riel
(Svay Rieng): While Vietnam is spreading a deadly disease called "African swine fever", many pigs were seen being transported by truck along the border in Svay Rieng province. In fact, on March 22, 2019, a total of 146 pigs were arrested by the Svay Rieng Provincial Police for irregularities.
After the arrest, the police handed over to the Production and Veterinary Officer of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to handle the procedure. Of those, 89 pigs were fined 25 million riel for illegally transporting pigs, while the blood test results did not show the virus.
Mr. Thach Ratana further stated that officials fined 55 CPs 15 million riel and 34 trucks carrying 10 pigs fined 10 million riel.
"But if the Ministry imposes more fines, we will call for more fines and make the right contract. First, do not drive in the wrong direction, and second, require CP cars to wear the right number plates, and third, do not transport pigs. No more than the number of cars that buy pigs without a clear source, buy a motorcycle suspected of buying Vietnamese pigs to make a contract.
In addition, Mr. Thach Ratana pointed out that officials also seized 250 kilograms of chicken and pork in the corridor of Kampong Spean, Bavet City on the morning of March 25.
To date, African swine fever has spread to 20 countries, and according to the World Health Organization, the virus has not been vaccinated. In Vietnam, many provinces, especially from central to northern areas, including Hanoi, have been hit by a series of outbreaks, prompting many countries to temporarily suspend pig imports from Vietnam.
