Press and Quick Reaction Unit of the Office of the Council of Ministers opens a training course on fake news
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 25, 2019, at the Office of the Council of Ministers, a vocational training course on fake news was organized under the chairmanship of Mr. Svay Sitha, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Press and Quick Reaction Unit, with participants About 100 people from ministries, national institutions and provincial capitals.
This 5-day training course is conducted by foreign trainers with many years of experience. The purpose of this training is to share experiences and additional knowledge to the leaders from the ministries, institutions, capitals and provinces in charge of information and public opinion to understand the false information, as well as strategies, tactics and other methods to implement the work of Be professional and efficient.
Mr. Svay Sitha also noted that the false information that occurred was the strategy and methods of some groups with the purpose and plan to paint, causing social unrest or in order to create a color revolution.
He also suggested that in order to continue to better manage the public, and especially to participate in the protection of peace, independence and national sovereignty, all ministries and institutions must strive to prevent pollution by false information and must Act proactively as a firefighter or suppressor of false information as quickly as possible.
