(Phnom Penh): In the meeting to review the work of education, youth and sports for the 2017-2018 school year and to raise the work direction for 2018-2019, this morning, March 25, 2019, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports confirmed Cambodia currently has nearly 15,000 public and private kindergartens and general education schools.
This morning's opening ceremony was presided over by Dr. Binh Chin, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, with the participation of leaders of the Ministry of Education at all levels and stakeholders at the Institute. Cambodian Technology (Techno). This conference is held for 3 days from today to March 27, 2019.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron stated, "As a result, across the country, we have a total of 14,522 kindergartens and general education schools, both public and private, including: 4,810 kindergartens, 7,716 secondary schools. 1,324 high schools and 672 high schools.
The Minister of Education added that as of September 2018, the construction of school buildings donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, a total of 4,310 buildings, equal to 26,538 rooms.
The Minister continued that through the campaign to collect children to school age, the construction of school buildings, the provision of teachers, the provision of funds to run schools, the provision of scholarships to students from poor families, especially female students, etc. have created conditions for children to be able to More to get an education.
Currently, 63.1% of 5-year-old children attend pre-school education, 63.6% of girls. The actual enrollment rate in public and private primary schools is 98.0 percent (98.5 percent females) in the standard and similar to other countries in the region. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron.
