Labor Minister Asks Japan to Recruit More Cambodian Apprentices and Provide Training in Accordance with Japanese Labor Market
The talks took place on March 25, 2019, during the visit of Prime Minister Ith Sam Heng to the Cambodian delegation in Tokyo, Japan.
On that occasion, Mr. SUZUKI informed that this organization has many branches throughout Japan to provide support, counseling and support services to Cambodian trainees who are doing internships and working in Japan and prepare new forms for recruiting trainees from Other countries in accordance with the law.
The President of the Japanese Organization informed about the progress of the cooperation in the past and asked for further cooperation in order to provide legal protection, especially the provision of real skills to They can do business both in Japan and in Cambodia.
Minister Ith Sam Heng requested to further strengthen the good cooperation between the two countries and to support the training and recruitment of more Cambodian trainees to Japan and to assist the Ministry in preparing various procedures in accordance with the procedures. Of the new law and provide technical assistance on the training of technical skills to Cambodian trainees in accordance with the needs of the labor market in Japan.
He also asked the organization to help disseminate and guide the Association of Workers from Cambodia to know the new procedures in accordance with the laws of Japan and to visit Cambodia in the future to have the opportunity to discuss these work. Even better.
Russey Keo District Governor Launches Phnom Penh Capital Hall's Joint Plan for Officials to Implement During Khmer New Year
(Phnom Penh): In the meeting of the Board of Governors of Russey Keo District Administration this morning, March 25, 2019, Mr. Chea Pisey, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presented a joint plan, which is the core work of the Capital Hall. Phnom Penh for officials to have the capital to continue to perform their duties effectively during the upcoming Khmer New Year.
He said that the main plans include: First: Scheduling a weekly meeting for the Board of Governors every Friday, Second: Paying attention to public order, Third: Monitoring all clubs. On drug prevention, 4th: Focus on the preparation of water tanks for fire prevention may occur from now until the upcoming Khmer New Year.
