(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province, accompanied by Mr. Hem Rithy, Deputy Governor and Mr. Sun Yi, Governor of Pailin City, this morning, March 25, 2019, led a working group and local authorities to visit and bring Emergency donations to support 11 families affected by typhoon in O'Breus Village, Sangkat Otavao, Pailin City, Pailin Province.
Mr. Phan Chanthul said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, has made the country peaceful and has built infrastructure development in all areas, as well as taking into account the well-being of the people throughout the country. By not allowing any citizen to die of starvation unknowingly and unresolved.
The provincial governor continued that, in fact, the visit and distribution of emergency gifts to the victims at this time is to encourage and contribute to solve your difficulties to some extent, even if these gifts are not fulfilled. According to your needs, it can also be solved to some extent, so all of you have to work hard to earn a living and grow agricultural products to improve your family's livelihood.
On that occasion, Mr. Phan Chanthul also instructed all citizens to be very careful about personal safety and family, as this season has rain mixed with wind and thunder, which is dangerous and if you have Any problems should be reported to the local authorities that are close to you so that the team can help you quickly and in a timely manner.
Please note that the victims who received donations from the provincial authorities were 11 families, each family received: 50 kg of rice, 1 noodle, fish sauce and 1 soy sauce, 1 sarong and 1 rubber tent.
Residents criticize Sihanoukville administration and KSWM for poor waste management
(Preah Sihanouk): Most people and traders living in downtown Sihanoukville criticized the Sihanoukville Municipal Administration Authority for not being able to manage waste properly and asked the authorities to encourage investment companies to collect garbage. KSWM to increase its garbage collection activities regularly.
Residents say that the inactive problems caused by waste management in Sihanoukville have continued unabated in recent years. Residents of Sihanoukville say that every day they have many problems in their lives, such as the delay of the garbage collection company KSWM walking to collect garbage regularly.
Residents say that KSWM, which has been awarded the right to invest in garbage collection in this tourist city, does not seem to be responsible for its work properly according to the contract and always causes consequences for people. Citizens claim that the company collects rubbish irregularly, leaving the rubbish piled up on the sidewalks for a long time and stinking.
Starting from this issue, the people living in Sihanoukville requested Mr. I Sok Leng, Governor of Sihanoukville and Mr. Yon Min, Provincial Governor, to encourage and expedite KSWM to increase the collection activities. Dispose of it in front of people's houses along public roads as soon as possible, because the garbage accumulated for a long time creates a strong odor.
Responding to the garbage problem, the Sihanoukville administration official wrote a message posted on social media or the Telegram system of the municipal administration that in response to the public's claim that recently there has been a lot of congested garbage almost everywhere in Sihanoukville. The municipal authorities are not indifferent to this.
Sihanoukville city administration officials explained that the case of garbage congestion in the subsequent garbage collection company KSWM claimed that due to the company is facing a crisis, lack of manpower or lack of workers. Some of the workers of this company also asked for leave to go to the district during the approaching rice season. Some workers have asked to leave the company to be transferred to work for other companies.
Sihanoukville administration officials explained on behalf of KSWM that every day recruiting garbage workers to work is the most difficult to find, while the labor market in Sihanoukville today has a wide range of job options and salaries or labor costs. High.
However, KSWM representatives said that they are looking for more workers from other provinces to fill the gaps, and the company has a policy to increase subsidies for workers to collect garbage and increase technical capacity for workers. Can improve the garbage collection process in Sihanoukville in the future.
In addition, Sihanoukville City Administration officials also informed the people that in case of garbage, congestion or long-term storage at any location for a long time, it is possible to contact the local commune hall where they live to To intervene to collect the garbage. Currently, KSWM has divided the garbage trucks to the garbage collection station in each commune.
