More than 300 students from Cambodian specialized universities attended a panel discussion on "The Role of Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) in Economic Development." The keynote speakers, who are experienced in research, management, direct leadership on small and medium enterprises, explained and elaborated on the role of SMEs in national economic development and the Royal Government's focus on Develop SMEs as well.
Senior Minister Son Kunthor, accompanied by the Prime Minister, spoke about the implementation of the Royal Government's policy to promote the development of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. The Senior Minister highlighted the Royal Government's efforts to develop a policy to open the door for people to have the opportunity to create small and medium enterprises by reducing the loan interest rate of 1.5 per month or 18% per annum. Original.
Dr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Universities of Cambodia, shared his experience with students about the "role of small and medium enterprises in the national economy."
At the same time, the development of small and medium enterprises depends on the owners of small and medium enterprises know how to unite, such as students from universities, cooperating to open SMEs or organize a community to open SMEs. In the same way, you have to study, research, learn and work hard to get results.
Mr. Sok Kheng also highlighted the challenges of the business and micro-enterprise parliament, such as financial and human resources issues. Also presented the management structure, leadership and vision of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry to contribute to the development of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. Small and medium enterprise owners can become members of the Business Council and micro-enterprises can also enjoy some benefits.
Dr. Ma Bun Sengbithy, Director of the Small and Medium Enterprise Research Institute, presented four different case studies in Thailand, South Korea, China, and Taiwan to present to students as a basis for research and comparison of important roles. Of small and medium enterprises to participate in economic development.
He also mentioned the effectiveness of management of small and medium enterprises, found that it is related to a number of factors such as business planning factors, personnel factors, management factors, human resources factors, use factors, technology, economic factors and support factors. From the Royal Government.
After the speaker gave a presentation, shared and explained many questions to the students, Dr. Steng Sokhom also instructed all students to study hard, research and cooperate after graduation at the university to initiate the idea of starting a business or As a community as a community to participate in building the family economy, community economy and national socio-economy.
It should be noted that so far, more than 20,000 students have graduated from CUS from associate degree to doctorate and nearly 20,000 are studying. CUS currently has eight locations, two in Phnom Penh and six in Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Kampot.
10,000 cases of Cambodian pure water have already been distributed to people in Traing district, Takeo province!
