(Prey Veng): During a meeting with about 500 people from 8 villages in Boeung Preah commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province on March 24, Mr. Prum Sokha, Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group, said that Cambodians support democracy. Realistic, peaceful like today.
Mr. Prum Sokha thanked for the efforts of the people and local authorities to maintain security, order and improve the development of the village-commune to progress steadily, actively contribute to the success of the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy. Fourth, the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group clearly emphasized that our society has evolved and changed rapidly in all areas as today, depending on our country is full of peace, people have real rights and freedoms, especially the right to choose their representatives. Through elections to contribute to the building of democratic institutions within the framework of the rule of law in accordance with the situation and reality of Cambodia.
In short, after overthrowing the genocidal regime and ending the civil war more than 40 years ago, the CPP has been at the core of the unity of the people at all levels and in all walks of life. All obstacles, difficulties, trials to push the Cambodian nation on the path of democracy to a future full of pride and hope.
In this regard, the Chairman of the Working Group emphasized that "unrealistic democracy that is not associated with the rule of law and which is inconsistent with the reality of Cambodia is just a rhetoric full of imagination. Extremist politicians use it as an excuse to deceive the public to lure people to support the illegal movement to serve their political ambitions.
The current reality shows that all their stubborn actions violate the law by inciting propaganda, inciting the people against the current government and attempting to overthrow the legitimate government that emerged from the election. Anything other than pushing the nation to fall again into the abyss of catastrophe as in the past.
However, given our past experiences of war and genocide, we strongly believe that Cambodians across the country continue to support the CPP in support of a peaceful, realistic democracy. BREAKING NEWS: Polling stations in Thailand close at 5:00 p.m.
