In 2007, the parties to be dissolved for opposing the rule of democracy with the King as the head of state were:
Thai Rak Thai Party, Phat Tha Na Chat Thai, Phen Din Thai. Then, in 2008, the parties that were dissolved for election corruption were: Phlang Prachachon, Chad Thai, Mach Chim, Mathip Pattai, and in 2019, just two months before the election, the Thai Rakshasat party was dissolved. For opposing the regime in a democracy with the King as the head of state.
