After realizing the mistake, the principal, Leng Sarin, and his wife came to his house and asked for a compromise to end the 1 million riel, but he refused and came for the second time, offering $ 400. In agony, he filed a complaint at the flagpole for legal assistance to his daughter.
Mr. Seng Sothy, Deputy Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Koh Kong Province, confirmed that he had received information about this case. He will appoint a review and research committee on Monday earlier this week.
He added that the use of violence against students in both public and private schools has been eliminated by the Royal Government, as the director violated the Ministry of Education's code of conduct and internal regulations and measures. By issuing a warning letter or suspending the process.
Legal Awareness: Unions
(Phnom Penh): In the field of labor, workers and employers are the main actors who have a working relationship with each other and receive their respective benefits. Of course, in the labor relationship between workers and employers all have rights and obligations to each other, but if one party violates the rights and duties as well as the interests of the other party, the problem Risks will occur.
To better understand the legal awareness program of Fresh News in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, please bring the topic of "union" to the people and students as follows:
According to Article 4 of the Law on Trade Unions, a union is a professional organization that refers to the union formed by workers in groups, by union and voluntarily, to cooperate, act or develop legislation. Personal to achieve specific goals or objectives of the profession. In the sense of this law, the professional organization of workers is called "union".
The labor law also states that all workers, regardless of age, gender, nationality, are free to join the trade union of their choice. Union members are free to choose their representatives as well as to determine their work. They have the right to define their own statutes as well as set separate administrative provisions that are legal and not contrary to the provisions of the law in force or contrary to public order.
The structure of unions in the Kingdom of Cambodia is divided into three (three):
Local unions are unions formed by workers in that local enterprise or establishment with at least 10 (ten) members. A trade union federation is made up of at least seven (seven) registered local unions. A union or trade union confederation is formed by a union of at least five (five) registered unions.
In order to obtain legal status as a legal entity in accordance with the law, the union must be registered in accordance with the law of the Kingdom of Cambodia. When a law recognizes a union as legitimate, it also creates rights and obligations for that union.
In general, in order for a union to function well, the members of that union always organize the election of the manager and the person in charge of the administration of that union. In addition, the law also gives all union members the right to stand as candidates for election.
Unions can represent their workers to communicate with employers. Unions have duties such as honest negotiations with employers in order to seek a specific agreement between workers and employers, focusing on working conditions, hygiene, job security and other benefits.
In general, unions are legal entities that have a role to play in representing workers in negotiations with employers to find solutions to challenges that arise in relation to working conditions, as well as to reach an agreement between workers and Employers, too.
