There are reports of 4 thieves kidnapping people in Pichreada district, Mondulkiri province, leading the police to launch an operation to help crack down, but in reality, the wife hid the money for fear of her husband stealing and drinking
(Mondulkiri): Many police forces in Mondulkiri province immediately launched an operation to interrogate and intervene in the crackdown after receiving information that four thieves wearing masks almost went to kidnap people in the district. Pichrada to rob property.
After receiving this information and until the information was sent directly from the Governor of Mondulkiri Province, Mr. Svay Sam Eang immediately ordered the Provincial Police Commissioner to launch an immediate operation to crack down on the thieves in order to strengthen security for the people in a tourist province. This.
But after the local police interrogated and researched carefully, they found out that in fact, there was no group of thieves who hijacked the people's property, starting from a woman who hid the money. Fearing that her husband would steal it and drink it, she made up the story that there was a case of robbery.
Mondulkiri Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Lor Sokha told Fresh News this morning, March 24, 2019, after receiving information and direct orders from Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, he ordered Specialist and local police arrived at the scene immediately to investigate and investigate the case.
Immediately after the investigation, the Major General confirmed that there was no case of kidnapping, the reason was because the wife hid the money and was afraid her husband would steal it to drink alcohol until the fabricated information was created.
