Rotary is a regional entity established in accordance with Rotary International Charter, which aims to provide social services and promote trade relations. Each member features a different business, with weekly meetings at specific times and places (but at least twice a month).
Each regional rotary is an independent executive body, but must be requested and authorized by an international rotary to be established. The rotary of each region is usually named after the region or city in which it is located. The first Rotary in the world was founded on February 23, 1905 in Chicago, Illinois, with Paul Harry as its founder.
