Hot weather: People should not raise the price of generators too much (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Due to the dry season in Cambodia in 2019, the hot weather has made the dam can not produce power. Enough leads to a shortage of energy in Cambodia. That is why the government has called on people to use temporary generators until about two months after the summer.
After the government's announcement, we observed that many people rushed to buy generators. According to the activities at the machine shop, it is now as busy as a fish market. Just by looking at it for a moment, we see that many generators are being shipped from warehouses, both small and large.
Sao Prohm Sophoan, an employee of Leap JDP, said that after receiving information from the government about a temporary power shortage, he bought several generators for his company's work in the construction sector. Almost unbelievably, his company's standard generators are sold out.
Out of necessity, Mr. Sophoan said he would order from the warehouse owner, even if he had to make a reservation in advance. As for the price of the generator, the staff of the drug company said that the price of the generator is much higher than before.
Mr. Davuth said: "Let the price of sales be taken into account, not to mention the high demand, he raised the price too much to make a reasonable profit, not just at the same time make it difficult for people to buy each other. "Too much, especially at this stage requires a lot of oil or diesel, if possible, the price is still reasonable, it is better not to increase the price, still acceptable, but please do not seize the opportunity to increase the price of oil."
Of course, it is usually during the immediate aftermath of such a demand that there is always an unusual price increase. But raising prices too much is hurting people's minds, according to Chheng Khun, a resident of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Chheng Khun stated: "Normally, when the sale is over, there are some shortages according to the reality, because it looks like our brothers and sisters come to buy a lot, so the sellers can run out of stock. . "And I also call in the past, we see that there have been opportunists at this time, he knows how to increase the price, so let all the sellers consider the standard price, we sell not to sell wrong."
The increase in the price of the generator is not only mentioned by the people, even the seller of the generator himself acknowledges that there is a price increase. Due to the urgent needs of the people, despite the increase in prices, the generators have to be sold out. This was confirmed by Mr. Ing Bun Mao, the owner of a generator wholesale warehouse near the Chroy Changva bridge. Mr. Ing Bun Mao confirmed this: "Generators these days are selling very well."
In addition to calling for an increase in electricity prices, people are also aware of the power shortage. Apparently, as Mr. Chheng Khun said, this lack of energy is caused by the hot weather, a reason that can not be known long ago.
Chheng Khun added: “His government has taken this action, it is good that the people have been informed in advance. Such as buying a generator to use this temporary to solve the necessary work. "And I also thank the government for notifying me in advance so that it can be easily prepared."
In connection with the power shortage, Samdech Techo Prime Minister had explained on March 18 that the power outage was caused by overheating, which made the hydropower unusable, leading to a shortage of up to 400 megawatts of power. Forced power outages in some areas, but the lack of electricity has not yet affected the production line in factories, because Cambodia still has more than 1,000 megawatts of electricity.
On the other hand, Cambodia faces a shortage of electricity due to higher demand, such as in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville, which previously used only more than 20 megawatts, but now need more than 100 megawatts. In fact, the construction sector increased by more than 700% compared to January and February last year. This is where Cambodia has more electricity consumption, which is different from the previous government's forecast.
