Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture Organizes 2018 General Assembly of Meanchey Agricultural Community Union and Announces Transfer of Duties of Deputy Chiefs of Forestry Administration
(Preah Vihear): The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province on March 22, 2019 organized the 2018 General Assembly of Meanchey Agricultural Community Union and announced the transfer of duties of Provincial Forestry Administration officials from Sangkat Forestry Administration to Chief. Deputy of the Forestry Administration.
According to Peng Trida, there are currently a total of 43 farming communities in Preah Vihear province, coordinated by the Agricultural Community Development Office and registered as legal agricultural communities by the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
He said that in 2018, the agricultural community across the province has a total of 9,285 members, in which the main business of the agricultural community focuses on credit, cash supply, agricultural equipment, sharing services, distribution of clean water and rice and organic cassava market. .
He said that in addition to the organic rice production community, eight of the organic rice production communities have signed contracts to produce and supply organic cassava to agricultural community corporations. This is due to the favorable conditions for many farmers in Preah Vihear province to grow crops without using fertilizers and other chemicals, especially rice and cassava, making it easier to apply organic crops.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear also thanked the development partners, both local and non-government, who have been partners and supported the Union of Agricultural Communities in the past, such as Amru Rice, Signetch Company, Asia International, Volunteer Organization. Of Yamakata (IVY), Agricultural and Veterinary Organization Without Borders ... etc.
In particular, the Forestry Administration officials to be announced today, including the Deputy Chief of Forestry Administration and Sangkat Chief of Forestry Administration, must work hard to perform their duties well in order to prevent natural resource crimes. Effective.
