The confirmation of the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia was shown in a 60-second video where the Japanese Ambassador talked about the completion of the repair of the Chroy Changvar Bridge and the temporary opening before the traditional Khmer New Year, posted on the official Facebook Page Of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia on March 23, 2019.
"The repair of the bridge did not cause any accidents," said Hidehisa Horinochi. The bridge will be opened on April 3, 2019, our repair team using the latest Japanese technology.
Recently, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport announced that the Cambodia-Japan Friendship Bridge, or Chroy Changvar I Bridge, is scheduled to reopen on April 3, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director. Minister of Cambodia.
The Cambodia-Japan Friendship Bridge, 971 meters long and 13 meters wide, located along National Road 6A in Phnom Penh, was built and inaugurated in 1963 with a grant from Japan.
Due to the age of the bridge, and as economic growth and traffic flow have steadily increased, the bridge needs to be repaired urgently at a cost of about 30 million US dollars under a grant from the Japanese government.
The renovation process started on September 15, 2017, so far, the work to restore and repair the bridge has reached 97 percent.
Joint Police in Svay Rieng Province Detained 3 Trucks Transporting 146 Pigs Suspected of Illegal Pigs Imported from Vietnam
(Svay Rieng): Coalition forces cracked down on and detained 3 trucks transporting pigs, a total of 146 pigs, which are suspected of importing pigs across the border from Vietnam.
After the arrest, the police handed over to the Production and Veterinary Officer of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to handle the procedure.
According to the local police officer of Ang Prasre commune, the crackdown was carried out because a group of corrupt traders brought pigs from Vietnam across the border into the administration of Ang Prasre commune, Romeas Hek district, transported them by motorbike and then built tuk-tuks. And the number of trucks per night is from 30 to 35 tuk-tuks per 10 units, and if those vehicles can transport back to 35 to 40 piglets.
Meanwhile, a man said that he and other people were hired to transport pigs for traders from the Vietnamese border to a truck for 10,000 riel.
He added that the 104 CP pigs were transported from CP farm in Tbong Khmum province, where only 90 pigs were transported, more than 14 were illegally transported and suspected of importing pigs imported from Vietnam. 25 in Prey Veng and 20 in Kandal.
However, on the morning of March 23, 2019, professional officers pumped all the pigs' blood to be tested at the Phnom Penh Laboratory, and if the results are found to be diseased, they will be destroyed and if there is no disease, they will be fined accordingly. The law will be returned to the owner.
