(Sihanoukville): Authorities in Sihanoukville have arrested two people suspected of masterminding nearly 30 people to illegally encroach on state forest land in the Sihanoukville National Park (Ream). In Sihanoukville to own.
The two masterminds of land grabbing were arrested by the authorities in violation of the Law on the Protection of Natural Areas on the afternoon of March 23, 2019 and sent to the Sihanoukville Provincial Police to build a case. The case was sent to a court of law.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra also appealed to the public who are trying to buy land in the Ream National Park area to be careful because buying and selling land in the protected area is illegal and the perpetrators will face legal action. .
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment emphasized that no one has the right to sell state land and issue a title deed to any person. "If you continue to buy and sell land in the protected area under the deception of crooks, you may lose money if the authorities find that the land is in the national park."
He said that in the past, in cases of crackdowns or denial of ownership, traders had incited protests and sometimes came to protest in Phnom Penh, and were voiced by some civil society groups working as human rights activists. Violation of human rights and housing rights. In fact, this is clearly a violation of the law.
In order to prevent land encroachment in protected areas, the Ministry of Environment, in collaboration with the relevant ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations, shall take strict measures to prevent and suppress all the above-mentioned illegal activities based on legal procedures. Effective.
At the same time, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Net Pheaktra, emphasized that using citizens as an excuse to encroach on state land is illegal and will not be tolerated.
(Siem Reap): In response to the request of the people and students, a 3-kilometer stretch of red gravel road in Poeng Chhat village, Khun Ream commune, Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province has been repaired and officially inaugurated. And in the presence of Mrs. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, President of the Water Well Foundation, Mr. Hun Neang on March 23, 2019.
