Ministry of Environment warns of legal action against individuals buying and selling land in Ream National Park after some individuals announced the illegal sale of land in the area
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has announced and urged the people who have been occupying and selling land in the area of Sihanoukville National Park (Ream), Sihanoukville Province to immediately stop this illegal activity. The Ministry of Environment warns that anyone who continues to buy and sell land in the national park will face legal action.
This is the warning of a senior official of the Ministry of Environment on March 23, 2019, as some crooks have been announcing the sale of new plots of land illegally located in the area of Ream National Park, which is under Management, protection and conservation of the Ministry of Environment.
Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment Neth Pheaktra also called on the public who are trying to buy land in the Ream National Park area to be careful because buying and selling land in protected areas is illegal. Violators will be able to face the law. He stressed that no one has the right to take state land to sell and issue titles to any person.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that if some individuals continue to buy and sell land in the protected area under the fraud of the crooks, it may cause a waste of money if the authorities find that the land is. In the national park area.
The Secretary of State said that the perpetrators of illegal encroachment on state land as well as land grabbing on private property in Sihanoukville have been arrested and charged pending trial. For offenses committed against the law on protected areas, natural areas and illegal encroachment on land and land laws.
He said that in the past, in cases of crackdowns or denial of ownership, traders had incited protests and sometimes protests in Phnom Penh, and were voiced by some civil society groups working as human rights activists. Violations of human and housing rights. In fact, this is clearly a violation of the law.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra also called on all people to participate in the protection and conservation of natural resources that Cambodia has to save for future generations. He added that if people really lack land, please apply for social land concessions from the authorities should not encroach on the illegal occupation of state land.
Army officers and authorities bring money and food to support the poor for the ninth time without money
(Kratie): Lieutenant Colonel Sos Hussein, Deputy Chief of Army Inspection, cooperated with village authorities and Orussey commune chief to bring financial support to poor fishing families living in huts when their midwives could not afford to live in Sre Sdao village. Sangkat Orussey, Kratie City, on the afternoon of March 22, 2019.
Mr. Sos Hussein said that the donation was made through the village authorities, who told him that the poor family had no money to give birth and that he had donated 300,000 Riels and 1 kg of rice, 50 kg of fish sauce, 1 can of soy sauce. Yub Bi Cheng half to help alleviate his difficulties.
He added that this is not the first time that money has been donated to the poor when his wife gave birth in Orussey commune. He has been helping nine families for some time now. In that, one family received 300,000 Riels equally, and these funds are his own budget, and he continues to support poor families when giving birth without money.
According to the arrangement of the midwife who did not have the money to solve the problem that her husband is currently fishing and this season, fishing is not enough, she went to work in exchange for a little money to raise children. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Tax found more than 700 cars without paying road tax in 2018 with a fine of more than 700 million riels
(Preah Sihanouk): The head of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Tax Branch, Mr. Sorn Siphal, said on Saturday afternoon that the provincial tax officials have been cooperating with the joint police force to set up checkpoints on public roads since February. As of March 23, 2019, more than 700 vehicles have not been found to have paid the road tax for 2018.
He said that for the cars not taxed above, tax officials require car owners to pay the 2018 road tax again and required to pay a fine of one hundred percent in accordance with the tax law.
In this regard, Mr. Sorn Sophal stated that for cars that do not pay the 2018 road tax, the owners of those vehicles will lose double the tax, that is, they will have to pay double tax because they will have to pay a fine. He said that the budget collected from the fines for duty-free vehicles in 2018, more than 700 vehicles above, collected 376 million riels in taxes and 376 million riels in fines.
The official warned that people who own all kinds of vehicles will not be able to avoid the obligation to pay road tax, because the tax officials in the capital and provinces across the country will put checkpoints on the means of your vehicle. On public roads without exception.
In addition, when the tax authorities find that your vehicle does not meet the road tax obligation, you will be fined twice, which will result in a loss of time and a greater fine. Therefore, every citizen must not avoid going to fulfill the obligation to pay road tax each year.
