Phnom Penh Customs and Excise Officers Raid a Car Garage in Por Sen Chey District and Seize 15 Vehicles
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Customs and Excise Department this week cordoned off a large garage and car dealership in Por Sen Chey district, seizing 15 left-hand drive vehicles, three of which were 100 percent installed and one with license plates. Fake, while the other 12 units are installed and connected.
Phnom Penh Customs and Excise Branch calls on garages that take parts or spare parts to be used as tourist cars and garages that use parts to be illegally installed as right-hand drive vehicles to stop their activities immediately.
President of French animal feed company: This year, Cambodian pig farmers are happy with the high price of pigs
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Gaten Morisor, President of Breast Feed Company, claims that this year, pig farmers in Cambodia are very happy because the price of pigs has risen to 10,500 riel per kilogram.
This statement was made by Mr. Gaten Morris on the occasion of his participation in the annual party to thank the representative of the feed company Presence on the night of March 22, 2019.
According to Gaten Morrisor, the increase in farm prices this year has prompted farmers to start buying high-quality feed to maximize yields and profits. Leading in customer service.
He added that the company sells Presan feed, which ranks fourth in the pig feed market.
He added that Presence has been in Cambodia for more than a year. Sales for 2018 are expected to increase by 75%, and the company hopes that Presence's feed sales will continue to increase.
He added that although Cambodia now has to import pork or chicken from neighboring countries, the company continues to believe that the sale of animal feed in Cambodia is successful and growing.
He added that the increase in sales of Presence was due to the efforts of the company staff as well as distributors throughout Cambodia and the trust in customers' Presence feed.
He said that today, to thank the distributors who work hard to sell, the company has organized an annual party with the participation of 400 distributors.
Please note that Presan feed is the feed of Neoviyang, which has recently become part of ADM Feed, a company that supplies a wide range of animal feed.
Summer has arrived! Coca-Cola installs new water treatment tower in Kampong Cham to meet this need
"Coca-Cola is proud to have contributed to the development of this important project, which is bringing clean water to schools and communities around the world," said Outh Chandy.
Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, emphasized that the presence of this water filter tower is very important and provides benefits for students, teachers and people in the whole Prey Chhor district, especially in the summer of this year. Climate change (extreme heat) and high water demand.
Coca-Cola says six more water treatment towers will be installed across Cambodia in 2019, with more to come in the coming years.
The Cambodian Coca-Cola Beverage Company said that the 15 water treatment towers that the company has installed in Cambodia since 2016 provided 44,990,286 liters of clean water to more than 40,000 communities. This figure is expected to double this year with the installation of seven more water treatment towers in 2019.
Plant more than 10,000 mangrove trees into sewers in Sihanoukville to reduce odors
(Preah Sihanouk): Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Nen Chamroeun, said that three ministries have cooperated to plant about 15,000 mangrove trees into a canal or stream in the commune. No. 4, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
He said that the purpose of planting mangroves into the sewer above to reduce toxins or reduce the odor emitted from the sewer after the Sihanoukville Provincial Administrative Authority. Machinery came to pick up the garbage that had been clogged from the stream recently.
At this point, Mr. Nen Chamroeun confirmed that the mangrove planting activities followed the instructions of the leaders of three ministries, including: Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Mr. Veng Sakhon. The Minister of Agriculture and Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province.
The director of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Agriculture said that the planting of mangrove seedlings into the sewage canal through the town of Sihanoukville began working on Friday, March 22, 2019 yesterday. He said that for the large-scale mangrove planting ceremony with the participation of the representatives of the Ministry of Land Management, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture will take place on March 30, 2019.
The canal or stream where the relevant officials are planting curves every day is located behind the Sihanoukville Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters in Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville.
Mr. Nen Chamroeun believes that when more than 10,000 mangrove trees have been planted and the mangroves grow, it is likely that the canal will have a cleaner and more beautiful environment. In particular, it is likely to reduce the odor to some extent.
