Eight Khmer National Heritage Sites Featured on Vital Pure Water Case
(Phnom Penh): To promote Cambodia's eight World Heritage Sites officially inscribed on UNESCO Vital, it has designed its new packaging to highlight eight Cambodian heritage sites, especially to celebrate the traditional New Year. The upcoming Khmer.
This new case style is new and unique like never before in Cambodia, as the eight heritage properties are incorporated into the beautiful Vital case.
Vital also displays information about the name of the heritage property and the date of the official registration date on the bottle label, highlighting the beauty full of pride.
Mr. Chun Heang Thav Sithy, Commercial Manager of NVC Corporation Vital, said that the packaging design of the World Heritage Site that Cambodia has acquired is based on three main objectives, including: Raise national pride during the traditional New Year 2. Disseminate knowledge about the world heritage of Cambodia 3. Participate in the care and conservation of Cambodia's rare heritage.
It should be noted that the eight Khmer heritage properties that have been highlighted on Vital packaging are:
Royal Ballet: Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, registered on November 7, 2003.
* Temple of Preah Vihear: World Heritage List, registered on July 7, 2007.
* Big Skin Shadow Theater: Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, registered on November 25, 2015.
Draw game: Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, registered on December 2, 2015.
* Chapey Dang Veng: Intangible Cultural Heritage Needs Urgent Registration on November 30, 2016.
* Sambor Prei Kuk Temple Area: World Heritage List, registered on July 8, 2017.
* Svay Andet Pagoda Puppet Theater: Intangible Cultural Heritage Needs Urgent Registration on November 28, 2018.
