National Police calls on private security agencies to protect the scene before local authorities arrive
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the National Police General Commission, called on all private security agencies stationed at all targets to participate in protecting the crime scene. Well before the local authority or professional authorities go down to the scene.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey at the Closing Ceremony of the 13th Private Security Agency Training Course on the evening of March 22, 2019, stated that the scene is very important and good protection of the scene leads to convenience To the competent authorities to research or collect various exhibits to identify the perpetrators and to crack down on all the perpetrators.
The director of the Department of Private Security Management stated that the private security agency is an auxiliary force to the National Police Force and a guardian of security, safety and order on the spot with the people, so if the private security agency has a clear profession, it will improve. Participate in better security.
The director of the department encourages all private security agencies to report to the local authorities all crimes that occur in the targets they are guarding and all information will be kept confidential and provided. Incentives as well.
