Chief of Samdech Techo Sen Lawyers, Mr. Ky Tech, led a working group to meet with the Minister of Women's Affairs to find ways to help women in prison
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ky Tech, Chairman of the Bar Association of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of March 22, 2019, led a group of lawyers to meet with Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs to discuss solutions to help women. Who is being held in prison.
Ky Tech's lawyer confirmed to Fresh News that the discussion was in line with the Prime Minister's recommendation that the lawyers and relevant ministries meet to find a solution to the problem of women incarcerated in prisons. Especially women, minors, women with small children, women who are pregnant in prison.
During the meeting, the Minister agreed to the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's lawyers and promised to urge all Women's Affairs Departments to widely disseminate Samdech Techo Hun Sen's lawyers to help women in need who have been abused. Legally.
