Tuol Khpos High School Students in Kampong Chhnang Province Receive Education and Dissemination on Road Safety Before Khmer New Year
(Kampong Chhnang): Students of Tuol Khpos High School in Kampong Chhnang province receive education and promotion on road safety before the Khmer New Year. The ceremony was held at Tuol Khpos High School on March 22, 2019.
The event was attended by Mr. Ou Sereyvuth, Officer of Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Pea Kimvong, Road Safety Advisor, Mr. Khlot Sophon, Officer of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, and teachers. More than 500 teachers and students, including about 300 women, participated.
Toul Khpos High School is located on National Road 53, which connects Kampong Chhnang to Kampong Speu. . Tuol Khpos High School has a total of more than 800 students and all students use bicycles, motorbikes and pedestrians to come to school every day.
Mr. Ou Sereyvuth said that traffic accidents are a concern of the Royal Government of Cambodia, traffic accidents have caused many deaths, injuries, disabilities and damage to equipment, and among the deaths due to traffic accidents in 2018, nearly 2. , 000 due to traffic accidents.
He said that seeing this problem, the Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is really concerned about the safety of road users after the road is improved, especially during the upcoming Khmer New Year, which people will use. This road will increase, which is why the number of road accidents will also increase.
In particular, the main causes of accidents are human factors, which account for up to 95%, including speeding, driving after drinking, overtaking in a dangerous situation, turning left-right carelessly. Respect the right of way and disregard for vehicle technical issues. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Ou Sereyvuth.
Seeing these challenges, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, through the Road Construction Unit (MPU3), conducted road safety education and dissemination to people living along the project road.
This program will continue until before the traditional Khmer New Year, during each New Year, the number of accidents as well as the number of deaths has increased dramatically. At the end of the course, participants will be provided with T-shirts and helmets for the safety of motorcyclists, as the number of motorcycle fatalities is now alarmingly high.
On that occasion, Mr. Pea Kim Vong, Advisor of the Road Traffic Safety Program, also stated the purpose of this education and dissemination that the organization of education and dissemination on road safety at this time is in order to prevent and reduce Road accidents that are threatening the lives of road users and hindering the nation's development.
He added that the program will continue to educate people living along the road, including students studying at schools along the road.
At the same time, Mr. Pea Kimvong urged all road users to pay attention to road traffic safety, especially respect for the law on road traffic at all times, especially speeding, driving after drinking alcohol and respect Priority rights.
Mr. Chung Muth, Principal of Tuol Kpoch High School, also said that he always reminded his children and grandchildren about traffic safety, especially when leaving school and traveling on the road, must pay attention to obey the road traffic law because there are currently traffic accidents. Roads threaten and kill many
He said that today's participation, he was very happy and have more understanding on road traffic safety, he will continue to promote to those who do not participate and encourage them to adhere to traffic laws for their safety.
