(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Customs and Excise Authority said on March 23, 2019 that the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Customs and Excise Branch cooperated with the provincial police and military police to seize three duty-free vehicles. Recently kept at the Customs and Excise to continue the legal process.
At present, the three duty-free vehicles have been stored at the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Office so that the owners of these vehicles can come and solve or fill in the tax payment form in accordance with the tax law and fines.
Please be reminded that on March 21, 2019, at the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Department, a press conference was held to present 13 luxury cars, which are tax evading vehicles, and were circulated in Sihanoukville Province by customs officials. And the provincial revenue.
Speaking to the media, Mr. Tum No, Head of the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Department, confirmed that the luxury cars seized by the customs officers were both left-hand drive and right-hand drive, and that the customs officials cooperated with the relevant authorities. Others capture and save to continue the legal process.
Mr. Tum No said that for left-hand drive vehicles, professional officers have given the opportunity to the owners of those cars to come in and fill out tax forms and fines in accordance with the tax law. However, right-hand drive vehicles are to be confiscated as state property without being returned to their owners. He said right-hand drive vehicles have been banned from importing since 2016.
Mr. Tum No, President of Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Department, said that from the end of 2018 to March 23, 2019, the Customs and Excise officials of this province seized luxury cars to evade taxes or not pay total taxes. 30 units for a fine.
Mr. Tum Nou pledged that under the direct guidance of the leadership of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and under the guidance of the leadership of the Sihanoukville Unity Command on the suppression of all kinds of tax evasion, especially cars. Tax evaders are officials of the Sihanoukville Customs and Excise Department.
Mr. Tum Nou emphasized that he will continue to lead customs and excise officials in cooperation with other authorities to continue this activity regularly and effectively in order to collect more national budget revenue in the years. Upcoming.
