(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Dry Port Control Officer in cooperation with the Department of Commerce, Deum Kor Market Commission and some stalls in Toul Kork district this morning, March 22, 2019, inspected goods and researched to prevent defective goods. Which some crooks steal to sell and distribute on the market.
Mr. Kong Vuthy, Deputy Director of Camcontrol Dry Port Branch in Phnom Penh, said that during the operation, the experts took 32 food samples and tested them in the mobile laboratory to find banned chemicals on goods such as all kinds of vegetables, yellow noodles, etc. Noodles, meatballs, beef, meatballs, pork, pickles, cucumber, squid, shrimp, dried fish, fish, sausage, etc. As a result, there are no banned chemicals.
