(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his strong hope that all relevant ministries, institutions, private sector, national and international organizations, development partners and citizens will continue to contribute to the promotion of disease eradication. TB in the cause not only contributes to the well-being of the people, but also to the dignity, excellence and prestige of Cambodia.
"I sincerely hope that all ministries, institutions, stakeholders, the private sector, national and international organizations, development partners and all citizens will continue to contribute and support the promotion of TB eradication in Cambodia," the statement said. "The cause not only contributes to the well-being of the people, but also to the dignity, excellence and prestige of Cambodia."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his belief that Cambodia will continue to move forward on a stronger, broader and more autonomous basis and would like to dedicate the content and meaning of the World TB Day on March 24. 2019 under the theme "It is time to end TB together" has become a reality so that the Kingdom of Cambodia can move towards a brighter future and a TB-free territory.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech thanked all stakeholders, both domestic and foreign, including officials, health workers across the country and all people who have contributed to the success of TB control in the past. And once again, I would like to express my full support for the fight against tuberculosis in Cambodia as well as around the world.
