(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has found an increase in cases of hand, foot and mouth disease in children under 5 years of age and some severe cases that require hospitalization for children during the emergency period. The heat rises.
The Ministry of Health has presented measures to prevent this disease, such as:
Practice good hygiene and get your child to the doctor on time if the symptoms are severe.
* Wash your child's hands often and often with water and soap or alcohol, especially after touching blisters or sores, before preparing food, before eating, before feeding the baby, or after using the toilet and after changing the baby's diaper. Or wipe the child's body clean.
* Avoid touching the hall (kissing, hugging, eating together) with children with blisters on the hands, feet and mouth can also reduce the infection. Provide children with nutritious food and clean water. Separate dishes for each child.
Meanwhile, the Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, called on people to be very careful about blisters on the hands, feet and mouth when the weather is very hot by maintaining good hygiene and washing hands often. Give soap and water frequently to both the child and the caregiver. If the child or infant has danger signs such as drowsiness, seizures or convulsions or respiratory symptoms (fatigue), rush to the nearest hospital.
