After questioning three witnesses and an independent forensic expert, Mr. Horm Mengse, Deputy President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, as the President of the Trial Chamber, decided to adjourn the hearing in the morning of May 1, 2019. Ahead.
The victim, Chev Sovathana, was found hanged in her bedroom in a large rented house rented by Mr. Lay Vannak in Phsar Ta Kor village, Rokar commune, Daun Keo city, Takeo province on the evening of the 26th. January 2018 ago.
The Chinese Deputy Foreign Minister made the remarks at the groundbreaking ceremony for the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, Cambodia's first expressway, on March 22, 2019.
At the ceremony, the Chinese Deputy Foreign Minister stressed that Chinese investment and assistance in Cambodia is not a trap, and stressed that in order to maintain good relations between Cambodia and China, the Chinese government will continue to support investment and Provide assistance to Cambodia to the best of its ability.
"Some malicious groups have turned black on Chinese investment as a trap. In fact, it has always won protests over baseless Chinese investment, not Chinese investment," he said. The trap is not only a threat, but it is a sincere help, a driving force for Cambodia's development capacity and an act that brings benefits to Cambodia.
Significant Chinese investment in Cambodia has been repeatedly attacked by Sam Rainsy, the head of the National Salvation Movement, and some former leaders of the former CNRP. Pro-opposition analysts have criticized China's credit and aid as plunging Cambodia deeper into China's trap.
The Chinese Deputy Foreign Minister said that as a good neighbor, good friend, good partner and good brother, China attaches great importance to developing relations with Cambodia and continues to stand with respect. Mutual and equal communication for the common good deepens political trust, strengthens mutually beneficial cooperation for mutual benefit.
At the same time, he stressed that the Chinese side will continue to respect the sovereignty and independence of Cambodia as before and support Cambodia on the path of development that is appropriate to its actual situation. The Chinese side will provide as much assistance as possible for economic development and improving the living conditions of the Cambodian people.
