Badminton adds two leaders to boost development ahead of SEA Games-2023
(Phnom Penh): The Badminton Federation of Cambodia has announced two leaders to promote the development of the sport and ensure the journey to host the 2023 SEA Games, in which Mr. Sok Pang received support as an executive member. Newly replaced by Mr. Steng Chea, who announced his resignation, and Mr. Oknha Im Phan Sophal were announced as senior advisers to the federation.
The announcement of the composition of the leadership was made at the General Assembly to review the work of 2018 and the direction of 2019 of the Federation at the headquarters of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia on March 21, with the participation of Lt. Gen. Ly Kosal, President of the Boxing Federation. Cambodia will also be witnessed by Mr. Prum Bunyi, Advisor to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Mr. Ly Kosal said that through the presence of new executive members and senior advisors, it is an important factor in contributing to the development and organization of various events more successful to refine sports resources. The best athletes are ready to participate in international competitions, especially the journey to the 2023 SEA Games in Cambodia.
In addition, the president of the federation focused on two important points to increase attention in 2019 and the next three years. Ability to compete on the international stage. In this regard, the federation is also committed to organizing competitions to promote high-level competition.
Second, Sports for the Disabled was requested by Mr. Ly Kosal to all stakeholders, starting from the Federation of Associations and Clubs to find resources for disabled athletes to train to become a professional sport to be ready to compete on the international stage. The sport has a high probability of competing for medals. Therefore, he suggested and encouraged people with disabilities to participate in sports according to their ability.
Last year's achievements were highly praised by the President of the Federation after the Badminton Federation of Cambodia achieved a large number of results, which resulted in an increase in both technology and resources. Especially in 2018, Cambodian badminton has emerged on the international stage after Vat Vanthon won a gold medal in the multi-national team event of the 3rd Youth Olympic Games in Argentina.
