(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pich Keo Mony, Governor of Meanchey District, visited the fire victims in Prek Toal 1 Village, Sangkat Steung Map Chey 2, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh on March 22, 2019. Mr. Touch Sam Ol, Second Deputy Chief of Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, and Ms. Teav Thida, Vice President of the Women's Association of Khan Meanchey and First Vice President of Sangkat Stung Meanchey II.
On that occasion, Mr. Pich Keo Mony brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to visit the affected people with compassion and express their condolences for the house fire that destroyed the shelter and property. Of the affected people.
At the same time, Mr. Pich Keo Mony brought the call from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all people to be careful about electricity, gas tank or stove that can cause fire as in the above case as well as disaster. Nature caused by climate change.
At the same time, Mr. Pich Keo Mony would like to encourage all the affected people to continue to earn a living, strengthen their spirit and strength to restore their family life and maintain hygiene in order to avoid any disease.
On that occasion, Mr. Pich Keo Mony and his team brought donations from the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Meanchey district to the 51 affected families, each family received 30 kg of rice, 1 lamp, 1 gas stove, 1 box of noodles. 10 cans of fish, kit (mosquito net, blanket, sarong, krama), 2 packages, 1 tent and some budget.
