(Phnom Penh): 100 million Riel of Carabao energy drink continued to fall into the hands of a young man named Tuy An, 19 years old, currently working as a brick kiln worker around Prek Anchanh and his hometown in Mesor village, Prek Koy commune, Kang Meas district Kampong Cham Province.
In front of the team representing the company to hand over 100 million Riels to the house located in the above geographical location, Mr. Tuy An described that today in terms of family living standards is difficult. Strong because my father is also sick and he has no job other than working as a bricklayer.
He added that especially for winning the grand prize from Carabao energy drink company now is also the most coincidental, because from the beginning, he never thought he would be lucky to win the prize from No carabao, even though there have been frequent winners on television.
But last week, after taking a break from work and returning home, feeling tired, he went to buy a can of Carabao energy drink near his house to eat. Riel on canned earrings. Immediately tell the seller and call the company immediately.
Tuy An stated that after receiving the grand prize of 100 million riels, he will use some to treat his father's illness and build a suitable house, and leave some for the establishment of a family business in the future.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng orders the police to crack down on drugs in casinos and clubs (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, believes that in some casinos and clubs may There are more or less drug crimes, so the relevant authorities must pay more attention to cracking down on drugs in all areas.
On the afternoon of March 21, 2019, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng confirmed that the most drug-prone areas may be in Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province. Poipet, Osmach or any other place with a casino.
In order for this operation to be successful, the Chief of the Ministry of Interior has instructed all officials to be honest with the profession and not to come into contact with drugs.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also stressed that the second target after the casino area and the entertainment club is in a number of rural areas that are facing this problem, and if it is found that there are drug offenses, it must be addressed immediately. ⁇.
In addition, the third goal that must be strictly prevented is the drug entering the school, and the drug control committee of each existing school must continue its activities. This is an additional emphasis of Prince Sar Kheng.
According to the report of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, in 2018, a total of 8,002 drug crimes were cracked down on, with 16,216 people arrested and more than half of the drugs involved. Tons.
Please be informed that this year 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has set out seven important measures to be implemented in the fourth anti-illegal drug campaign for one year from January 1 to December 31, 2019. This is according to the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's plan, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of March 21, 2019.
US to spend $ 21 million on Prey Lang conservation in Cambodia
The new project was confirmed during a meeting between Minister Veng Sakhon and Dr. San Ily, Director of Food Safety and Environment Project, Mr. Matthew Ed Vussen, Director of Prey Lang Baitong Project and colleagues on March 21, 2019.
The new project is called "Climate Change Status, Hydrology, Ecosystems, Production Chains and Livelihoods of the People, as well as the capacity of relevant institutions to adapt to climate change in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary."
Dr. San Ely confirmed to the Minister of Agriculture that he will lead the Prey Lang Baitong Project Research Team to inspect and assess the overall situation of the area in order to determine the scope of the first phase of the study, then during April. Next May, the team will visit and evaluate the initial data in depth, clear and comprehensive.
The main objectives of the project are 3: to understand the situation of climate change, hydrology, ecosystem in the area, 2: to understand the production chain and livelihood of the people in the area and 3: the ability of relevant institutions to Adapt to climate change to prioritize the implementation of this five-year project (2018-2022).
The Minister said that this project will definitely help to improve and maintain the health of the forest and water ecosystem around Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary through the development and sustainable management within the Prey Lang area.
The Minister expressed his hope and confidence that the project would be successful as expected, and requested that the project cooperate with the Forestry Administration and relevant units under the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, along with relevant development partners and the private sector. Excellent at all times: Make sure that the project implementation process runs smoothly and achieves better results.
The Minister requested the partners to pay attention to integrating appropriate agricultural technologies into planting, animal husbandry, aquaculture, agro-processing, agribusiness and agro-tourism, so that community members can improve their living standards. Reduce poverty and achieve the vision of the Royal Government by 2030.
