According to Lt. Col. Thach Sovanna, Chief of the Ang Snuol District Criminal Police, the victim was 31-year-old Mol, a factory worker in Ang Snuol II Village, Peuk Commune, Ang Snuol District, Kandal Province. The suspect is Un Sothy, 43 years old, a construction worker in Ang Snuol II village, Peuk commune, Ang Snuol district, Kandal province.
Lt. Thach Sovanna said that before the incident, the victim returned from a night shift and went to sleep alone on the roof. At the time of the incident, the suspect went upstairs and saw the victim sleeping in a mosquito net. He kept his mouth shut so that he would not scream, but then the victim moved and shouted for his mother to help and ran downstairs.
Mr. Thach Sovanna said that after the victim ran downstairs, the suspect put on his pants and ran after him and fled home. After being shocked, the victim reported and filed a complaint with the police, who took the suspect to the district police inspectorate for questioning.
