(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Industry and Handicraft this morning, March 21, 2019, held a national workshop on "Building a Demonstration Map of ASEAN Small and Medium Enterprises on Health and Tourism Industry." The workshop was held at the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts.
Dr. Lam Kim Leng stated that this project aims to raise the awareness and capacity of the trainees of the owners of handicraft enterprises on linking their business with other businesses and integrating their business processes, products or services into Regional and global markets as well.
Mr. Chhea Lay Hy, Director of the Department of Small and Medium Enterprises of the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts, said that in this context, the Royal Government has focused on:
* Completion of the development and effective implementation of the "Support Policy for Small and Medium Enterprises" * Strengthening the implementation of support mechanisms to facilitate registration * Provision of facilitation services * Dissemination of comprehensive market information in a timely manner And promote the value chain of products * Promoting entrepreneurship and innovation in response to the era of the fourth generation industrial revolution and promoting SME Go Digial
Mr. Chhea Lay Hy stated that the Royal Government has encouraged the tourism industry to attract national and international tourists with the multi-purpose of visiting Cambodia, and that some ASEAN member countries have been implementing this strategy.
Therefore, promoting the product quality of small and medium enterprises by strengthening compliance with sanitary and phytosanitary conditions, hygiene and standards, as well as promoting innovation, is a necessary task for the government to link SMEs and tourism as well as service providers. Health and so on. This is the additional emphasis of Mr. Chhea Lay Hy.
He said that the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts has set out the policy of supporting infrastructure to support enterprises developed in the SME cluster, which is defined as short, medium and long term, depending on the support action plan. All relevant partners, including the private sector, government institutions and development partners.
(Kampot): On March 21, 2019, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Committee for the 2019 Golden Dragon Exercise Committee, continued to lead the team to inspect the 2019 Golden Dragon Exercise between the Cambodian Army - China.
In reality, the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019, a joint training between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army, is going smoothly on the territory of Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province. It is concluded that the third Golden Dragon exercise between the two countries' armies will be successfully completed as planned in the next four days.
The Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army officially started on the morning of March 13, 2019 at the live shooting range of the 70th Brigade Techo Sen Chum Kiri Training School in Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province. It will be closed on March 25, 2019 under the high presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense.
Defense Ministry spokesman General Chhum Socheat asserted that the exercise was not a threat to anyone, and that the exercise was a demonstration of regional security participation through exchanges of experience, especially Experience in the fight against terrorism, rescuing people in the event of natural disasters.
