Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An Holds a 3-Year National Workshop on Military Alliance with Civilian Institutions
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, presided over the opening ceremony of a national seminar on the work of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) and its allies. The three periods are from 2015 to 2018.
The purpose of this workshop is 6 points, including:
First: Review the work results of the sisterhood for the past 3 years
Second, to encourage the Sisters to continue their activities and to strengthen the work of the Sisters to be more active.
Third, strengthen and expand the achievements of the sisterhood and filter the direction for long-term strategic benefits.
Fourth, to mobilize more of the sisterhood's contribution to the reform of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, especially in the socio-economic development of military families in the performance of national defense duties, as well as to prepare for retirement. Civil society
5th: Through this workshop to attract new sisterhood partners
Sixth: Properly evaluate the strengths (strengths) and find out the disadvantages and weaknesses of the past to encourage and orient the improvement in a timely manner.
