Cambodian diplomat: Cambodia is proud of its active role in Mekong-Lanchang cooperation from the very beginning (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, said that Cambodia Proud of its active role in Mekong-Lanchang cooperation from the very beginning.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon stated: “Cambodia is proud of its active role in the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation from the very beginning and we are confident that the concept of this initiative will continue to meet the needs of Cambodia. "And the Mekong region, especially when we are transforming our region into a region of peace, sustainable development and common prosperity."
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon said that Cambodia appreciates the special fund of China Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation of China with a budget of 300 million US dollars launched in 2016. The five-year plan is being used to support small and medium-sized software cooperation of all member countries.
"I am confident that the results of these projects will bring tangible benefits to the people of the entire Mekong region. Of those projects, Cambodia has received a total of 35 projects worth about US $ 14 million to support the development of infrastructure, software, knowledge and experience sharing, people-to-people exchanges and independent research projects. This is according to the message of the head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps.
The first Mekong-Lanchang Summit was held on March 22-23, 2016 in Sanya, Hainan Province, China, co-chaired by China and Thailand. The second Mekong-Lanchang Summit will be held from January 10-11, 2018 in Phnom Penh, Cambodia, with Cambodia and China as co-chairs and Laos as co-chair. China at the third summit.
