This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presents Diplomas to 1,578 Asia-Europe University Students
(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, March 21, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presented diplomas to 1,578 students at Asia Europe University. There are 640 women. The ceremony will take place at the National Institute of Education near the Independence Monument.
Dr. Duong Leang, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Asia-Europe University, said that the graduates today include undergraduate, bachelor's, master's and doctoral students who graduated in the 2016-2017 and 2017 academic years. -2018.
According to Dr. Duong Leang, today's graduates are also 35 scholarship students of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, including 14 women, 4 people with disabilities and 4 foreign students. People, too. The foreign students are two Laotians and two Koreans.
Dr. Duong Leang also said that students who receive this degree, master's degree and doctoral degree are 100% employed, and associate degree and bachelor's degree are 78% employed.
The President of the Board of Directors of Asia Europe University said that today's graduation ceremony is the 12th award for Asia Europe University.
Dr. Duong Leang claimed that currently Asia-Europe University has a total of 11,992 students and students studying at all levels, 5,468 females. There are 22 foreign students, including 1 American, 5 Koreans, 11 Laotians, 2 Chinese, 2 Taiwanese and 1 Nigerian.
Dr. Duong Leang emphasized that in order to participate in the spirit, will, commitment and cause of building and developing human resources of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government, Asia-Europe University has actively contributed to the Royal Government in promoting the effectiveness of Intellectual resource training.
Asia-Europe University also cooperates to exchange experiences with many national and international partners in the development of the field of education, including inviting famous national and international speakers to give experiences to share experiences with students of all generations. Study and provide opportunities for students to do internships to link theory to practice, which is an important capital for dissertation and graduation thesis.
