The European Commission has announced the suspension of the EBA under the EBA from 12 February 2019. Cambodia has six months to protest and negotiate with the European Commission to maintain the EBA.
If the European Commission does not accept Cambodia's interpretation and the European Union finally decides to suspend the EBA from Cambodia, the EBA suspension will take effect within 18 months from 12 February 2019. And if the EU decides to suspend the EBA, Cambodia will lose nearly $ 700 million in profits from the tariff, for which Cambodia exports more than $ 6 billion to Europe.
Speaking on the territory of Pursat province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that the dependence on others is Cambodia's independence will be limited, that is, Cambodia does not dare to protest with donors for fear of cutting aid. However, Samdech asserted that as long as an independent country had enough food, Cambodia would have equal rights and full rights to respond as an independent and sovereign country.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: Promotion and appointment are decided based on the thorough examination and evaluation of the management
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army, stated that promotions, appointments and assignments are decisions based on a thorough examination and evaluation by the leadership. Of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in accordance with the principles of law in force.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet made the remarks while attending the inauguration ceremony of the Special Zone Commander, Deputy Commander and Special Zone Commander at the Phnom Penh Special Military Command on March 19, 2019.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet added that the appointment of this position was not a transfer of authority or a transfer of power, but a transfer of responsibility from one generation to the next in order to have authority. In leadership, responsibility must be high to ensure the efficiency of all troops.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also congratulated on this special occasion and brought a heartfelt greeting from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and General Staff. Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to the officers, deputies and soldiers of the Special Zone today.
The Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Phum Min, the Commander of the Army, would like to express his sincere appreciation for the efforts made in building the unit in the past. In all fields, including the construction of camps, shelters, training, as well as close communication with the authorities with other units to serve the people.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet emphasized that in response to the merits, merits and achievements of the General in the past to serve the nation and the people, which is the confidence for the leadership, he has been promoted to the most appropriate position. Recognize and encourage the cause of the motherland in his efforts.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet continued that the achievement of all these results is a reflection of leadership, ability, will and creativity in leadership, mobilizing enough strength in the mission, even in difficult circumstances. And complicated circumstances sometimes occur in both political and military work. Appreciate the work that the Special Zone has achieved in the past under the leadership of all the commanders and officers.
"Currently, I see that the Special Military Zone, including its subordinate units, has been strengthened and made significant progress in all areas and professional work, especially unit building, security and public order cooperation, security cooperation," he said. "Give senior geographical leaders responsibility, improve the livelihood and maintain the well-being of the army, including the rescue of poor people."
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet added, "I am very proud of these achievements, especially as they reflect the hard work and commitment as well as the great internal unity of the leadership. And soldiers throughout the regional army to fulfill the duty to serve the motherland.
Customs and Excise Department issues measures to prevent and suppress the import, export and transit of ivory, rhinoceros and illegal sculptures
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is highly committed to participating in the fight against illegal wildlife trafficking through the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia issued measures to prevent and suppress the import, export and transit of ivory, rhinoceros. Illegal ivory and rhinoceros sculptures.
Dr. Kun Nhem said that the import, export and transit of ivory, rhinoceros and sculpture made from ivory and rhinoceros is illegal. The occurrence of these activities on the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia will have a negative impact on the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia as a Member State of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora, as well as Damage Cambodia's reputation on the international stage.
The six measures include strengthening the study, analysis, evaluation of information contained in the issuance of permits, invoices and / or packing lists to identify the import, export and illegal passage of prohibited goods such as ivory, rhinoceros Illegal ivory and rhinoceros sculptures. This is an offense that is subject to judicial action.
Measures to tighten the work to prevent and suppress the import, export and transit of ivory, rhinoceros and illegal ivory and ivory sculptures submitted by the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia are fully welcomed and supported. From the Ministry of Environment.
