Minister of Water Resources holds a technical review meeting to prepare for the diversion of Stung Prek Tnaot for the rainy season, which often causes floods
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on March 20, 2019, continued to chair a technical inspection meeting to divert the Prek Tnaot River, which often causes threatening floods during the rainy season. To Kampong Speu, Kandal, Takeo, especially Phnom Penh.
Minister Lim Kean Hor said the main purpose of the project was to find an immediate solution because the development process did not allow the use of existing infrastructure.
Therefore, the purpose of the project is to divert the maximum amount of water with water up to 1200-1500 m3 / s, diverting from the upper part before falling to the construction on 7 January, heading towards Takeo province as a rule to release water. Flooding and irrigation of crops by keeping the water flow along the old Stung Prek Tnaot at a reasonable level that can only be guaranteed.
