Chili sauce, fish sauce, Koh Kong, candy and pastries expired for sale at Samaki Krakor market, Pursat province, CamControl branch officials immediately confiscated and burned
(Pursat): CamControl Branch, Pursat Province, led by Mr. Touch Chao Koy, Branch Manager, in collaboration with officials of the Department of Commerce, Local Authority and Market Commission, on March 20, 2019, inspected the food products displayed at Samaki Market. Krakor is located in Pursat Province.
Mr. Toch Chao Koy said that during the inspection, his professional officers carried out preliminary analysis of dried fish, dumplings, prahok and pre-packaged goods at the stalls to find banned chemicals that could affect people's health. . As a result, his team did not find any banned chemicals.
According to the branch manager, however, Cam Kong Truol officers confiscated 70 kilograms of defective goods (expired) such as chili sauce, Koh Kong fish sauce, candy and sweets and immediately burned them in front of the police. Join.
Mr. Toch Chao Koy also instructed the traders and the owners of the goods to make a thumbprint contract to stop the sale of food products with the addition of banned chemicals and expired goods and made a record of the confiscation of those goods. Take it to destroy.
On that occasion, CamControl officials also explained to educate and guide traders to understand the law on quality and safety management of products, goods and services, and also distributed and posted posters.
