Seven Veterans Families in Pailin Receive Homes Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Pailin): On March 20, 2019, Lt. Col. To Kim Khun, Deputy Commander of Pailin Provincial Military Operations Area and a permanent member of the Provincial Veterans Association, representing Major General Prohm Pat, Commander of Pailin Provincial Military Operations Area and Chea The President of the Provincial Veterans Association helped build houses for 7 poor veterans' families, a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
Colonel To Kim Khun said that under the initiative and care of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, who always care about the well-being and livelihood. Live the lives of veterans all the time.
Currently, the Cambodian Veterans Association of Pailin Province is building houses for poor veterans who have no land and houses to live in so that they can have a decent place to live. He continued that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the veterans as comrades who fought to sacrifice their fresh flesh, blood and life for the cause of the motherland.
