Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The current situation in Cambodia, only the CPP can keep the peace (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party said that in the situation of Cambodia. At present, no political party can control the situation and keep the peace except the CPP.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement was made during a meeting with more than 10,000 workers in Pursat province on March 20, 2019. Pursat was also the last stronghold of the Khmer Rouge.
Cambodia is known to have been severely torn apart by the flames of war after March 18, 1970, after a coup d'état to oust King Norodom Sihanouk as the then-head of state. Divisions, brutal killings took place during the Khmer Rouge regime led by Pol Pot's group, which seized power from Lon Nol's group on April 17, 1975.
The flames of war devastated Cambodia, a famous country in the region in the 1960s, to the point of devastation of infrastructure and human resources. Cambodia began to recover after the fall of the Khmer Rouge on January 7, 1979, through the resistance movement of Khmer Krom fighters, the movement of the United Front for National Salvation, with many leaders and political figures as leaders of the CPP. Cambodia today.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the current President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), is a Cambodian statesman who has set out a win-win policy to mobilize Cambodians from all parties to the conflict, including the Khmer Rouge and border fighters, to live under the Royal Government. One. Bring Cambodia to know the peace and unity in the Khmer nation from 1998 to the present, which has never been seen in the history of Cambodia for about 500 years.
To date, peace and unity in Cambodia have lasted for 20 years. However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen still sees that the situation in Cambodia is still fragile and prone to war again if there is no strict and clear control.
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the fragility of this war is also due to the group of former CNRP members with Sam Rainsy as the mastermind. Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that not even leading the country, the former CNRP has already incited the army against the government.
Complete peace in Cambodia over the past 20 years has made the country highly developed with maintaining an economic growth rate of about 7%. Has become a poor country as a low middle income country and has set its ambitions to become a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
In order to ensure the maintenance of peace, which is the most important factor for national development and building a better life of the people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he will continue to lead Cambodia until the former opposition party disappears from the planet. This.
