Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks came after Mr. Sam Rainsy and his allies repeatedly attacked and insulted some of the 118 former CNRP leaders who had been banned from politics and had applied for re-election. Considered as an ideal sale to the CPP.
Speaking at a meeting with workers in Pursat province on the morning of March 20, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen strongly criticized Mr. Sam Rainsy, who considered his former colleagues as commodities.
As the leader of the country, Samdech Techo has given the concept of respecting the freedom of all people, regardless of their political affiliation. "Those who come out to ask for political rights, we respect those who do not ask for rights, we respect your decision, why do you despise those who used to work with you as a commodity," he said.
As of now (March 20, 2019), nine former leaders of the former Cambodia National Rescue Party (CNRP) have been reinstated by the King and the Acting Head of State out of 118 political prisoners. Subsequently, they submitted an application to the Ministry of Interior.
Some of those who applied for political rights reacted angrily to those who insulted them for selling their heads, while others only called for understanding not to insult those who applied for political rights.
Ou Chanrath, a former CNRP lawmaker, declined to comment at this time, waiting for an announcement at an upcoming conference. But in the past, he has called for former members of the CNRP not to insult individuals who apply for political rights.
During the same ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded the special and dignified point of the Cambodian People's Party not to attack and insult the person who left the party like the former opposition party. Samdech expressed sympathy for those who left the opposition party, which was insulted as puppets or rotten meat.
Samdech continued: "Surprisingly, since 2008, I have observed that at that time, some former MPs from other parties to the CPP were considered rotten meat, now it continues to be meat. "Rotten meat is bought, exchanged."
At the same time, the Prime Minister of Cambodia asked all foreigners to judge the people they consider to be democrats in the past. Samdech questioned whether Democrats should block their rights? At that time, Samdech also broke the story that Mr. Sam Rainsy worked for Samdech in 2006 to change the Constitution from two-thirds to 50 plus one.
"In Cambodia, there is no politician who does not cooperate with Hun Sen, but if you say that, I say you used to serve me and help me solve the situation without getting stuck," he said. "Any crashes after the election, I thank you, but please confirm that I used your head when you insulted me as a puppet."
As for applying for the right to do politics, Samdech is still helping to create conditions for the King to ask for political rehabilitation as the Prime Minister, who has been given the job by law. However, Samdech also stated that if they do not apply for political rights, the opposition will lose the opportunity to vote in the May 2022 commune council elections.
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered that the fact that some opposition groups that have been banned from entering the country to apply for political rights at this time also helped to make it easier for Samdech to control the country.
