Washington: US President Donald Trump has vowed to support Brazil's accession to NATO, including the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), to make it easier for the Latin American country to buy weapons from the United States. America. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday morning, March 20, 2019.
Donald Trump made the remarks during a meeting with Brazilian President Jair Bolsonaro at the White House on Tuesday. In addition, the United States is reported to be granting NATO special alliance status to Brazil, which will make it easier for Brazil to purchase military equipment or weapons and technology from the United States.
On Tuesday, the State Department said Washington had signed an agreement with Brazil on protecting US technology over its participation in the launch of the spacecraft in Latin America.
Supreme Court Leaks Trial of Dr. Kem Ley Murder Due to Absent Lawyer
(Phnom Penh): The Supreme Court hearing scheduled for the morning of March 20, 2019 to hear Oeut Ang's appeal in connection with the assassination of Dr. Kem Ley has been postponed indefinitely. After today's hearing, the convict's lawyer was absent.
Ouk Kimsith, spokesman for the Supreme Court, confirmed to Fresh News that the criminal case in the case of the accused murder requires the presence of a defense lawyer before the trial can take place. Also demanded a lawyer. Therefore, the Supreme Court has reserved the right to provide a lawyer for the accused in accordance with the law.
Mr. Oeut Ang, alias Chuob Samlab, appealed the decision of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and the Court of Appeal, which sentenced him to life in prison for the murder of Dr. Kem Ley.
