Japanese in Cambodia set up fund to help families of victims of Siem Reap robbery
(Phnom Penh): A few days ago, there was a horrific robbery case with two Japanese people robbing and killing a Cambodian taxi driver in Puok district, Siem Reap province. This brutal murder case caused a great deal of surprise and regret among the Cambodian people, especially the Japanese people living in Cambodia, who expressed their apology to the Cambodian people for the robbery and murder by the two suspects who are Japanese. On.
At the same time, the Japanese people living and working in Cambodia also agreed under the initiative of Koichita Kumar, a Japanese national and president of the Japanese Association in Cambodia. A fundraiser to help the families of the victims, their wives and four children, who have lost their good husbands and good fathers.
Koichita Kumar said that on behalf of the Japanese people, he would like to express his condolences to the families of the victims, and all Japanese people are deeply saddened and ashamed of the atrocities and lack of consideration of the people. These two suspects, which affect the good relations between Japan and Cambodia.
As a result, Japanese people living in Cambodia have started to raise funds to support the families of the victims by starting to raise funds from March 19 to 31, 2019. As of the morning of March 20, more than 150 Japanese people have donated their own funds, and it is expected that more Japanese people will join the fund before the day it is handed over to the families of the victims. Next April.
