Tbong Khmum Provincial Governor sets out six principles to improve the health sector while the provincial hospital worth nearly $ 50 million is under construction
(Tbong Khmum): After the Cambodia-China Tbong Khmum Hospital worth nearly 50 million dollars, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the recent construction process to serve the health sector in Tbong Khmum province.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, also set out six additional principles to strengthen the provision of health services to citizens to be better to be ready to receive medical treatment for citizens in the province as well as throughout the country.
The introduction of these six important principles was made on the occasion that he presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the results of 2018 and set the direction for 2019 of Tbong Khmum Provincial Health Department on March 18, 2019 yesterday. At Tbong Khmum Provincial Hall.
The six principles include:
First, the improvement of the health sector, both public and private, diagnosis, treatment and care, which need to be more focused.
Second, to enhance the professional capacity of health workers in medical practice, professional ethics and communication attitudes to build trust and confidence of the people.
Third, monitor and evaluate the quality of services on a regular basis, including the quality of services in the private sector. Ensure that hospitals, health centers need to have doctors, staff, and guards on duty 24 hours a day, both on holidays and other holidays, for regular medical check-ups and care, adhering to their own code of ethics.
Fourth, the Department of Health must pay more attention to find and resolve in a timely manner the root causes of all the issues raised in this conference.
Fifth, regular monitoring and inspection on food hygiene for human health is a duty that must not be delayed or delayed any restaurant, restaurant, guesthouse, hotel or other places, because most of the disease. Out of lack of hygiene. So think about food before thinking about medicine.
And 6: Local authorities at all levels must provide good cooperation in the process of providing health services to people throughout the province, especially on urgent work required by the health sector.
At the same time, Mr. Cheam Chan Sophoan will also hope that all of the above are additional inputs to contribute to the implementation of the goals set by the Provincial Health Assembly for 2019.
According to Ty Norin, Cambodia's seven hydropower plants, which can generate about 7 million kilowatt-hours, equivalent to about 7,000 megawatts, currently generate only about 3,000 megawatts due to the water in the reservoir. Each is very dry.
Mr. Ty Norin also said that according to the plan in 2019, the demand for electricity is around 9,000 megawatts, but the current energy demand has increased to more than 10,000 megawatts.
To solve the current problem, Mr. Ty Norin said that Cambodia has used two mechanisms, the first is to ask factories, enterprises and hotels to turn on their generators and to cut off electricity in some areas during the day. . The second mechanism is to buy electricity from neighboring countries such as Thailand, Laos and Vietnam.
According to Ty Norin, the power shortage could last until the end of May. However, during this time, for Sundays and other national holidays, there is no power outage.
