Well-known historical researchers: Khmer was the first person to create zero in the world
(Phnom Penh): A group of well-known historians and scholars have claimed that the Khmer people were the first to create zero in the world. This was stated by a group of professors who are well-known historians in Cambodia, confirmed in an interview after the conference on the history of mathematics zero on the morning of March 19, 2019 at the Center for Cooperation in Cambodia. Korea (CKCC).
The conference was attended by representatives of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, as well as stakeholders and hundreds of students.
Professor Pat Suy Kry, head of the Cambodian Volunteer Researchers Group, said that Cambodia was the first country to find zero. He said that the number zero is written to represent the number written as a character is 604, and this number has been studied for many years.
"We have been studying this zero spread for five years to let our Cambodians know that our Cambodians are the creators," he said.
Mr. Sastra Vong Sotheara, Head of the Department of Charity and History of Khmer and Southeast Asia, said that it is known that Cambodia has a long history because of the inscriptions on the stone.
Mr. Chhun Hok, Vice Chancellor of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, stated that the conference on the history of mathematics of zero aims to provide knowledge such as education, mathematics, history and evolution of mathematics, the promotion of mathematics, the promotion of research culture. Mathematics.
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, urged all inmates in Kampong Cham Provincial Prison and Tbong Khmum Provincial Prison to transform themselves into good citizens in society. After serving the sentence, the sentence is final.
Mr. Keo Remy issued this warning on March 19, 2019, on the occasion of his visit and visit the detainees in Kampong Cham and Tbong Khmum Provincial Prisons located in Chiro 2 Commune, Tbong Khmum, Tbong Khmum Province.
Along with the visit, he also handed over the donations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the officials and detainees in this prison.
Mr. Keo Remy continued that the Prime Minister always takes care of people from all walks of life, even in prison, especially women prisoners, so please change yourself to become a good citizen who lives in a land of peace and prosperity in all fields. .
He said a large number of detainees were involved in drugs. So when you are in a correctional center, try to break free, and when you leave, stay away because drugs destroy us, our families, our brothers and sisters, and our society as a whole. He also praised the administrators of the two provincial prisons, which have set up libraries, gyms, especially vocational training for all detainees, which is useful for them to have skills when they leave.
According to the report of Mr. Hun Khy, Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Prison, as of March 6, 2019, the prison has 1,825 inmates in both provinces, including 128 women.
