Fire engulfs 4 houses, injures 2 in Mondulkiri
(Mondulkiri): A huge fire started to burn at the gas station, causing 4 houses to burn, injuring two women at around 5 pm on March 18, 2019 in Mepai village, Po Chrey commune, Pichda district Mondulkiri Province.
Authorities say the fire started in a gas station, which was suspected to be under construction. Authorities claimed that before the incident, the owner of the provocative house suddenly poured gasoline into the kitchen and caused the fire to spread quickly to the neighbor's house.
Sources said that immediately after the incident, the fire truck of the Mondulkiri Provincial Police immediately intervened. However, due to the power of the fire, it could not be extinguished in time, causing four houses to catch fire. In addition to the house fire, two women also suffered severe burns.
The fire was completely extinguished around 7 pm on the same day. Authorities have not yet been able to sum up the extent of the damage caused by the fire.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Leang Phaly, Chairman of the Volunteer Medical Team, Mr. HUN Many confirmed that so far, more than 4,000 volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many, have examined and treated 170 people. There are 414,294 people (forty-four thousand two hundred and ninety-four) in 17 capitals and provinces, and the charitable work of all doctors has been done for the past seven years, helping the Cambodian health sector to some extent.
The confirmation of the Chairman of the Working Group of Volunteer Doctors, Mr. HUN Many, was made on the occasion that the working group inspected and distributed free medicine to 12,969 people at Tbong Primary School, Tnot Mlou Village, Reab Commune. Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, on March 17, 2019, with the participation of Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, along with many other provincial leaders.
