(Phnom Penh): Twelve representatives from educational institutions and universities from New Zealand traveled to Phnom Penh to participate in the New Zealand Study and Scholarship Fair to be held on March 27, 2019 at ACE. Toul Tompong Branch from 9am to 4pm. Every year, this exhibition is organized by IDP Cambodia and is open to the public free of charge.
Mao Sreng, Director of IDP Cambodia, said: “New Zealand is becoming a popular study destination for Cambodian students studying abroad. The New Zealand Study and Scholarship Fair is a unique platform for those wishing to pursue their studies in New Zealand to meet directly with representatives of educational institutions and universities from there.
Separately, IELTS test center officials in Cambodia will come to advise on exam registration and IELTS preparation. Representatives from the Australian Center for Training (ACE) will also be present at the event and provide information on learning English to prepare for the New Zealand Institutional Qualifications.
Meanwhile, Mr. Chheang Vantak, Head of Student Relations Abroad at IDP Cambodia, said, "New Zealand provides students with a world-class education and global recognition. "The people there are friendly and the environment is safe, along with a multicultural culture."
He added, "Students have the opportunity to work part-time while studying. "All of these factors make New Zealand a great destination for students to study abroad."
In Cambodia, students and parents can call for more information regarding study abroad at all IDP study abroad offices located at all ACE Phnom Penh and Siem Reap branches.
