Samdech Prime Minister: Vietnam and Thailand also face the same electricity problem as Cambodia, while Cambodia requests for additional supply (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that Cambodia has requested additional power supply from the country. Vietnam and Thailand, but these countries also face electricity shortages like Cambodia, and Samdech continues to call on people to be patient with this problem.
The speech of Samdech Techo Prime Minister was made this morning, March 18, 2019, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the presentation of certificates and diplomas to vocational and associate students, associate degree, bachelor's degree and master's degree. 709 of the New Generation Khmer Institute at the National Institute of Education.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "We ask Vietnam to help supply more than what was previously requested, they are sending 200 megawatts, but Vietnam is also facing the same problem as us .... We propose to Thailand, Thailand also has a problem, we propose to Laos, but (Laos uses) transmission network. "Laos has electricity, but the transmission line needs time to build because we need to draw electricity from Laos to supply the Preah Vihear area."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia confirmed that the development plan for the power sector was misjudged because the growth of consumption exceeded expectations. However, Samdech Techo claimed that the shortage of electricity has not yet affected the production line in factories, because Cambodia still has more than 1,000 megawatts of electricity.
"So this issue continues to call on our people to be patient with this difficult situation, but it does not reach the production area to affect the production area," he said. However, we still have more than 1,000 megawatts of electricity in use today ....
When talking about the shortage of electricity, Samdech also mentioned the shortage of water. In this sense, Samdech told institutions to know how to turn on the air conditioner, because it can reduce the use of electricity to some extent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Thailand has also experienced this water shortage to the point of restricting the use of water. Samdech Techo stated that the lack of water, lack of electricity is not a disaster until it can not be controlled.
Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) recently also explained to the people the problem of electricity, as in the past, the power supply was stable and there were not many outages. Unfortunately for Cambodia this year, despite the large number of sources of electricity generated, due to the rising sun, the source of hydropower, which uses hydropower to generate electricity, has not been able to generate its full power. .
Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) said that the increase in heat caused the water stored in each dam to evaporate abnormally, causing the water in the dam to begin to recede, making it impossible for the hydropower station to produce energy. Not enough of its own strength and also cause the production of electricity distributed to consumers is not enough on demand.
Please note that in the dry season in 2019, Cambodia will experience severe drought, especially during April and May, the temperature will rise to 40 to 42 degrees due to the indirect effects of El Nino (El Nino). . The Royal Government has called on the authorities and the people to take measures to conserve water for use.
Through this circular, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has set out three important measures to deal with this problem. The three measures include:
1: The work of cultivating dry season rice in 2019 can only be done once, as it is not possible to make dry season rice for the second time, even though the water in the reservoirs and some places with natural water It should be stored for daily use and for growing other crops besides rice.
