The visit to inspect the construction site of the expressway was also attended by Mr. You Sunlong, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister and members of the relevant project working group.
It should be noted that the project to build the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway was signed between Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and Mr. Leav Chhithav, President of the China Transport Construction Company in early 2018. The signing ceremony was presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang during his visit to Cambodia.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway is planned to be built in four lanes, with two lanes to two lanes to the district, asking for a garden in the middle of the road. You travel too. The expressway is scheduled to take four years to build.
Mr. Sun Chanthol expressed the expectation that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway will play an important role in transporting goods to the two main economic poles, Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville. In particular, the transportation of goods from factories to the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port for export to the country, as well as the transportation of goods from the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port to other regions.
The Minister believes that this expressway will contribute more to boosting Cambodia's economy.
