The coup came as Sihanouk was traveling to Europe, the Soviet Union and China, and large-scale anti-Vietnamese protests erupted in Phnom Penh. Protesters attacked the embassies of North Vietnam and the Viet Cong (Provisional Revolutionary Government of the Republic of South Vietnam).
