Tbong Khmum (Tbong Khmum): Two Thai officers involved in the blast at a Chinese quarry named "Chai Naroth Enbrit Corporation" in Andong Lve village, Chob commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province, hit a truck driver in the head. The Investigating Judge of Tbong Khmum Provincial Court issued a temporary detention order.
Please be informed that this incident happened at 05:10 pm on March 15, 2019 at the stone grinding site of the Chinese above, causing a man to die immediately at the place named Chum Rachana, 29 years old, driving a car. Ben Dek Thmor The above company is located in Svay Village, Rohat Teuk Commune, Mongkul Borey District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Regarding this case, the General Commissioner stressed that he has opened a careful investigation to reach legal action against the owners of the above location, which may have caused harm to the lives of others. The commissioner claims that as determined before the blast, the site owner must notify residents, such as turning on the siren or using a microphone.
Lt. Gen. Ben Roth confirmed that "I am taking action according to the procedure, the commander can face the crime of involuntary manslaughter, because in the conditions before the explosion, they have to inform the people first, have a siren, have a microphone and shout. "Now we are investigating."
According to the commissioner, immediately after the incident, the specialized police force arrested eight people who could be involved, including the Chief of Administration, the Chief of Interpreters, and one of them was a Thai who was the commander of the bombing. The arrest was made after the approval of Mr. Pok Dara, Deputy Prosecutor of Tbong Khmum Province.
(Phnom Penh): Wing Specialized Bank (Cambodia) Limited received the “Digital Innovation Institution” award from the “Cambodia ICT Awards 2019” held at Raffles Royal Hotel last night. March 15, 2019.
The award ceremony coincided with Wing, a leading mobile banking provider, showcasing innovative digital products and services at Cambodia's largest technology expo called "Digital Cambodia" on Diamond Island. March 15-17, 2019.
At the award ceremony, Mr. Wojo Malolos, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said that it is a matter of pride for Wing Specialized Bank to serve Cambodian customers over the past 10 years by providing state-of-the-art financial technology. But simple, bringing customers to a new world of mobile banking, especially people who have never used banking financial services.
"This award is a testament to the fact that Wing is a company that brings the latest digital technology innovations to Cambodia, opening up many possibilities for Cambodians, whether in their business or not. Their daily lives. For customers who want to know more about Wing's products and services, they can also visit the Wing booth at the Cambodia Digital Expo.
The CEO of Wing Specialized Bank stated that Wing's presence in the "Digital Cambodia" technology exhibition aims to bring people closer to the latest technology, especially financial technology, because Wing Specialized Bank believes that the people of Cambodia Will be ready for the digital economy that the Cambodian government aims to achieve by 2023.
Jojo Malolos also said that participants or private companies can seek a wide range of consultations related to Wing products and services, especially how Wing Specialized Bank can help arrange their business payments more quickly and easily. Safe.
It should be noted that the ICT Award of Cambodia, organized by the National Institute of Posts, Telecommunications and Information and Communication Technology (NIPTICT) was established in 2015, is the largest national communication technology competition in Cambodia aimed at Demonstrate the achievements and success of innovation in the field of information and communication technology (ICT) in Cambodia.
