Cambodia has 170,000 hectares of cashew cultivation area, harvested more than 130,000 tons, 4 large cashew processing factories are operating!
(Phnom Penh): According to the data of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in 2018, Cambodia has more than 170,000 hectares of cashew plantations and harvested 136,094 tons of cashew nuts.
Minister of Agriculture Veng Sakhon stated that 10% of the harvested cashew nuts are processed to meet domestic demand, 20% are processed for export and 70% are exported to Vietnam.
At present, Cambodia has many small cashew processing factories, while there are about four large processing factories in Kampong Thom, Kampong Cham, Preah Vihear and Tbong Khmum.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Agriculture on March 12, 2019 issued a decision to establish a working group to promote the development of cashew crops in Cambodia in order to accelerate the program to achieve fresh yields of 1 million tons of cashew nuts this year. Up to 2029. Khieu Samet elected 5th AFF President
Khieu Samet was the Vice President of the Southeast Asian Football Federation and also the Acting President last term. But as the AFF prepares for the 2019 General Assembly, all members voted in favor of Khieu Samet as president of the Southeast Asian Football Federation, and this is also the first time AFF has had a Cambodian leadership.
It should be noted that this Sunday, the Football Federation of Southeast Asia held its annual general assembly, choosing Siem Reap, Cambodia to host. The General Assembly was held in the presence of Mr. Sao Sokha, President of the Football Federation of Cambodia, and was also attended by representatives of the International Football Federation (FIFA) and the Asian Football Confederation (AFC).
