(Kampong Cham): Dr. Ma Chhoeun, Member of Parliament for Kampong Cham Constituency and Chairman of the Central Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) visited Cheung Prey District on March 17, 2019, opened a public forum with representatives of people living in Pring Chrum Commune, Cheung Prey District. More than 200 people in the Pring Chrum pagoda in Pring Chrum commune, Cheung Prey district, Kampong Cham province.
This forum is designed to collect all the needs, requests as well as challenges of the people to examine the possibility of solving the problem of water shortage in the dry season, and especially the construction of housing for the poor homeless.
Dr. Ma Chhoeun said that the purpose of this public forum is to provide opportunities for people to raise their needs as well as suggestions and raise their local challenges such as security, public order issues. Gambling, drugs, theft and so on.
According to residents of Pring Chrum commune, security, public order, gambling, drugs and theft in their locality are not significant, including the provision of Local authority services.
