Legal Awareness: Labor Dispute Resolution Mechanism in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In general, in the Kingdom of Cambodia, in all disputes that have arisen, whether in the economic, commercial and labor sectors, judicial mechanisms and non-judicial dispute resolution mechanisms, such as negotiation, have been used. And conciliation, for example, to resolve those disputes on the basis of the law in force.
According to the Labor Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, labor disputes are divided into two types: individual disputes and joint labor disputes, both of which use different mechanisms to be used in resolving disputes. The mechanisms to be used include negotiation, conciliation, settlement in the Arbitration Council, strikes or lockouts, and settlement in the judiciary.
The mechanism for resolving individual disputes according to the Labor Law has two stages:
The mechanism for resolving joint disputes according to the Labor Law has three stages:
