Mr. Som Aun leads the union delegation to return to Cambodia after a five-day visit to Laos
During the five-day official visit, Mr. Som Oun and the accompanying delegation of the National Union Congress of Cambodia were warmly welcomed by the Lao Confederation of Trade Unions (LFTU).
The Lao Confederation of Trade Unions also held a bilateral meeting with five NACC leaders and five Lao union leaders. The bilateral meeting was to exchange experiences and strengthen cooperation, and agreed on six principles that are fundamental to the implementation of the two sides.
A delegation from the Cambodian National Trade Union Congress also visited the Cambodian Embassy in Laos to pay a courtesy call. Mr. Kiet Satharady, Adviser to the Cambodian Embassy in Laos, Representative Mr. Cheng Manit, Ambassador of the Kingdom of Cambodia to Laos welcomed and supported the trade relations between the two countries and urged the two countries' unions to further strengthen cooperation for the common good. Of the people of both countries.
Delegates from the Cambodian National Trade Union Congress also continued to fly from Vientiane to Luang Prabang, a former old city dating back to the 13th century AD. The Luong Prabang Provincial Union welcomed the Cambodian Union delegation and organized a program for the Cambodian Union delegation to visit a number of tourist sites, such as historical, cultural and natural sites.
It should be noted that at the invitation of the Lao Confederation of Unions, the National Assembly of the Cambodian Confederation of Unions has organized a five-day delegation led by Mr. Som Oun to pay a five-day official visit to Vientiane from 11 to 15 May. March 2019, which is the third delegation exchange since 2013.
