Samdech Prime Minister urges all provinces to use the points in each province to attract tourism (Video inside) (Kampong Chhnang): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, urged all stakeholders to work hard Develop tourism in cities, towns, riverside and make Kampong Chhnang an attractive tourist destination.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "To use the points in each province to attract tourism, such as in our province of Kampong Chhnang, there are some places that we need to expand it into an attractive tourist resort. "
The Prime Minister's encouragement was made on the occasion that Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, presided over the celebration of the 5th River Festival in Kampong Chhnang province on the evening of March 16. This 2019.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has requested that Kampong Chhnang province not be a place where people and tourists pass by, so the Kampong Chhnang provincial authorities must find attractive ways for tourists to visit. Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that Samdech used to eat noodles at a place called delicious noodles in Phsar Leu area, this small point and Samdech wanted to show the attraction of tourists.
Speaking of tourism, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the decline in tourism in Sihanoukville, stating that in other provinces there is an increase in tourism, so look at the whole forest better than the original. One tree. Samdech Techo said that people do not visit only one province, that is, all provinces in Cambodia have places to visit.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Some people say that tourism in Sihanoukville is declining, but they forget that with tourism in Sihanoukville, tourism in Kampong Chhnang has increased. Kiri is on the rise Tourism in Ratanakkiri is on the rise. At this point, I say that looking at the whole forest is better than looking at one real forest, and looking at one forest is also combined with looking at the whole forest. ”
At the same time, in order to give Kampong Chhnang more potential, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced the construction of roads and bridges from Kampong Chhnang to Kampong Thom. Samdech Techo stated that the three tributaries of the Phsar Krom, Chroy Mok and Kampong Hav rivers must be connected.
The announcement of the big gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the occasion of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit presiding over the celebration of the 5th River Festival under the theme "River: Connecting Peace, People and Tourism" in Kampong Chhnang Province. This evening, March 16, 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Today, I would like to announce to the people in Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom that I have decided to grant permission to build a bridge and a road connecting Kampong Chhnang to Kampong Thom, which is more specialized. 57 km, which connects Kampong Leng district of Kampong Chhnang province to Stung Sen city of Kampong Thom province Please give New Year gifts to the people of Kampong Chhnang and Kampong Thom provinces.
The Prime Minister also announced that the bridge to be built is the longest bridge in Cambodia up to 3,900 meters and will cross three tributaries, including Phsar Krom, Chroy Bos and Tonle. Kampong Hav, which is a bridge so as not to affect the waterway and fish traffic.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen strongly hopes that all people will benefit greatly from this new road and bridge, as experts have already studied that there is no impact that leads to the destruction of natural resources or Diversion and blockage of waterways and movement of fish.
