Samdech also stated that Cambodia was very difficult during the last war and can be found as it is today. Samdech stated that Kampong Chhnang province 30 years ago was also a war zone between the army of Samdech and the Khmer Rouge, and now this province has become an area where the development of peace until the land grab.
Samdech urges all people to keep the peace so that our river does not become a river of suffering like in the past.
Cambodia went through decades of civil war following the March 18, 1970 coup overthrow of Norodom Sihanouk by Lon Nol. The Khmer Rouge then overthrew the Republic of Kampuchea on April 17, 1975, establishing Democratic Kampuchea. Later, the Khmer Rouge regime, led by Pol Pot, was overthrown by the Kampuchean National Salvation Army under the participation of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army on January 7, 1979.
Although the Khmer Rouge regime collapsed in 1979, the war did not end there, dragging it along the border until the Paris Agreement of 1991 and continued confrontation until a win-win policy was set out by Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the Khmer Rouge surrender completely on December 29, 1998. Until now, the winning policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is 20 years and 3 months old.
France: 30 arrested in yellow vest protests in Week 18
Protesters on Saturday drew 7,000 to 8,000 people and violence erupted in the Champs-Elysees district of Paris after some protesters stormed shops on the streets. In response, French police used tear gas and arrested at least 30 people.
The yellow-vested protesters have entered their 18th week since it began in November 2018 against French President Nicolas Sarkozy's economic policies.
