On the occasion of the opening ceremony, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, said, "This is the first time that we have organized a conference and a digital exhibition of Cambodia 2019 in the country to bring together all relevant institutions. All at the national and regional levels coincide with the start of a new mandate, the sixth mandate of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth added that digital technology will give Cambodia the opportunity to expand its scope of development beyond traditional development, but it will take at least 10 years to build a full-fledged digital economy.
He said that progress with Huawei's clear vision and mission by bringing digital to everyone, every home and every institution to a smart network and a smart Cambodia in line with the theme of the Cambodian Digital Conference and Exhibition.
He said that Cambodia is an emerging market, which is a great power to connect innovation and business. 2019 will be an important year for 5G technology in Cambodia. Huawei, the world's leading supplier of 5G technology, will help all operators achieve their 5G technology dreams.
Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, praised Huawei for its 20-year commitment in Cambodia and expressed appreciation for Huawei's support and support in the program.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Donation to Poor Veterans in Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): Donations from the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association were handed over to the needy veterans in Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province this morning. March 16, 2019.
Major General Chan Sopheaktra, Commander of the Preah Vihear Military Operation Area and President of the Provincial Cambodian Veterans Association, said that the Cambodian Veterans Association, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always taken care of their well-being. Veterans across the country.
In particular, for Preah Vihear Province, as the President of the Provincial Cambodian Veterans Association, he always advised the Veterans Working Group in the cities and districts to pay attention to the challenges in the daily life of the veterans in order to have measures to solve them. Timely.
He added that today, the Cambodian Veterans Association of Preah Vihear Province brought the precious gift of Samdech Techo, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, to the families of veterans in Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, who have a poor living standard.
Separately, on March 15, 2019, yesterday, the Cambodian Veterans Association of Preah Vihear Province also led a working group to help build a house for the families of veterans in Chhep District and distributed donations in the form of money and materials donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. To 20 elderly families as well.
Authorities launch garbage collection campaign from Boeung Trabek and Boeung Salang canals, nearly 10,000 tons of garbage per year is removed from Boeung Trabek canal
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration and the Department of Public Works and Transport this morning, March 16, 2019, continued to collect garbage from Boeung Salang and Boeung Trabek canals, which people dumped anarchically in the past.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, said that environmental cleaning and garbage collection from the Boeung Salang canal will be carried out from Street 336 in Sangkat Boeung Salang, Khan Toul Kork to the base of the Stung Meanchey flyover.
Separately, Boeung Trabek canal, Chamkar Mon district, will be implemented from the corner of Street 484 and Street 105 to the station of Street 371, in which the team collected garbage along the mouth of the canal. He said that the machinery of the Department of Public Works and Transport also seized garbage from the canal to transport trucks to the landfill in Dangkor.
Mr. Sam Piseth also said that for the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, not only the Boeung Salang canal, but also the Boeung Trabek canal.
"Boeung Trabek canal, we put out about 150 cubic meters of garbage per day and about 8,500 tons per year, and we do this every month so that the whole canal can release water," he said. . In addition, we have also been restoring drainage and groundwater reservoirs near Wat Botum Vat.
On that occasion, Mr. Sam Piseth also called on all people to cooperate in cleaning the environment, especially to avoid throwing garbage in the canal.
