(Phnom Penh): At the beginning of 2019, the Ministry of Health continued to deploy health workers in public health facilities in a good, equitable and efficient manner to improve the provision of health services to people living in rural and urban areas. Remote.
According to a report by the Ministry of Health, obtained by Fresh News on March 16, 2019, along with the development of health infrastructure at the local level to increase each year, the number of health workers is increasing. In rural areas as well as through the assignment to work at those health centers and health posts.
To encourage health workers working in remote, disadvantaged areas, the Royal Government also provides incentives (local allowances) on a monthly basis to 4,316 health workers working in the districts. 576 health centers and 78 health posts.
