Scientists: The last 30 years are the hottest period in 2,000 years
BEIJING (Reuters) - A joint study by Chinese and US scientists found that the last 30 years were the hottest times in 2,000 years due to the effects of climate change. Of greenhouse gases caused by gradual human activity. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Saturday morning, March 16, 2019.
According to the scientists of the above research group, the highlands are vulnerable to climate change due to the main natural factors that used to affect the weather, namely solar radiation and volcanic activity, but by the end of the century. Second, greenhouse gases from human activities have become the largest cause of global warming.
