Obviously, as in the past year, the power supply has been stable and less frequent. Unfortunately for Cambodia this year, although many sources of electricity have been generated, due to the rising sun, the source of hydropower, which uses hydropower to generate electricity, has not been able to generate its full power. No.
This increase in temperature causes the water stored in each dam to evaporate abnormally, causing the water in the dam to begin to recede, making it impossible for the station to produce enough energy. That is why the production of electricity distributed to consumers is not enough as needed.
In addition to meeting the needs of the people, electricity plays a very important role to serve the production line in factories, enterprises and tourism service providers such as hotels.
Factories, enterprises and tour operators such as hotels need electricity to run production lines to meet the needs of their customers who can not miss, and hotels also need electricity to meet. Needed by tourists visiting Cambodia.
However, the Royal Government and Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) have not been indifferent to addressing and responding to this challenge. Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has continued to seek the purchase of additional power sources from neighboring countries, as well as to generate more power on its own, such as negotiations with Turkey to bring in a power plant to generate electricity.
Due to the power outage, some Cambodians who experienced power outages and did not understand the problem began to complain about the difficulties caused by the power outage. Others have gone so far as to insult the Royal Government and Electricite du Cambodge.
In fact, in a democracy, criticism is the freedom of the people, but it should not lead to insults, because in the Cambodian constitution and law, insults are prohibited. On the other hand, this insult is also an indication of the moral deficit of our Cambodian people.
People in developed countries such as China, Japan and South Korea, which are all countries prone to natural disasters. This nation, when faced with problems, they are patient, not so much as to sit and complain or sit and blame only the government, they also try to find a solution or find other ways to solve their problems. With the Royal Government.
Because of the habit of not complaining when faced with this problem, the people of the nations of the Asian countries, like the Cambodians, have come up with clever ideas to create devices that meet the challenges of their daily lives. People.
Cambodians of Asian descent, such as Chinese, Japanese, and Koreans, should change their habits and attitudes with great patience when facing problems, and turn from complaining and insulting to finding solutions. Better. Solutions cannot be made by sitting around complaining or cursing.
