1: Monitor computerized prescriptions, which the Ministry of Health has already issued guidelines that can help manage patient data, gradually reducing inaccurate prescriptions.
3: Encourage the use of drugs according to the guidelines to avoid drug congestion
4. Disseminate the textbook and study the minimum set of guidelines (MPA) to all health center staff and request the health center director to ensure that all staff members have a copy, and that the provincial health department (PHD) monitor the work. This
8. Encourage hard-working employees and set an example for others.
