(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate of the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), on March 15, 2019, stated that he discussed the option of placing a ship to a power plant of a Turkish company as an additional emergency measure to address Lack of electricity for the dry season in Cambodia.
He added that this option was more expensive than other options, but could soon consume energy while Cambodia waited for the completion of other sources under construction.
He stressed that the lack of energy in the dry season due to abnormal hot weather and high energy demand after the 2018 election.
Please be informed that on March 14, 2019, through Fresh News, Mr. Keo Rattanak called on the people to kindly understand and tolerate the shortage of electricity supply, which is disrupted in some areas due to the dry season. The weather is getting hotter and the demand for electricity is getting worse.
He also called on people to use electricity sparingly to help reduce some of the volume, while Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has been working urgently to find additional sources of electricity.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that due to the unusually high heat of this year's dry season, including investment in all sectors very fast after the election, the electricity supply has encountered problems and this dry season, hydropower is not. There is a lot of running water to help generate electricity, so wait until it rains again.
"The solution in front of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has been working hard to negotiate with neighboring countries to buy electricity this dry season, and also called for understanding and call on people to save on electricity consumption," he said.
Currently, the Royal Government team is negotiating more hydropower projects and new transmission projects, while EDC itself is negotiating to increase the supply from Thailand and Vietnam.
