Japan Provides Nearly $ 300,000 Grant to Three Local Development Organizations in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has provided a grant of $ 275,296 to three entities in Cambodia under the Japan Economic Cooperation Scheme for a small-scale humanitarian security project.
The signing ceremony for the grant was held on March 15, 2019 at the Embassy of Japan, in which the Japanese side was represented by Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia and representatives of three units.
The three currently signed projects include:
* First, the road improvement project in Totong commune, Dang Tong district, Kampot province, with a budget of 106,146 USD, and the grant unit of the Department of Rural Development of Kampot province, in this project, two old bridges will be replaced by concrete box drainage. Two in Totong commune, Dang Tong district, Kampot province.
The project is expected to benefit about 155,800 people in the region. It is also expected that the improved road will make it easier for local people to travel to schools, hospitals and markets, and especially boost people's economic activity by improving connectivity in the region. .
* Second: Road improvement project in Da commune, Chit Borey district, Kratie province, with a budget of $ 82,450, Kratie Provincial Department of Rural Development. In this project, a 15-meter bridge will be built in Dar commune, Chit Borei district. Currently, people are using wooden bridges that are prone to collapse after the old concrete drain was destroyed by floods. The project is expected to benefit about 3,800 people in the region.
Please be informed that Japan's Kusanoni Grant Project started in Cambodia in 1991 to support Cambodia's efforts to develop and rebuild the country at the grassroots level. The aid program aims to protect vulnerable people from a number of factors, such as poverty and misfortune, which can directly threaten their livelihoods, livelihoods and dignity, as well as promote people's self-reliance. Community.
