Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "For 2019-2023, the Republic of Korea will continue to provide a total of 700 million US dollars in concessional loans, which our two governments have just signed a coordination agreement on the concessional loan framework of the Cooperation Fund. "Economic development a little earlier."
The Prime Minister of Cambodia added that the Republic of Korea's cooperation financing has focused on infrastructure, water resources and public welfare, education and human resource training, and rural development, including the establishment of civil aviation training centers, national road rehabilitation projects. No. 2 and National Road No. 22.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked the Korean government and people for their continued involvement in the restoration and development of Cambodia through financing, cooperation and direct investment. Cambodia and the Republic of Korea have had good relations for a long time, but this relationship was temporarily suspended due to the civil war in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo further emphasized that the diplomatic relations were re-established on October 30, 1997 after Samdech paid a state visit to the Republic of Korea in July 1996 and decided to resume relations. Diplomacy between the two countries.
He said that since the resumption of ties, the friendship and bilateral cooperation between the two countries have steadily developed, which should be proud of the political, economic and social as reflected through the visit. The return of the leaders of the two countries, the growth of people-to-people contacts, and the growth of trade, investment and tourism.
It should be noted that in the framework of cooperation financing from 1996 to 2018, the Government of the Republic of Korea provided about 632 million US dollars, of which 300 million US dollars in grants.
