Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) opens construction site for 500 kV high voltage transmission line from Stung Treng to Laos to meet domestic electricity demand
(Stung Treng): Electricité du Cambodge (EDC) on March 15, 2019 opened the construction site of a 500 kV high voltage transmission line from Stung Treng to Laos to meet local electricity demand. This was confirmed by Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge to Fresh News on the afternoon of March 15, 2019.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that the first step is that Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) is preparing to connect to a voltage of 230 kV to prepare for electricity from Laos in early 2021. Separately, the construction site for the construction of a 500 kV high voltage transmission line in the first phase, EDC will have a 230 kV transmission line.
Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has signed an agreement with Electricite du Laos (EDL) to purchase an additional 200 megawatts of electricity from Laos in early 2021 to address the country's fastest-growing domestic demand.
The Director General confirmed that the measures to buy electricity from Laos, especially as Cambodia awaits the completion of the construction of a 700-megawatt coal-fired power plant in Sihanoukville by 2024 and a 240-megawatt solar power plant. Watts, which will be launched continuously from the middle of this year onwards.
At the same time, in the dry season, when the weather is unusually hot, the director-general called on people to use electricity sparingly and asked for understanding for the disruption of electricity supply. Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: "Adoption of technology by the private sector and the government will be a place to increase productivity and economic transformation"
