Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Mines and Energy of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Energy of the Republic of Korea on Power Supply Project for Miniature Power Networks and Charging Stations in Cambodia signed by Minister Suy Sem Ministry of Mines and Energy of Cambodia and Mr. Song Yoon-mo, Minister of Commerce, Industry and Energy of Korea.
5: Memorandum of Understanding between the Royal Academy of Cambodia and the National Research Council for the Humanities and Sociology of the Republic of Korea signed by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Mr. Song Kyung Ryeong, President of the National Research Council for the Humanities Economics And Korean Social Sciences.
Ministry of Public Works Organizes Road Safety Education for Road Users in Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport has organized education and dissemination on road safety to about 50 people from 4 villages: Chi Prang village, Top Talat village, Chok Kandol village and Kork Penh village in Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province. On both sides of National Road 53, which connects National Road 5 to National Road 44 at Chiep Commune Hall.
The event was presided over by Mr. Ou Sereyvuth, Coordinating Officer of the Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Pea Kimvong, Road Safety Advisor of the Road Improvement Project of the Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and Mrs. Hem Kien, Chief of Chiep Commune Chief, also.
During the opening ceremony of the campaign, Mr. Oum Serey Vuth stated that traffic accidents are a concern of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Nearly 2,000 people.
Mr. Oum Serey Vuth said that almost every year, Cambodia loses more than 300 million US dollars due to traffic accidents, seeing this problem, the Road Construction Unit of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is really concerned about the safety of road users. Roads are being improved now.
In particular, the main causes of accidents are human factors, which account for up to 95%, including speeding, driving after drinking, overtaking in a dangerous situation, turning left-right carelessly. Respect the right of way and disregard for vehicle technical issues.
Seeing these challenges, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, through the Road Construction Unit (MPU3), conducted road safety education and dissemination to people living along the project road. This program will continue until before the traditional Khmer New Year, during each New Year, the number of accidents as well as the number of deaths has increased dramatically.
Mr. Oum Sereyvuth added that at the end of the training, T-shirts and helmets were also provided to the participants for the safety of using motorcycles, as the number of people killed and injured by motorcycles is now worrying. .
Mr. Pea Kim Vong, Advisor of Road Safety Program, also stated that the purpose of this education and dissemination is to organize education and dissemination on road safety at this time in order to participate in preventing and reducing road traffic accidents. Which is threatening the lives of road users and hindering the development of the country.
Mr. Pa Kimvong added that the program will continue to educate people living along the road, including students at schools along the road.
