(Pailin): A woman almost cried while walking to open a reserve stall to sell as usual, suddenly found a lot of luggage in her stall lost after the thieves locked and locked.
The burglary occurred at 6: 3 am on March 15, 2019 in Samaki Market called Pahi in Pahi Cheung Village, Pailin Sangkat, Pailin City.
According to the coffee seller, at 1:10 AM on March 15, two suspects were seen dragging a cart with all their belongings, but thought it was scrap metal. They dragged the cart with the luggage on the motorcycle and fled in the shadows.
According to the victim, Meas Srey, her stall was already locked using a normal lock, and when she came to lock in the morning as usual, she lost all her belongings.
He did not agree to file a complaint to the security guards or the market manager to find a solution for him because the security guards did not seem to pay good attention to the guards.
