This statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and South Korean President Moon Jae-in hosted a luncheon on the occasion of the Cambodia-Korea Business Forum in Phnom Penh on March 15, 2019 at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to call on the private sector and Korean investors who have not yet come to Cambodia to come and learn about the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia and decide to invest to develop Cambodia with. We will make the most of the achievements of all these collaborations. ”
"Cambodia is the most open country in the region, allowing foreign investors, including Korean investors, to invest in all areas as well as local investors," he said.
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, added that recently, in order to enhance competitiveness, promote economic diversification and improve the business and investment environment in Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to introduce in-depth reform measures to reduce costs and operating costs. . The Royal Government considers the private sector to be the engine of economic growth and a real partner in the development of the country.
Samdech Techo further stated that on March 29, 2019, Samdech will lead the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum at the Peace Palace, on which occasion Samdech will set out some sharp measures: Increase the competitiveness of the Cambodian economy, 2: Improve and enhance the investment and business environment, 3: Diversify the national economy and create more quality jobs for Cambodian workers.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, I would like to ensure that all investors have a favorable environment, especially peace, security and political stability, as well as macro-economic stability, legal framework and effective institutions. "Transparency, accountability and predictability."
Please be informed that Korean investment in Cambodia has 212 projects with a total investment of $ 4.56 billion from 1994 to 2018.
