Mr. Pech Sokha, Member and Deputy Secretary General of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council, made the remarks while attending a workshop on disseminating programs and methods to assess the impact of legal documents held at the University. Chea Sim Kamchay Mear, Kampong Cham province, this morning, March 15, 2019.
Mr. Pech Sokha stated, "Every country needs laws and regulations to govern society and the economy harmoniously, but we must also be careful about the negative effects of those laws and regulations, such as barriers to competition or competition." "Put unnecessary costs on business and the public, etc."
On that occasion, Mr. Pech Sokha added that during the drafting of laws and regulations, ministries and institutions must study and thoroughly assess the potential impact of these laws or regulations.
In this sense, he said, a thorough analysis and consideration of the costs and benefits of laws or regulations is essential for reporting to management, which is the basis for deciding whether to create other laws or regulations. Or which option is better?
