The French Embassy organizes "Two Weeks France in Phnom Penh" to Celebrate and Strengthen Franco-Cambodian Friendship
(Phnom Penh): The French-Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry, the French Embassy in Cambodia and the French Institute in Cambodia will jointly organize a "Two-Week French Program in Phnom Penh" from March 18 to 30, 2019 to promote French culture. And Cambodia, as well as strengthening partnerships and exchanges between the two countries by introducing the public to a wide range of cultural and economic events.
According to the announcement of the French Embassy in Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on March 15, 2019, it was confirmed that the "Two Weeks France in Phnom Penh" program, all participants can explore creativity, liveliness. French skills and talents.
The first week of the program will coincide with Francophone Day. A variety of events will be held to promote the use of the French language in Cambodia, including poetry camp at more than 15 partner institutions, including:
The second week will begin with a demonstration of modern cooking at the Food Institute of Cambodia. In addition, there will be a panel discussion on the topic of sustainable urban development as an opportunity for experts to discuss urban planning in Cambodia.
The two-week French program in Phnom Penh will conclude on Saturday, March 30, with the organization of a "French market" on the campus of the French Embassy in Phnom Penh, with more than 50 booths on display.
From 10 a.m. to 6 p.m., the Embassy will be open to the public who wish to attend a French food tasting exhibition and enjoy a variety of entertainment activities (such as sports activities, cooking lessons with celebrity chefs, spectacle views). Small presentations and play areas for children, etc.
The French Embassy in Cambodia confirms that the French Market is an opportunity to learn about French culture and products, as well as the skills of French entrepreneurs in Cambodia, mixed with Cambodian skills and traditions.
