Announcing the appointment of Kampong Thom Provincial Customs and Excise Manager, Mr. Ly Bunsong to replace Mr. Thong Sokhamphou
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chhun Chhon, Chairman of Kampong Thom Provincial Council, Mr. Sok Lou, Provincial Governor and Mr. Tha Eng Veng, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, announced the transfer of duties of the Chief of Kampong Thom Customs and Excise Department.
The handover ceremony of the Chief of Kampong Thom Customs and Excise Office was also attended by many Deputy Heads of Departments. Mr. Ly Bunsong has been appointed by the management of Kampong Thom Provincial Customs and Excise Department to replace Mr. Thong Sokhamphou, who has been transferred to be the Director of the National Customs Office with the same rank as the Director of the Department.
Mr. Ly Bunsong is committed to lead the strengthening of the quality of the Kampong Thom Customs Branch to further improve in response to the trust of the management and maintain a strong internal unity to effectively collect revenue. Taxes as planned, especially the suppression of illegal tax evasion and commitment to solve challenges, continue to cooperate with relevant authorities at the local level.
Mr. Tha Eng Veng thanked the Armed Forces, local authorities and relevant authorities for their support and cooperation with customs officials in fulfilling their duties and responsibilities. In particular, the customs is not only responsible for collecting taxes, but also facilitating the flow of trade, both domestically and internationally, and protecting social security.
He said that the customs has collected more than 2,500 million dollars in the past 5 years, an increase of more than two and a half times, plus the revenue of the General Department of Taxation in 2018 revenue of nearly 5 billion dollars. At the same time, he instructed the new chairman to draw on the experience of the old chairman in various geographies and ask the customs officials to strictly follow the nine points of advice of the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Lou sincerely hoped that the new President would fulfill his commitment to the mechanism of collecting customs duties, preventing the evasion of various goods, including the crackdown, which must cooperate with the Chairman of the Municipal Unity Command, the director of the provincial unit. To get good results, because the customs sector is an important source of income for the salaries of civil servants, we have to rely on ourselves.
The new chairman must cooperate with the partners of the unit, the internal unity within the unit must strive to fulfill its roles and responsibilities, fill the gaps and cooperate with all officials.
The provincial governor also thanked the ladies and gentlemen who participated now to strengthen and implement their work better and know how to work together in solidarity to develop progress.
