National Bank of Cambodia Officially Launches National Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing Strategy
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia on March 14, 2019 officially launched the National Strategy on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing 2019-2023.
The inauguration ceremony was attended by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Coordinating Committee for Combating Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing (OCSC), Mr. Chive Scott, Advisor. Senior members of the International Monetary Fund, as well as many National Bank officials.
The implementation of the National Strategy for Combating Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing aims to:
1. Financial institutions and non-financial occupations and professions to avoid being used to launder money and seek the benefits of crimes and assets related to terrorist financing.
2. Ensure that all law enforcement authorities jointly investigate, prosecute, punish and confiscate the proceeds and tools of criminal prosecution and money laundering and terrorist financing effectively.
Mr. Chea Chanto outlined the 10 key strategic objectives of the National Strategy and the work activities, setting priorities and specific timelines that the relevant ministries and institutions must work together with the private sector to achieve the effectiveness of the anti-money laundering system. And terrorist financing in Cambodia.
He added that especially in response to the national risk of anti-money laundering and terrorist financing, which was assessed in 2016 and the recommendations set out in the 2017 Assessment Report on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing.
Please be informed that the Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing (CPF) has co-developed the National Strategy on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing 2019-2023 under the guidance of It will have technical assistance from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to serve as a full-fledged long-term guide for the Royal Government of Cambodia.
