The visit is aimed at boosting bilateral ties and expanding cooperation in various fields, including boosting trade between the two countries. Two happened in sequence.
In 2009, the trade volume between the two countries amounted to more than 218 million US dollars in Cambodia, more than 93 million US dollars to Korea and more than 209 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2010, the trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea was more than 272 million dollars, of which Cambodia exported to Korea, the amount dropped to just over 24 million dollars, while Korea imported more than 244 million dollars to Cambodia.
In 2011, the trade volume of the two countries was more than 346 million US dollars in Cambodia, more than 46 million US dollars exported to Korea, while Korea imported 300 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2012, the trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea was more than 493 million US dollars, Cambodia exported more than 70 million US dollars, while Korea imported 422 million US dollars.
In 2013, the trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea was more than 464 million US dollars, Cambodia exported more than 94 million US dollars to Korea, while Korea imported 369 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2014, the trade volume of the two countries was more than 513 million US dollars in Cambodia, more than 123 million US dollars exported to Korea, while Korea imported 390 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2015, the trade volume of Cambodia-South Korea amounted to more than 596 million US dollars in Cambodia, exported more than 137 million US dollars to Korea, while Korea imported 459 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2016, the trade volume of the two countries was more than 602 million US dollars in Cambodia, more than 164 million US dollars to Korea, while Korea imported 438 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2017, the trade volume of Cambodia-South Korea amounted to more than 625 million US dollars, Cambodia exported more than 169 million US dollars, while Korea imported 455 million US dollars to Cambodia.
In 2018, the trade volume of the two countries is more than 746 million dollars in Cambodia, exports to Korea more than 202 million dollars, while Korea imports back to Cambodia more than 543 million dollars.
Cambodia's exports to South Korea include clothing, electronics, footwear, beverages, rubber bags, medicines and cardboard. While most of Cambodia's imports from Korea are textiles, trucks, beverages, electronics, machinery, home decor, medicines, soaps and plastics. Cambodian beer exports to foreign markets increase by 30%!
