Minister Thong Khon: The 5th River Festival is an opportunity for Kampong Chhnang to win the ASEAN Clean Cities
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that the organization of the 5th River Festival in Kampong Chhnang is an opportunity for the city of Kampong Chhnang to inspire the movement that can lead to winning the "ASEAN Clean Tourism City. The second will help further national prestige on the international stage.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to nominate six cities to participate in the second "Clean ASEAN Tourism City" competition, including Kampong Cham, Pursat, Kampong Chhnang, Takhmao, Kampot and Daun Penh. The second ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities Award is scheduled to be announced at the ASEAN Tourism Forum (ATF) in early January 2020 in Brunei Darussalam.
In the workshop to celebrate the 5th River Festival under the theme "River Connected: Peace, People and Tourism" accompanied by the award ceremony for businesses in the field of tourism in Kampong Chhnang on March 14, 2019. Minister Thong Khon said that "the river festival is an opportunity for Kampong Chhnang to strive to promote all kinds of movements to make this city a winner of ASEAN clean city."
He added that Siem Reap and Battambang have already won the ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities for the first time, but this award is only once every three years, and now the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to place four cities and one district. Candidates for the Clean ASEAN Cities in 2020, including Kampong Cham, Takhmao, Daun Penh, Pursat and Kampong Chhnang.
He stressed that the province of Kampong Chhnang to host the River Festival is like preparing to win the "ASEAN Clean Tourism City". He praised that Kampong Chhnang is a beautiful city, well-structured, has a good culture and history, especially the remains of buildings from the French colonial period, with large trees, although the city is a bit small.
