(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Thursday, March 14, 2019, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2018 and Raise the work direction for the new year 2019 of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
The closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work as well as the new work direction of the Ministry of Agriculture was held at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Agriculture has been a key sector in supporting Cambodia's economy in the past.
* The Prime Minister stated that promoting the growth of the agricultural sector remains the main goal to ensure food security, nutrition and exports. In particular, Cambodia's agro-industrial crop production has increased significantly due to the increase in demand from the international market as well as the increase in investment in agro-industry.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, continued that the development of the agricultural sector is an important duty of the Royal Government to strengthen the role of the agricultural sector, create jobs, ensure food security, reduce poverty and develop rural areas. Overall, the agricultural sector provided employment opportunities up to 41.5%.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges the modernization of competitive agriculture by promoting research to develop modern agricultural technologies and techniques in order to increase quantity, quality and nutrition, promote the use of new agricultural technologies digitally, and strengthen crop management. Agriculture and better agricultural inputs.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded to continue to promote investment in the agricultural sector through the public-private partnership approach to establish agro-processing zones for export, which will help solve the problem of farmers' markets and opening up. Expanding the mechanism for implementing "contract agricultural production" even more widely. With this, investment must be encouraged to build agricultural wholesale markets and promote agricultural markets to farmers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the processing of rice for export is still limited, making it impossible for Cambodia to achieve the goal of exporting one million tons of rice per year. On the other hand, it is difficult to compete with rice in the market because Cambodian rice production is more expensive than some other rice exporting countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered all relevant ministries and institutions to find ways to reduce production costs to increase competitiveness.
* Samdech Techo stated that it is a matter of pride for Cambodia that the use of machinery in the agricultural sector has increased, but it must also be seen that the use of machinery and machinery has increased the cost of production.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that if the increase in the use of machinery in the agricultural sector and lead farmers to stop raising animals, both for dragging and for selling meat is also a challenge for farmers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to solve this agricultural problem, it requires the participation of all relevant ministries, not just one Ministry of Agriculture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on billionaires in Cambodia to invest in Cambodia's agricultural sector.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated to his critics that they did what they could under the leadership of Samdech, not to mention the positivity of the leadership. But he always tried to insult and criticize Samdech.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged to continue to improve the quality of crop production, animal husbandry, aquaculture and the safety of agricultural products. Use negotiation mechanisms with countries that buy agricultural products from Cambodia to international markets. Must participate in strengthening food safety in the direction of ensuring and improving the safety of consumers better.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister continues to urge to continue to train and disseminate rubber technology to more rubber farmers to continue to expand the family rubber community for the benefit of farmers when selling rubber products. Continue to encourage investment in rubber processing to increase value added, create jobs and reduce poverty.
* Samdech Techo stated that it is not possible to use the policy of subsidizing investors because it is against the rules of the World Trade Organization.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Ministry of Agriculture to continue educating the people not to change their crops by running according to changes in product prices in the market.
* The Prime Minister stated that it is necessary to jointly strengthen international cooperation with neighboring countries and development partners in the bilateral, multilateral and regional and sub-regional frameworks to mobilize new financial and technical assistance. In addition, to modernize Cambodian agriculture to contribute more to the national economy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to push for the use of existing market mechanisms to decide on Cambodia's rice exports.
* The Prime Minister stated that this evening, Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit will have a family meal with the President of South Korea and his wife.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in a meeting with the President of South Korea, Samdech will discuss additional markets for Cambodian products in South Korea.
* Samdech Techo also confirmed that this year, Samdech will travel to some Asian and European countries to find markets for Cambodian products.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia can not live by the requirements of any country. Samdech Techo said that Cambodia is proud of the progress, but also to continue to work together to solve other challenges.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen finished his speech at 9:35 a.m. the same day, thank you for watching the live broadcast.
71 Families with Disabilities thanked Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for their continuous encouragement, love and support
(Phnom Penh): At the head office on the morning of Thursday, March 14, 2019, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, decided to provide humanitarian donations. Eighth to the Organization for Action on Youth with Disabilities for Development, which has 71 members with disabilities living in Phnom Penh and from some provinces.
During the meeting, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, conveyed the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent greetings, love, encouragement and appreciation to all the disabled people who struggled. Every obstacle in life strives according to their respective skills, virtuous and moral.
This is part of the participation of the Royal Government of Cambodia in implementing the national policy to promote people with disabilities to live on an equal footing in a society of peace, stability and development.
At the same time, she brought the advice of Samdech Kittipritthbandit to all people with disabilities to increase contact with relevant institutions or philanthropists to ask permission or co-organize concerts on the occasion of festivals such as the Royal River Festival. Water Festival, etc., because this opportunity will be attended by many people, which will enable people with disabilities to receive more support.
People with disabilities also pray for Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to be healthy and live a long life to continue to lead the Cambodian ship to be more prosperous and peaceful.
Donations provided to Action for the Disabled Youth for Development include: rice, noodles, fish, pure water, orange juice, fish sauce, soy sauce and 5 million riels. Separately, each of the 71 disabled people received: 30 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish, 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket, 1 sarong, 1 scarf, 1 T-shirt and 50,000 Riels.
It should be noted that the Cambodian Red Cross has already donated food, materials and funds, as well as supported the charity concert program of the Organization for Action for the Disabled Youth for Development 7 times, which today is the 8th time. .
