Nop Heng, director of the Sihanoukville Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, said that the 104-meter road to be rehabilitated is 1,300 meters long, 7 meters wide, reinforced with reinforced concrete and has drainage on both sides. This road costs the state budget, while the cost of installing sewers on both sides is the contribution of the province and the people on the streets. Report: US does not recognize Golan Heights belonging to Israel
