Phnom Penh Traffic Police Office Holds 2-Day Training Course for Trainees to Prevent and Improve Traffic Safety
(Phnom Penh): Colonel Sem Kunthea, Director of the Land Traffic Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, this morning, March 14, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of a two-day training course focusing on control. Check for alcohol, international driving licenses, exercises on force discipline and first aid to prevent and improve the legal aspects of road safety.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Representative of an organization of Singapore, Colonel Thi Visal from the General Department of Traffic Order, Ministry of Interior, Deputy Inspector in charge of traffic planning of 12 districts and Mr. Traffic and some other relevant officials.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Sem said that this two-day short training course is very important for professional officers to pay attention to the implementation of the streets, focusing on alcohol control, card control. International driving, exercise discipline, force and first aid in times of trouble to prevent and improve the law of road safety more effectively.
Minister of Public Works Inspects National Road No. 71C in Chamkar Leu and Stung Trang Districts, Kampong Cham Province
(Phnom Penh): This morning, March 14, 2019, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, led a team to inspect National Road No. 71C in Chamkar Leu Village, Stung Trang District, Kampong Cham Province.
On the occasion of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inspecting Street 71C, there were also the participation of relevant officials, including many authorities. Cattle consumption in agriculture fell to 3.2%, while mechanization increased to 96.86%
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sokhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presented a report that in 2018, the use of cattle in agriculture has decreased to 3.2 percent while plowing and cultivating. Rainfed rice by agricultural machinery accounted for more than 96.86%.
This is according to the report of the Minister of Agriculture revealed on March 14, 2019 at the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2018 and the work direction of the new year 2019 of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries under the chairmanship. His Excellency Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
According to the Ministry of Agriculture, "The evolution of agricultural modernization is increasing significantly. In 2018, the plowing and cultivating of rain-fed rice by agricultural machinery accounted for more than 96.86%, which is a factor. One facilitates the decline of the rural labor force compared to the total labor force, while the use of cattle is 3.2%.
As of 2018, the Ministry has established 1,116 agricultural communities, of which 120 communities are being promoted by professional units to become model and agro-business communities. At the same time, the Ministry has produced 187,876 tons of rice seeds and 25 tons of horticultural seeds for use and prepared for disaster relief.
He added that in 2018, the processing of freshwater and marine fisheries reached 84,000 tons and the export of fresh and processed fisheries reached more than 14,000 tons.
Separately, more than 3,200 cases of fishery crimes were cracked down by the Ministry of Cooperation, compared to 2017, there was a decrease of 721 cases. Meanwhile, Mr. Veng Sakhon said that in 2018, the Ministry has established 516 fishing communities, of which 27 communities are becoming ecotourism communities.
Among them, there are 475 freshwater fishing communities and 41 marine fishing communities, with a total of more than 332,000 community members. There are a total of 665 fisheries conservation areas nationwide and 884 community fish ponds have been established.
The Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces tells all officers to be loyal to the nation, religion, the King and to strictly abide by the rules and regulations as the core force for the defense of national independence.
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of Thursday, the 9th day of the month of Phalkun, in the year of Samreth Sak. On March 14, 2019, at the Army Institute, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, presided over the closing ceremony of the seventh generation of Army Officers Training Course, entitled " "Jan 7 Army" with a total of 207 trainees.
The ceremony was attended by the Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Ministry of National Defense and His Excellency the Commander-in-Chief of the Ministry.
On that occasion, the Commander-in-Chief also thanked the Armed Forces of the People's Republic of China, which has always provided substantial support for socio-economic development, especially Chinese investment, which ranks first in the country. Cambodia, which is the foundation for building and developing a prosperous nation.
In addition, the Chinese side has provided a lot of support for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be able to build and strengthen its capacity, especially to enable the training of young resources to become potential turnover resources.
However, the activities of the Golden Dragon Exercise and Exercise 2019 on a bilateral basis between Cambodia and China are a testament to the participation in training to gain experience and strengthen professional skills to another level.
On the occasion of the ceremony, Commander-in-Chief Vong Pisen brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense to the leaders, officers, deputies and soldiers of the Institute. Infantry and all trainees.
At the ceremony, General Vong Pisen advised all trainees to be loyal to the nation, religion, and the King to strictly abide by the general rules and regulations of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the regulations of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense and the General. Commands assigned to merit as officers trained by the Higher Institute, a core force of national defense.
On the other hand, continue to study in all forms, both skills and foreign languages, and grasp new situations to better understand the types of information. In addition, to strengthen the bonds of solidarity and unity within the unit, as well as to know how to organize, maintain, repair and maintain weapons and ammunition in accordance with the technical specifications. Former tycoon Ho Chamroeun sent to court for further questioning in connection with fraud case
It should be noted that on the morning of February 14, 2019, the Court of Appeal held a hearing to announce the verdict in the case of the former tycoon Ho Chamroeun involved two crimes: fraud and embezzlement and decided not to allow the former tycoon Ho Chamroeun was released on bail and will remain in prison under the jurisdiction of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Court has sentenced the former tycoon to 18 months in prison for threatening to shoot his wife at his mansion in Dangkor district.
It should be noted that the former Duke Ho Chamroeun was arrested by the police of the Bureau of Minor Offenses of the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of May 15, 2018, in connection with the shooting of nearly 10 people on April 21. 2018 ago at a villa in Prey Sar village, Sangkat Prey Sar, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
