Parachute carrying more than 7 and a half tons of chemicals from Vietnam into Cambodia was caught by the police on the road
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Economic Crimes Police Department of the National Police in collaboration with the General Department of CamControl on March 13 cracked down on the import of more than 7 and a half tons of shrimp and seafood containing chemicals at km 15 National No. 3 while transporting three cars from Vietnam.
The operation was carried out on the recommendation of General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, and was based on the investigation of professional officers under the coordination of the procedure by Mr. Kham Sophary, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
After inspecting the three vehicles, the joint police force actually found 376 cases of shrimp (shrimp with jelly-like substance in the shrimp head) and some seafood without permission, equivalent to about 7 , 520 kg.
For all of the above exhibits, Deputy Prosecutor Kham Sophary decided to temporarily confiscate them at the department (taking some of the exhibits to be tested for banned substances) and then ordered the shrimp with the chemical injection as described. The other side was burned at the Boeung Jing Ek landfill in the evening of the same day.
Three car drivers were brought in for questioning at the department to find the owner to continue the legal process. The King issued a Royal Decree ordering the promotion of two officers to the rank of lieutenant general.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree ordering the promotion of two lieutenant generals, including Lieutenant General Ouk Dara and Lieutenant General Chhoeun Kosal Virak. This is according to the Royal Decree appointed by Fresh News on the evening of March 13, 2019.
