Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Receives Outgoing EU Ambassador
During the meeting, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia for the contribution of the European Union in the development process of Cambodia in the past, and Samdech also said that although recently the relationship between Cambodia. - Europe faces some challenges, but the prince hopes that things will be resolved and relations will be restored.
Mr. George Edgar also thanked Prince Sar Kheng for facilitating his work in Cambodia for more than three years, and said that although some EU projects were Suspended, but he was pleased that Europe continued to support decentralization and deconcentration reforms in Cambodia.
The EU Ambassador said that while working in Cambodia, he really saw the progress of Cambodia compared to 20 years ago. He expressed his appreciation for the good results and the organization of the civil society forum with the government, which made the civil society organization and the government better understand each other.
In response, the Prime Minister also thanked the European Union for its assistance in decentralization and deconcentration reforms, and hoped that the EU would continue to support this work, especially as Cambodia begins to transfer key functions and sectors. Some to the sub-national level.
