Notice! The National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants will pay the first two weeks of Social Security for March for retirees and former civil servants from March 14 onwards.
(Phnom Penh): The National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation will pay the Social Security Fund for March 2019 and the pension policy for March 2019 for the first two weeks to retirees and former officials. Civil service from March 14, 2019 onwards through Canadia Bank and ACLEDA Bank in 25 capitals and provinces nationwide.
According to the announcement of the National Social Security Fund for Civil Servants, obtained by Fresh News on March 13, 2019, "Social Security Policy Funds and Social Security Supplements for Retirees and People "Loss of professional fitness for March 2019 for the first two weeks will be open from March 14, 2019 onwards."
For the above social security payment, all retirees and former civil servants must bring their account book and Cambodian ID card or ATM card to use at ATMs of the above partner banks throughout the country.
The statement from the Royal Government spokesman came after Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen told his lawyer to file a complaint against anyone who insulted him via Facebook.
The spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia informed all compatriots, as well as the media and non-governmental organizations about the case of incitement and insult to the life of Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia, which arose out of the will and choice of the people: It is against the law. The Royal Government, as well as the Armed Forces of all kinds and levels, has an absolute obligation to protect by force as well as by law.
According to the statement, "The Royal Government does not condone such acts or activities as described above, because those acts are an act that affects the national security and the choice of the Cambodian people and those acts are not right. Recognized as a political right or freedom of expression. "The Office of the Spokesman calls on the public to stay away from this systematically assigned insurgency."
In the past, for the sake of harmony and dignity in Cambodian society, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked all Facebook users to stop insulting each other. Continuing as well.
According to Article 307 of the Penal Code (the offense of public insult), "every insult, every insult, or every insult without blaming an act is an insult." This means that if an individual or group uses inappropriate words, such as swearing or insulting an individual or group, without intention of blaming an act, it is an insult.
Public blasphemy is a criminal offense that is punishable by a fine and only punishable. The relevant institution is a necessary condition for the prosecution of a criminal offense, and the prosecution is also dismissed by the withdrawal of the complaint of the relevant party or the relevant institution.
