Notice! A group of volunteer doctors, Mr. Hun Many, inspected and treated patients in Preah Vihear province for free on March 17.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, issued a notice to all people in Preah Vihear Province to visit for free medical treatment by a group of volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many on March 17. The coming 2019.
Through the notification letter of Preah Vihear Provincial Administration, which was received by Fresh News this morning, March 14, 2019, it informed the people all over the province, especially the people of Rovieng district, to go for free medical treatment. From the team of volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many, on March 17, 2019, in the area of Robiep Primary School, Robeab Commune, Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, from 7 am to 3 pm.
Specific diseases to be treated include: general disease, mental illness, general pediatric disease, gynecological diseases, hemorrhoids, pulmonary diseases, gastrointestinal diseases, respiratory diseases, digestive diseases, dermatitis, pruritus, anemia, rheumatism, hepatitis, sexually transmitted diseases. Malaria, dengue fever, eye disease, oral health, diabetes, heart disease, hypertension, ear, nose, throat, kidney disease, ultrasound, wound healing and minor surgery, etc.
Please note that the volunteer doctors, Mr. HUN Many are all doctors from abroad and in the country in public and private hospitals with many years of experience. For this reason, government officials, the armed forces and the people to receive free medical treatment for everyone. Minister of Agriculture presents his achievements in 2018
(Phnom Penh): On March 14, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of the old year 2018 and the work direction of the new year 2019 of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. The closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work as well as the new work direction of the Ministry of Agriculture was held at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
On this occasion, Mr. Veng Sokhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presented the report on the achievements of the Ministry, so that in 2018, the work of cultivating rice throughout the country reached 3.34 million hectares, equivalent to 113 % Of the plan, including 2.75 million hectares of wet rice and 590 thousand hectares of dry season rice. The area under rice cultivation has increased by about 4% compared to 2017.
Another special point is that the Prime Minister made great efforts to push for the signing of a memorandum of understanding with China to increase the export quota of 400,000 tons of rice with Vietnam and 300,000 tons with Vietnam. In one year and to other countries, I sincerely hope that the relevant ministries and institutions will work hard to promote the export of rice, which is the "white gold" of Cambodia to achieve the expected goals.
For natural rubber production in 2018 reached more than 436 thousand hectares, of which agro-industrial rubber accounted for more than 275 thousand hectares, accounting for 63% and family rubber accounted for 161 thousand hectares, accounting for 37% of the total rubber area. 202 thousand hectares of rubber plantations were applied, an increase of 19% over 2017. Rubber production reached 220,000 tons, an increase of 14% over 2017.
According to the joint assessment, meat production and supply is increasing every year, from 224 thousand tons in 2017 to 231 thousand tons in 2018, an increase of more than 3%, which reduces the import of meat for domestic supply. Down from 57 thousand tons in 2017 to only 54 thousand tons in 2018.
