(Koh Kong): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, on the occasion of accompanying a meeting with workers in Koh Kong province with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, inspected two freshwater sources to solve For lack of water for people living in Khemarak Phoumin and Mondul Seima districts.
Accompanying Samdech Pich Sena yesterday afternoon were Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry and Handicrafts, Koh Kong Provincial Governor Mithona Phuthong, and Tycoon Ly Yong Phat, Director General of Koh Kong Water Supply Company, and other officials.
Two freshwater sources are in the Tapon waterfall area and the Seila Meanchey resort area, which is expected to pump enough water to the reservoir to distribute water to the people.
During the search for fresh water sources, Mr. Cham Prasidh said that during this period, the drought season caused the water source that used to be used to dry up almost completely. According to direct research, what is a big problem is that the freshwater dam used at Tapon Waterfall is not able to maintain the amount of water during the rainy season, so there is a severe water crisis.
The Minister of Industry and Handicrafts has urged Tycoon Ly Yong Phat's water supply company in Koh Kong to speed up the repair of the Tapon Dam to prevent further technical errors. When completed, this dam will be able to receive 2 million cubic meters, which can meet the needs of the people enough in the future.
But at this time, it is difficult to solve, that is, the authorities and departments continue to buy tanks or water to give to people who are temporarily short of water until the rainy season arrives. Regarding the long-term settlement mechanism, the Minister of Industry will raise this issue with the head of government on what should be done next.
