(Phnom Penh): The Police Force of the Land Traffic Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police this morning, March 13, 2019, launched a campaign to seize more than 40 heavy vehicles that entered the city at the wrong time according to the authorities' decision. .
Mr. Sem Kunthea, Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Road Traffic Bureau, told Fresh News that under the order of the Phnom Penh Municipal Governor and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, today his forces launched a campaign to seize more than 40 trucks on the road. Forty of these vehicles drove into the city at the wrong time. Authorities do not allow heavy vehicles to enter the city from 6 to 9 am and from 4 pm to 8 pm.
For these cars, Mr. Sem Kunthea told the car owners to verify the car documents and re-contract to enter the city. It should be noted that the campaign to seize the truck was carried out after yesterday in Stung Meanchey, there was public criticism of a truck crashed into, causing the tragic death of a woman, the public blamed the authorities And the authorities allow trucks to enter the city at the wrong time.
