25 Ministries-Institutions Meet to Determine Specific Functions for Transfer to Municipal-District Administration
(Phnom Penh): Twenty-five professional ministries and institutions of the Royal Government on March 13, 2019 started a discussion meeting to identify specific functions and resources in each sector of the Ministry to integrate specialized offices into the management structure. Municipal-district administration in accordance with the principles of unified administration.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Ngan Chamroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Secretariat of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development (NCDD) in collaboration with the Secretariat for Public Administration Reform and the General Secretariat for Reform. Public financial management.
Representatives of the National League of Local Councils, a mechanism for representing the voice and protecting the legitimate interests of municipal, district, Khan and commune councils, were also present at the meeting.
Mr. Ngan Chamroeun stated that assigning specific functions and resources in each sector to the municipal administration in accordance with the new structure and management system is a necessary and priority task to ensure the improvement of efficiency and accountability in fulfillment. Roles and responsibilities of the municipal administration as the local administration in providing public services and local development to meet the needs of the people in its jurisdiction.
On March 14, representatives of six ministries will discuss education, health, land management, urban planning and construction, information and justice.
The Ministry continues to hold primary training courses to improve inspections more effectively to prevent, improve and take measures against corruption, abuse of power and inactivity.
Dr. Chap Sotharith, Secretary of State, on behalf of Ms. Men Sam An, Minister, opened the training and had participants from all General Departments, Departments and Ministries for all Ministries.
The second session has 42 participants, which is the same number as the second session, and after the completion of both courses will receive a certificate of training, scheduled for the official ceremony on March 20, 2019. This is according to Dr. Som Boran, Director of the National Inspection Institute.
Dr. Chap Sotharith said that the inspection sector is an important sector because it is one of the keys to more effective state governance, transparency and accountability. This institution exists in almost every country in the world, only with different names depending on the political, social or geographical context.
Dr. Chap Sotharith stated that on this basis, on behalf of the Honorary Doctor, he would like to make the following recommendations:
* First, the National Institute of Inspection must develop and improve the work system and training in consultation with the Undersecretary of State and the Secretary of State in charge, such as having a clear training plan and program, clear management structure and strengthening the quality of administrative work. Efficiency and responsibility.
* Second, the Institute shall prepare a Board of Directors, including the Board of Directors, the Director General and the inspection experts to determine the curriculum and develop the strategic plan of the Institute.
* Third: The National Institute of Inspection must strengthen the study, research and dissemination of work related to the field of inspection in order to expand and strengthen the knowledge of civil servants working in the field of inspection through surveys or consultations on the needs of Training, inspection skills and topics necessary for each stage to be able to meet the real needs of the relevant units.
* Fourth: Units under the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection at all levels, both national and sub-national, must support, cooperate and assign officers to participate in training so that the National Institute of Inspection can continue to perform more. Energetic can solve challenges and be able to provide education services in the field of inspection more effectively.
Fifth, the National Institute of Inspection must strengthen its relations with embassies, national and international organizations and educational institutions to seek cooperation and support, especially for the institute's training program in terms of technical, curriculum design and trainers. Rely entirely on the national budget.
(Kampot): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, stated that the Golden Dragon Exercise between the Cambodian and Chinese Armed Forces in 2019 is not a threat to any country or individual. This exercise will be held every year and on a large scale in order to strengthen the capacity of the Cambodian army.
General Ith Sarath told reporters on March 13, 2019, before the official opening of the 2019 Golden Dragon Exercise between the Cambodian and Chinese armies, that the 2019 Golden Dragon Exercise is to increase the capacity of the Cambodian Army and the exercise. This will greatly benefit the Cambodian army by gaining a lot of experience from the Chinese side in counter-terrorism, disaster relief and more.
"The Golden Dragon exercise is not a threat to any country or individual, while neighboring countries also have a US-Thai exercise," said General Ith Sarath.
The general confirmed that the Golden Dragon exercise will be held every year and on a large scale, the military equipment that is being displayed at the 2019 Golden Dragon exercise field, there are six Chinese helicopters and other weapons to work. Shoot together.
Please be reminded that this Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 lasts for 28 days from February 28 to March 27, 2019. The closing ceremony will be held on March 27, 2019 under the high presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense.
The exercise was attended by 252 people from the Chinese People's Liberation Army and 2542 from the Cambodian side, including: 382 people from the exercise force, 448 people from the exercise force, and 1 force from the opening and closing ceremonies. , 685 people.
In this Golden Dragon exercise, there are training in headquarters and field, focusing on a number of disciplines such as counter-terrorism, hostage rescue, rescue of people from natural disasters, duty under the UN umbrella and engineering. . The main weapons used in this year's Golden Dragon exercise include: armored vehicles, tanks, artillery, mortars, helicopters, air support weapons.
