(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has stated that in 2018, Cambodia produced more than 10 tons of rice, an increase of more than 3 percent, while agricultural exports increased to more than 4 million tons, including more than 620,000 tons of rice. Tons, too.
The Minister's speech was made on the occasion of the opening of the 2018 Conference on Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the direction for 2019 on March 12, 2019.
The Minister said that in 2018, the agricultural sector contributed about 23.5% of GDP and the total value added of the agricultural sector will continue to increase to 21913 billion riels in 2018.
He stated that the main achievements in 2018 are as follows:
Combined crop and industrial production will reach 16.64 million tons in 2018. Total agricultural exports reached 4.23 million tons, of which more than 626 thousand tons were officially exported.
In particular, in the first two months of 2019, unofficial rice exports amounted to more than 909 thousand tons through the main ports in five border provinces, including Takeo, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Kandal and Kampot.
Natural rubber has reached more than 436 thousand hectares, including more than 275 thousand hectares of agro-industrial rubber and 161 thousand hectares of family rubber. 202 thousand hectares of rubber plantations, 220,000 tons of rubber.
Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his gratitude to Mr. Walter Ruck and his colleagues for visiting Cambodia, and in particular for their in-depth discussions and insights into the potential of Cambodia's agricultural sector, progress and opportunities for review. Consider and decide to invest in this field in the future.
On that occasion, the Minister of Agriculture also informed the delegation about the situation and progress in all sectors, especially agriculture, such as rice, corn, mango, cashew, potato and aquaculture, etc.
Mr. Walter Ruck praised the progress of Cambodia and is actively developing according to its right plan and strategy, he hopes that the Royal Government of Cambodia will achieve the vision of 2030.
He also informed the Minister that the visit was aimed at enhancing trade cooperation, focusing on agricultural products, and in particular the preparation of credit support projects for the purchase of agricultural equipment from Austria.
