Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of meeting with more than 10,000 workers in Koh Kong province
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Wednesday, March 13, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with 13,866 workers. From 7 factories in Koh Kong province. The event will be held at Koh Kong Special Economic Zone in Neang Kok Village, Pak Klang Commune, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very happy to meet with workers in Koh Kong province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that factories in Koh Kong province have some factories that produce global products, such as car heads, which do not meet local demand.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister added that the factory in Koh Kong province also has a football factory, which is in demand in the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked what are the reasons for the development of Koh Kong province as now? Samdech Techo stated that Koh Kong is a province with a very sad history, in which even the Minister of National Defense, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, has a history of suffering, a Cambodian dignitary who escaped. Who was killed.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that Samdech took himself to the pond and solved the difficulties of the people of Koh Kong. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the people of Koh Kong are very sad like today.
* Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, said that without peace, no investor would come to invest in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that another important point that led to the development of Koh Kong to the current situation is the successful implementation of two strategies. 1. Transformation of all former battlefields into development and marketing areas; and Transforming Cambodia's border area with neighboring countries into a zone of peace and cooperation.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, stated that Samdech is working hard with Thailand, Vietnam and Laos to build peace along the border. Samdech Techo said that if there is no peace and stability in the border area, there will be no investment in the border area.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in recent years, Samdech has worked hard with the Thai Prime Minister to establish more special economic zones, such as the Orneang Special Economic Zone in Banteay Meanchey province.
* The Prime Minister stated that the trade volume between Cambodia and Thailand has increased to about 7 billion US dollars per year, which is a large trade volume.
* Samdech Techo also stated that currently the border area between Cambodia and Vietnam, which used to be a place for shooting, is also being developed by creating a special economic zone.
* Samdech Techo stated that the trade volume between Cambodia and Laos has also been gradually strengthened and expanded.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the connectivity policy is also a success for the development in Koh Kong province. In that, Samdech asked the Thai side directly to help build National Road No. 48.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in the past, neighboring countries shut down the Cambodian economy as one thing, and also want to shut down their own economy without doing business with Thailand. Samdech Techo confirmed that Samdech does not support the prevention of doing business with Thailand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that National Road No. 48 will become a highway in the future under the financing of South Korea.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his ambition was not only to connect Koh Kong to Sihanoukville and to Phnom Penh, but also to build a road connecting Koh Kong to the Thmor Da area in Pursat and to Battambang and Pailin.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the success of another connection of the Royal Government in addition to the road connection, that is, the connection of the electricity grid, which previously the electricity in Koh Kong province bought from Thailand. But now Koh Kong has become a battery to supply electricity to Phnom Penh and other provinces.
* Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia and Thailand have agreed that in order to reduce illegal migration to work in Thailand, factories must be set up along the Cambodian border without allowing Cambodians to work in Thailand. That no.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has decided to have Tycoon Ly Yong Phat build a long-term water supply facility in Koh Kong province. Samdech Techo also said that in order to solve the current water shortage, Cambodia has contacted Trat province of Thailand to help supply water in Koh Kong province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that tomorrow, South Korean President Moon Jae-in and his wife will pay a visit to Cambodia, and Samdech has a lot of work to do during this visit.
* The Prime Minister also thanked the Thai side for providing water to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen told the workers that as long as they have a job and get paid, do not worry about inspiring words. Samdech Techo's statement was in response to former members and leaders of the former opposition party who tried to inspire the EBA to make workers out of work.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister also did not forget to thank the workers and their families who went to the polls and voted for the Cambodian People's Party in 2018. Samdech Techo said that going to the polls was a blow to the pride of the homeless group and a decision to support peace in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that without peace, there would be no investment and no jobs. In this regard, Samdech Techo called on workers and other political parties to work together to maintain this peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on all factories to pay attention to maintaining the well-being of workers. Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call for no younger brothers and older brothers in factories and no more drug trafficking and use in factories.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in a meeting with a delegation of Japanese investors yesterday, Samdech requested Japan to expand its factory branch to Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is working to make workers receive higher wages and lower their expenses, including accommodation, electricity, food and other expenses, to improve their livelihoods. Of workers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodian Constitution stipulates that without the Prime Minister, the Council of State must be dissolved, that is, not even the Acting Prime Minister, because no one can appoint an Acting Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Minister did not wish for Samdech to die in order to get Samdech's position, but to wish for Samdech to die is to dissolve himself, because the entire Council of Ministers must be dissolved.
