The following is the full text of the announcement of the Ministry of Water Resources: This morning, the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 between Cambodia and China officially started.
(Phnom Penh): The Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 between the Cambodian Army and the Chinese People's Liberation Army has officially started this morning, March 13, 2019, at the actual shooting range of Techo Sen Chum Kiri Training School of the 70th Brigade. Located in Trapeang Veng Village, Trapeang Reang Commune, Chum Kiri District, Kampot Province.
The opening ceremony of the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 was presided over by General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and Major General Feng Xiang, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Chinese People's Liberation Army's Southern Military Region. There were national and international guests, military attachés, local authorities and all kinds of armed forces.
According to the report, the exercise was attended by 252 Chinese People's Liberation Army and 2,542 Cambodian troops, including: 382 exercises, 448 servicemen, Opening-closing ceremony for 1,685 people. This exercise lasts for almost a month and will end on March 27, 2019.
General Chhum Socheat, Spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia, said that the Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 was conducted to strengthen good cooperation between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army to exchange experiences on humanitarian work, disaster relief. Counter-terrorism, peacekeeping as well.
Please note that Cambodia and China have already conducted the Golden Dragon Exercise twice in Kampot province, the first time in 2016 and the second time in 2018. The Golden Dragon Exercise 2019 is seen as large-scale, with more troops and weapons involved.
