(Kampot): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Chairman of the National Commission for Project Management and Chairman of the National Commission for Tourism Development, said that Kampot International Tourism Port will be an important international gateway for seaborne insurance and facilitation. National Transport.
The Minister said this on the occasion of leading the working group and civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism to inspect the construction activities of "Kampot International Tourism Port" located in Teuk Chhou District, Kampot Province on March 12, 2019.
The construction of this international tourist port started on August 8, 2018 and has now reached more than 25%, and is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2019, while Kampot province will host the Sea Festival. Second.
The Minister also instructed the construction contractors and consultants to work hard to speed up the construction process by implementing the action plan and with high quality.
The port is an international tourist port that is planned to handle about 1 million tourists and passengers a year. This port has an international standard structure and is a passenger port (not a cargo port).
The port will be an important international gateway by sea, connecting tourists to the southern islands and connecting Kampot province of Cambodia to the world. Through this port, it will further promote the development of tourism and related sectors in Kampot province, Bokor mountain resort and Cambodia's coastal tourist destinations.
