(Phnom Penh): In 2018, an additional 538 people were infected with HIV. This was confirmed by Prof. Mam Bun Heng, Minister of Health in the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work in 2018 and raise the direction for 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the afternoon of March 12, 2019.
"Infectious disease control programs are continuing on the path to progress," the health minister said. "There are 538 new HIV infections, or 0.03 out of 1,000 non-HIV populations."
At the same time, Minister Mam Bunheng added that antiretroviral therapy covers 87.22% of the number of people living with HIV. The successful cure rate of TB has maintained above 93% for several consecutive years. Malaria cases increased in 2018, but no deaths.
He said that this progress will reach the goal of the Royal Government to eradicate malaria by 2025. Expansion of non-communicable disease screening and treatment services has achieved remarkable results. Thirty percent of the population aged 25-64 with high blood pressure received treatment and 32% of the population aged 25-64 with diabetes received treatment.
The Minister of Health also said that the number of drug users receiving medical services increased from 3,101 in 2017 to 8,096 in 2018. Oral health services to prevent blindness, injuries from traffic accidents, food safety, environmental health are in progress.
Ministry of Health spends more than $ 21 million to provide health services to workers in occupational accidents and health care (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, said that the Ministry has spent more than $ 21 million to Use the health services of workers in the occupational accident and health care system in 2018.
The Minister's confirmation was made on the occasion of his participation in the closing ceremony of the meeting to review the work of 2018 and raise the direction for 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the afternoon of March 12, 2019.
There were 43,932 cases of informal use of medical services by workers / employees of commune / sangkat councils, village officials, athletes, tricycle workers and deminers, at a cost of approximately $ 284,474.
In addition, the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) has signed agreements on the use and provision of services with public and private health facilities for 156 occupational risks and 1,349 for health care.
According to the Minister of Health, he has actively participated in the implementation of this reform program by launching a budget unit and operating budget with accountability, transparency and efficiency, and using the banking system to pay salaries, missions, hourly hours, maternity leave. And some other benefits of health workers. Improved national budget spending and financial management at both central and capital-provincial levels.
