Germany appreciates and congratulates progress in all areas of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Phnom Penh): HE Dr. Ingo Karasten, German Ambassador to Cambodia, on March 12, 2019, informed Senior Minister Ly Thuch that both the Royal Government and the German Parliament commended and congratulated the country on its rapid progress. Cambodia under the talented leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen ended the civil war, unified the nation, brought peace to the motherland peacefully and without the use of weapons and bloodshed between Khmer and Khmer.
At the same time, Germany will enhance good cooperation with Cambodia for the benefit of both countries and peoples, with a focus on promoting economic growth, agriculture, trade and mine action.
In particular, the Ambassador will ask the German Government to encourage the German private sector to assist in the demining sector in rural communities in Cambodia in order to alleviate the burden of the Royal Government of Cambodia in demining and reducing mine casualties.
So far, Germany has helped clear landmines in Cambodia through HALOTRUST, clearing more than 10 square kilometers of land with 2,991 anti-personnel mines and benefiting about 100,000 people.
