Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Instructs Ministries, Institutions and Provincial Governors to Disseminate Traffic Law Once a Month to Reduce Traffic Accidents
According to the letter, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that road traffic accidents are still a challenge and a long-term problem, causing deaths, injuries, disabilities, property damage every day, worrying.
In order to prevent and prevent road traffic accidents, Samdech would like to request all ministries, institutions and provincial capitals to instruct all units under their supervision to actively participate in education, dissemination and respect for the following road traffic laws:
1: Establish a separate program to educate and disseminate the law on road traffic and traffic safety standards on a monthly basis (at least once a month) to improve traffic safety awareness and report on this activity as follows: The sample is attached to the CCHR (General Secretariat) located at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
2. Develop internal regulations to promote the consistent implementation of important safety issues in the law on road traffic, such as wearing seat belts when traveling in cars, wearing helmets when traveling in motorcycles, technical inspections of vehicles. Driving is not under the influence of alcohol, etc.
3. Supervise and take strict measures to promote respect for internal regulations at the entrances and exits of ministries and institutions, as well as establish competitive examination programs for individuals who have knowledge of the law on road traffic and good implementation of internal regulations.
The following is the full text of the announcement of the Ministry of Water Resources: Senior officials of the Ministry of Land Management: Commune / Sangkat councils have the duty to cooperate with institutions and units in charge of resolving land disputes for their local people.
(Kratie): Mr. Tep Thorn, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Secretary General of the National Authority for Land Dispute Resolution, stated that Commune / Sangkat Councils have the duty to cooperate with the competent institutions and units in resolving land disputes for the people in In its base.
The senior official said this at the workshop on the Land Dispute Resolution Procedure of the Commune / Sangkat Council, which will last for 3 days from March 12-14, 2019, with the participation of more than 80 people from communes in Kratie province.
