He added that the Royal Government has made efforts to focus on land disputes and has expanded the procedures for sub-national officials to mediate and resolve land disputes of the people in a transparent and effective manner in accordance with the procedures. What must be done to resolve land disputes for the people in any case or use any force and resources.
Mr. Sreng Sopheap, Deputy Governor, said that 38 cases of land disputes have been resolved, 5 cases have been resolved and the remaining 33 are still being resolved. There were 91 cases outside the Cadastral Commission mechanism (41 cases were sent from the national level and 50 cases from the provincial level).
He said that the Land Dispute Resolution Team of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has resolved 20 cases 100% and is continuing 13 cases, the remaining 08 cases. And the Provincial Land Dispute Resolution Working Group has mediated to resolve 26 cases 100%, 15 ongoing cases and 9 remaining cases. Cuba: We do not have "25,000 troops" stationed in Venezuela as the United States claims!
Cuba: The Cuban government has denied allegations by senior US officials that Cuba has been supporting Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro, who now has 25,000 troops in the country. In Venezuela. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday afternoon, March 12, 2019.
A statement from the Cuban government said: "Cuba does not condone such blatant lies and dismisses allegations that Cuba is assisting in supporting Venezuela. "Our relationship is based on mutual respect and solidarity." According to Cuba itself, there are currently more than 20,000 Cuban doctors and advisers in Venezuela.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, has set out six main work directions to be implemented in 2019 and beyond.
Mr. Mam Bunheng emphasized that in order to continue to improve the implementation of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 and the Health Strategic Plan 2016-2020, the work direction for 2019 and the next year in the health sector will focus on:
1: Increase the access to people and the use of education, health promotion, prevention, treatment, care, rehabilitation, medical quality and safety at an affordable price.
2. Effectively implement the Royal Government's social health protection policy.
3. Provide adequate basic and continuing training, focusing on competencies, skills and equitable distribution of staff, as well as providing appropriate incentives.
4. Provide adequate medicine, equipment and infrastructure resources, including buildings, medical equipment and medical technology and information technology network to public health facilities.
5. Strengthen the management of health information technology and the use of information to strengthen the management of services and systems for disease monitoring and response, monitoring and evaluation of progress and improving health research.
6. Strengthen institutional capacity, especially regulatory capacity, to strengthen the implementation of health laws and regulations, enhance public-private partnerships, and increase local health accountability.
