Speaking in an interview with Fresh News TV's "Weekly Special Guest", Mr. Sim Sitha said that the problem that caused the water in Phnom Penh to be weak and diligent was due to the following reasons: Water must be distributed from the center of Phnom Penh to the suburbs, which are facing a shortage of clean water.
Mr. Sim Sitha said that the implementation of clean water from the new residents of the suburbs, which they currently do not have access to clean water. Therefore, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority must expand the pipeline to the suburbs, which weakens the water pressure in the city.
He added that the above reasons make Phnom Penh water shortage due to increasing population, increasing number of counters, while the amount of water to be supplied remains the same. In fact, the PPWSA produces only 560,000 cubic meters per day, but the demand for clean water is much higher.
He added that these problems also make the Water Supply Authority worried about the damage to equipment because the factory produces water 24 hours a day without time off.
He added that to solve this problem, the Water Supply Authority has been expanding the plant in other locations by receiving loans from the Ministry of Economy and Finance and AFD to build the Chamkar Mon factory, which is currently under construction and It cost more than 30 million euros and took more than two years to build.
He added that the Water Supply Authority currently has four water plants, one of which is under construction. These four factories have a capacity of only 560,000 cubic meters per day and now supply from three factories: Prek Village, Chroy Changva and Niroth.
