(Preah Sihanouk): The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Mr. Yon Min, on the evening of March 11, 2019, held an emergency meeting to take action against a group of people who seized illegal land in Preah Sihanouk Province.
The meeting was attended by the governors of the four districts, the Provincial Gendarmerie and the Sihanoukville Provincial Police Commissioner.
The main purpose of this emergency meeting is to focus on educating, disseminating and cracking down on the anarchic activities of some groups of citizens who have gathered to encroach on the vacant lands of others and public lands of the state.
Please be informed that for more than a week now, groups of people from various provinces have been gathering people to invade and occupy land in almost all districts and cities according to their respective divisions.
After the local authorities have investigated and found that these people are moving from different areas or provinces by the mastermind behind the scenes to encroach on their land. Others, along with state land, under the pretext of poverty, homelessness.
But in this case, the authorities conclude that it is the strategy of the anarchic people under the trick of winning land and losing money.
As a precautionary measure, the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, Yon Min, assigned all Unity Committees to educate and disseminate to the occupied areas so that they can understand and identify them. Clearly encourage them to understand the law and leave the encroachment site to avoid problems when the authorities take legal action.
The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province has also ordered the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner, together with the Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, to search for these brokers in order to take legal action without exception.
He added that the country has laws, so we must abide by the law and not allow anarchists to make storms and cause problems.
