Samdech Techo Hun Sen Instructs the Roles, Duties and Procedures for the National Working Group on Capital-Province (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, issues instructions on the Roles, Duties and Procedures For the National Working Group to visit the capital-province to fulfill the mission to monitor and support the political program and strategy of the fourth phase of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
* First, the chairperson of the national working group visited the capital and provinces to lead and be responsible for managing the working group in monitoring and supporting the implementation of various political programs and the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy at the local capital-province level. Take charge.
* Second, to link the Royal Government with the people through the widespread dissemination of the Rectangular Strategic Political Program, Phase 4, National Strategic Development Plan, Safe Village and Commune Policy, Sector Reform Program, as well as the national situation and Recent developments at the grassroots level.
* Third, enhance the responsibilities of ministries, institutions as well as sub-national administrations in carrying out their work by monitoring and supporting the implementation of programs, projects and action plans at the local level.
* Fourth, to cooperate in promoting and enhancing the accountability of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrative authorities in providing effective public services and local development.
* Sixth: Cooperate to solve challenges and difficulties of local people.
* 7th: Gather resources from various sources to participate in solving people's livelihood as well as local development.
