US Secretary of State: All US embassy staff in Venezuela will be laid off this week
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo said Monday that a number of other diplomats in Venezuela will be removed in the face of the country's dire development situation. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Tuesday, March 12, 2019.
"The United States will withdraw all remaining diplomatic staff from Venezuela this week," he said via Twitter. "This decision is in response to the situation in Venezuela, as the presence of US diplomats in this Latin American country has become an obstacle to US policy."
Currently, the United States continues to try to bring aid to Colombia to prepare for entry into Venezuela, despite obstruction by the Maduro government, which considers the US move to be intentional aggression. Opposition leader Jang Geun-hye has entered Venezuela without being arrested, as the Latin American country is still plagued by unresolved power outages.
Japan sees Cambodia as a potential place for investment and asks Samdech Techo to continue to support its investment
(Phnom Penh): A delegation of Japanese investors saw that Cambodia is still a potential country for investment and requested the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen to continue to support and support Japanese investors who are looking for investment opportunities in Cambodia.
The presentation of the potential for investment as well as the request for support and support was made by Mr. Norio Yamaguchi, Vice Chairman of the Japan International Friendship Exchange Council, while leading a delegation of Japanese investors to pay a courtesy call and discuss some work. With Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Peace Palace this morning, March 12, 2019.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during the meeting, Mr. Norio expressed his vision that over the past three years he has clearly seen positive changes and developments. And soon of Cambodia.
Norio informed Samdech Techo that at present, Japan, especially small and medium-sized Japanese investors, are looking for opportunities to invest abroad due to the Japanese economic problems. Mr. Norio requested Samdech Techo to continue to support and welcome Japanese investors who come to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen extended a warm welcome to Japanese investors who want to invest in Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the many reforms of the Royal Government to ensure the health and vitality of Cambodia's commercial economy.
Samdech Techo also stated that what Cambodia is doing now is to make the economy more competitive. The prince also told the delegation what the government had done in the past. In particular, the reduction of electricity prices, the removal of Camcontrol from the border and the dissolution of the Naval Agency (Kamsap), all of which are reforms to facilitate investment more effectively.
It should be noted that as of 2017, Cambodia has welcomed and registered Japanese investment projects with a total investment of approximately 1.6 billion US dollars through the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
In 2017, there are 9 Japanese investment projects with a total investment of about 63 million US dollars. Among them, eight investment projects are located in special economic zones with an investment capital of about 59 million US dollars.
(Phnom Penh): In an interview with Fresh News on March 11, 2019, Mr. Long Dimanche, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Cambodia to South Korea, stated that Cambodian workers working in the Republic of Korea About 50,000 gems send $ 600 million to their homeland each year, as part of their contribution to Cambodia's economic development.
The Cambodian Ambassador to the Republic of Korea said: "We have tried to negotiate with friendly countries, especially with the Republic of Korea to open the labor market for Cambodians to get professional skills and jobs. And have a high salary to send to families, and Cambodians who go to work in Korea just send money to Cambodia no less than 600 million dollars, so a large amount of money.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has strived to establish a long-term political line and vision for employment in Cambodia and to work with friendly countries to facilitate and increase interest in investment. Foreigners in Cambodia will send unskilled workers to work abroad to bring skills to the country, as well as a lot of money back to Cambodia. This is a further confirmation from Mr. Dimanche.
He added that the Cambodian community in Korea has more than 60,000 members, including more than 500,000 workers, more than 7,000 Cambodian women married to Koreans and more than 400 Cambodian students. Studying in Korea.
Mr. Long Dimanche stated that out of the 16 nationalities working in South Korea, our Cambodian workers have a better reputation than other nationalities: Korean employers always admire Mouth that they are patient with work, honest, respectful, love co-workers and cooperate well together for team work.
