(Rattanakiri): On March 11, 2019, the Climate Change Department of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development organized a training workshop on climate change for youth in Rattanakiri Province.
The ceremony was held at the Rattanak City Hotel in Banlung, and was presided over by Dr. Chuob Paris, Deputy Secretary General of the National Council for Sustainable Development, and Mr. Muong Pang, Deputy Governor, on behalf of the Governor. With the participation of participants from the youth of the province, the youth of the Red Cross, the youth of Scouts and about 200 students.
The two-day workshop aims to raise awareness of climate change, including causes, effects, and national and international responses to climate change.
In this workshop, Mr. Muong Pang, Deputy Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, said that climate change is a serious threat now and in the future to humankind around the world.
The Deputy Governor said that today's training workshop will provide basic knowledge to the workshop on the causes, effects and solutions of climate change and strategies and action plans to respond to climate change so that all participants understand better, as well as Incorporating climate change into their own daily plans and organizational action plans.
