Fire destroys a house and a factory overnight in Sangkat Svay Pak, Khan Russey Keo, destroying equipment worth nearly 40,000 dollars
(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out at the intersection of Concrete Road, Group 7, Lou Village, Svay Pak Sangkat, Russey Keo District, which destroyed a house and a workers' dormitory, costing nearly 40,000 USD. . The incident happened at 2:30 AM on March 11, 2019 and was completely extinguished at 3:20 AM after the intervention of the authorities.
According to the report of Lieutenant Colonel Koul Yi, Police Inspector of Russey Keo District, sent to Mr. Chea Pisey, District Governor, the cause of the fire is still unknown and is being investigated according to the procedures.
According to the inspector, the fire destroyed a house made of galvanized iron, measuring 14 meters by 8 meters, and a workers' shelter measuring 2 meters by 8 meters, made of galvanized iron, owned by 69-year-old San Sokchea. Leased the house to 55-year-old Le Young Tong, causing damage to an old Korean motorcycle and some household items.
The fire did not spread on a large scale, with the timely intervention of two vehicles of the Phnom Penh Fire Prevention Office to put out a series of 6 vehicles, including 1 vehicle of Russey Keo district and completely extinguished. In the next half hour, which did not cause any casualties.
