The NEC has issued an official statement stating that as of the fourth day of registration for the council election, there are seven parties participating.
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) issued an official statement on March 11, 2019, stating that the period of 4 days is the 4th day of the registration of political parties. There are seven political parties registered to run in the by-elections.
The seven parties registered to run for the Capital-Provincial Council are the Cambodian People's Party, FUNCINPEC, the Cambodian Youth Party, the Khmer Republican Party, the Khmer Will Party, the National Unity Party and the Cambodian Nationality Party.
Please be informed that the NEC started the voter registration process for the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council, 3rd mandate on March 4, 2019.
The voter registration period is 13 days, starting from March 4 to 15, 2019 (13 days excluding Sundays and official holidays). Voters for the council election are commune councilors in positions with a total of 11,572 members nationwide.
The following is the statement of the NEC: The Minister of Tourism urges the people to work hard to protect natural resources to serve the tourism sector, which earns more revenue than destruction.
(Kampong Chhnang): The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, urged the people to stop deforestation, hunting and turn to work together to protect those natural resources for the benefit of tourism. More than deforestation.
The appeal was made during a meeting with residents of Anlong Svay Waterfall Tourism Community, located in Kbal Teuk Village, Kbal Teuk Commune, Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province on March 10, 2019.
On that occasion, the Minister said that the Royal Government has taken care to establish and organize ecotourism sites, eco-tourism areas, especially community tourism, because this community tourism is very important to help protect. Natural resources include forests, wildlife, and so on.
He said that both the World Tourism Organization and ASEAN and the Royal Government of Cambodia have made great efforts to promote community-based tourism by mobilizing people into community-based tourism to divert deforestation and hunting to resource protection. Those natures.
Mr. Thong Khon assured the people, "If you stop deforestation, stop hunting and turn to animal protection for tourists, take care of the forest for tourists to visit, provide services to tourists, you will get a lot of income. "It helps to promote a better life rather than destroying those natural resources."
The Minister added that the development of the tourism community also requires the participation of four stakeholders, including:
* P1 = Public: The national and sub-national governments must pay attention to the development of infrastructure (access roads), the need for electricity, the provision of internet, telephone services, the establishment of schools for the people, the training of skills or Knowledge to the people, policy making, legal standards and laws to support and protect the community, etc.
The resumption of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal was made this morning, March 11, 2019, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the graduation ceremony for students of the Royal University of Law and Economics (RULES). 3,000 successful graduates held at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, said: "I, Your Majesty, on behalf of the Royal Government, call on all people who have not yet taken the census to continue their efforts to enter the census. "These days, to continue the census, those who have not yet entered the census must cooperate and the time is near."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the census is necessary so that we have enough data to set out a vision for the future as well as facilitate the development of our country. Therefore, all Cambodians who have not yet conducted the census should make an effort to qualify our census officials to enter their homes to conduct census statistics in accordance with the census procedures.
Please be informed that Cambodia has already conducted four censuses in 1921, 1962, 1998 and 2008. But the 1921 census by the French protectorate was not a real census, as the main purpose was to find out the number of people between the ages of 20 and 60 to collect taxes.
