US government may close again as Tram prepares to cut $ 8.6 billion from Defense and Homeland Security funds to build border wall
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Donald Trump's White House on Monday will request a $ 8.6 billion package to build a border wall with Mexico, as promised. Many say that the closure of the government can happen again. This is according to Reuters quoted by Sputnik on Monday afternoon, March 11, 2019.
According to Reuters, based on a 2017 US Boundary Commission request, the White House on Monday will ask the US Congress to withdraw $ 3.6 billion from the Pentagon's military budget and another $ 5 billion from the Pentagon. A budget for the US Department of Homeland Security will be used to build a 722-mile border, or more than 1,161 kilometers, with Mexico.
Monday's White House proposal also includes funding for hiring an additional 2,800 law enforcement officers and a 100-person immigration judging panel. The US Congress must make a final decision on the fiscal year 2020 by October 1, otherwise the closure of the US government could happen again.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on the authorities to pay attention to solving the problem of water shortage in the dry season this year (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on March 11, 2019 This continues to call on local authorities, the Ministry of Water Resources and the Department of Water Resources to continue to pay attention to solving the problem of water shortage in the dry season this year.
The renewed call of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the occasion of the handing over of diplomas to more than 3,000 students of the Royal University of Law and Economics (RULES) who successfully graduated on the morning of the 11th. This March 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Now, the challenge that I issued in the past still faces the problem of lack of water, which asks people to grow dry rice, but some people diligently use the water. The rest of the dry farming continues after the harvest, and he does it again, making the water reserved for this use lack.
Samdech Techo added, "Currently, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology is intervening to irrigate some of the threatened dry rice fields, asking the local authorities, the Ministry of Water Resources and the Department of Water Resources to continue their efforts to solve this problem. "The biggest concern is the water supply of our people."
At the same time, the Prime Minister of Cambodia said that in 2016, the Royal Government delivered water to the people, but then the problem is that our wells are dry, there is no well because there is no well. .. Because I used to dig 8 meters to breathe the water that came out, but the water fell to 10 meters to the bottom, making the well dry.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further stated that this year, everywhere, the authorities should pay attention to digging wells rather than transporting water from a distance, even if it is a little deep, but the use of digging wells is a good way. This year there is water, next year there is still water, there are still wells to use, so we have to continue digging wells where there is a lack of water.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also continued to call on the people in places where there is not much water, not always a waterfall, to end the rice cultivation and not to increase the rice season. That rain has not yet arrived.
In the dry season of 2019, Cambodia will experience severe drought, especially during April and May, the temperature will rise to 40 to 42 degrees due to the indirect effects of El Nino (El Nino). The Royal Government has called on the authorities and the people to take measures to conserve water for use.
