(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has reiterated that Cambodia does not need to amend its constitution to pave the way for the death penalty, as Cambodia now has a law that provides for life imprisonment for criminals. That is enough.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on Monday, March 11, 2019, on the occasion of handing over diplomas to students of the Royal University of Law and Economics. (RULES) More than 3,000 people have successfully graduated.
During the ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also supported the statements made by lawyers Sok Sam Oeun, Ou Virak and Sok Touch, who did not support the death penalty. Samdech Techo announced that now Cambodia does not need to amend the Constitution to have the death penalty law.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that this method of education, monks must also contribute to promote virtues for our society. This is the key point, the punishment is the next thing, but prevention is necessary to prevent it from happening, as doctors say, "prevention is better than cure."
"Education in our society must be strengthened to avoid committing unpredictable sins in our society, not just against our own relatives, but against women," he said. "Secondly, law enforcement must be very strict for the perpetrators. If this happens, the death penalty is enough for such a crime."
It should be noted that during the meeting with teachers and girls victims at the Vocational Training and Rehabilitation Center for Young Women, Acezip Tum Dy on March 10, 2019, because he was angry with the person who raped the girl too much, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said It is said that Samdech wants the death penalty for people who have a kind of animal to commit physical abuse of children, but must be done by referendum across the country.
